Battambang Provincial Governor Conducts a Meeting to Solve the Impact of the Construction Site of an Overweight Vehicle Weighing Station in Thmor Koul District
(Battambang): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, on May 2, 2022, chaired a meeting to discuss the impact of the construction of another overweight vehicle weighing station on National Road No. 5, located at Tros village, Otaki commune, Thmor Koul district.
The meeting was also attended by the Technical Advisor of the Project, the Deputy Director of the Second Impact Management Department of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Director of the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, the Governor of Thmor Koul District and other stakeholders.
After the discussion, Mr. Sok Lou said that because the old location has a lot of impact, especially affect some people, so to avoid the maximum impact and to reduce the national budget, he agreed to find New location to build overweight vehicle weighing station to easily deal with the impact without complications and without affecting the people, speeding up the settlement and speeding up the construction.
He instructed the technical team to study the location and construction of the entrance and make a request to the relevant ministries to approve the relocation.
