(Svay Rieng-Prey Veng): Mr. Var Kimhong, Senior Minister in charge of Border Affairs, yesterday continued to lead the working group to inspect the border, construction of border posts and the construction of the Cambodia-Vietnam border ring road in Svay Rieng and Prey Veng provinces. .
The inspection was accompanied by Dr. Koy Pisey, Deputy Director of the Permanent Secretariat of the National Authority for Border Affairs and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, General Kwan Seam, Commander of the Engineering Command, and Mr. Men Vibol, Governor. Svay Rieng Province (during the visit to Svay Rieng Province) and Deputy Governor of Prey Veng Province (during the visit to Prey Veng Province).
Dr. Koy Pisey told Fresh News that the inspection of the border, the construction of the border post and the construction of the Cambodia-Vietnam border ring road in Svay Rieng and Prey Veng provinces on April 30. 2022, that is, after completing the same mission in Mondulkiri, Kratie and Tbong Khmum provinces on April 28-29, 2022.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Var Kimhong stated that the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has set out a policy to build Cambodia's border with neighboring countries as a border of peace, friendship, cooperation and sustainable development. The implementation of national defense principles belongs to all people.
The senior minister said that the construction of border posts and the construction of the border ring road is also a contribution to social work, the opening of border gates, the expansion of agro-industry, tourism, increase potential products, multi-sectoral, promote economic growth. People's livelihoods contribute to building and strengthening national defense based on the people as a solid foundation, not dry and witness to sustainable living.
Dr. Koy Pisey also added that the achievements of the border posts and the border ring road clearly demonstrate the long-term efforts to maintain peace and stability for the people of the two countries to live in harmony with each other. And trust each other in the border areas, especially to protect the sovereignty and territorial integrity for the sake of future generations.
