Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation and Legal Contribution Continues Cooperation in Civil Law Training and Dissemination
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation and Legal Contribution continued its training and dissemination of law in the civil sector through the signing of the second Memorandum of Understanding between the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation and Legal Contribution for 12 months. Continuing.
The signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding was held on the afternoon of April 30, 2022 at the meeting hall of the Cambodia-Korea Cooperation Center (CKCC).
This memorandum also has three main objectives, including:
1. Contribute to the dissemination of the Civil Code, the Code of Civil Procedure and the law related to civil affairs more widely, clearly and effectively in the practice of the legal profession in the field of civil affairs.
2. Participate and increase attention in developing the capacity of lawyers and legal assistants in the legal team related to the civil sector, especially the preparation of documents in accordance with the format prescribed by the law, updates on the law and explanations of the law. .
3. Disseminate the law through standardized media and widely disseminated throughout Cambodia.
Lawyer Ly Raththy, President of the Cambodia International Cooperation Lawyers Group, said at the signing ceremony of the second MoU that the Cambodia International Cooperation Lawyers Association is pleased to cooperate with the legal contribution of the legal training and dissemination institution. Has the capacity and potential related to the civil sector and has become a partner in training human resources and disseminating laws related to civil law.
Please be informed that the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation has been building its new office building on an area of 600 square meters and 6 floors in Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, only about 5 minutes from Aeon Mall.
At the same time, Ms. Tep Bophal, Lawyer, Founder of Legal Contribution, also expressed her interest that she was happy to share her legal knowledge related to the civil sector to the lawyers and members of the Cambodian International Cooperation Lawyers Group, in particular. Ms. Lawyer is extremely excited to receive the value and trust in the training of legal contributors from an unprecedented group of lawyers.
Taking this opportunity, Ms. Lawyer appreciated the dedication of Mr. Ly Raththy, the leader of the Bar Association, who took care to develop the capacity of the lawyers and members of the Bar Association.
In the above ceremony, there were also certificates of education to the participants who participated and met all the requirements of the 21 training courses and the presentation of letters of thanks, as well as souvenirs from the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation. Also a legal contribution representative.
Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee Holds Conference to Analyze Economic Situation
BEIJING, April 29 (Xinhua) - The Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee held a conference on April 29 to analyze and analyze the current economic and economic situation and discuss human resource development plans during the implementation of the National Development Plan. 5 years 14 ".
Xi Jinping, secretary-general of the CPC Central Committee, chaired the conference. The conference highlighted that the spread of Kovid 19 and the Ukraine crisis has caused increasing risks and challenges, improving economic employment, ensuring security and improving the living standards of the Chinese people. .
To prevent the spread of infectious diseases, to stabilize the economy and secure development, this is the real need of the CPC Central Committee. The conference said that the preparation of the "Human Resource Development Plan during the implementation of the 14th Five-Year National Development Plan" is an important task under the auspices of the CPC Central Committee.
We should strengthen the comprehensive leadership of the Chinese Communist Party in human resource work, establish and strengthen the strategic position of human resource-led development, as well as train the import and use of human resources in all aspects.
Strong anti-viral solidarity between Cambodia and China shows the model of building a community of general health for humanity
Speaking to Cambodia-China Friendship Radio by telephone on the afternoon of April 29, 2022, HE Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Cambodian Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that Cambodia and China have been cooperating closely. Strong in the field of public health, especially in the context of Kovid 19, the two countries have shown strong solidarity, in which China has helped Cambodia a lot in the fight against Kovid 19.
He stressed that China is the first country to help Cambodia the most on Kovid, including technical assistance, medical equipment, volunteer doctors and vaccines, especially in the field of public health. Another important example is that both the Cambodian and Chinese sides have stood by the spirit of multilateralism in almost all areas, in general and in particular public health.
He added that Cambodia's liberation from mass obligations would help revive the socio-economic situation, and if nothing changed, he could predict that by 2023, Cambodia could return to normal economic growth. It also continues to demand that people must join the Royal Government in implementing the guidelines of the Ministry of Health and relevant authorities.
It should be noted that to celebrate the 50th Anniversary of Artemisinin and the International Cooperation Forum for Building a Community of General Health for Humanity, on April 25, 2022, Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, announced his support for all activities and cooperation. Operations that have been underway to build a community of general health for humanity.
