It should be informed that the gifts received from the above association for a family include: 20 kg of rice, 10 packets of noodles, 2 liters of cooking oil, 2 kg of sugar, 2 cans of milk, 1 kg of salt and 1 fruit. Kg. Deputy Chief of the Supreme Court Presides Over a Workshop on "Legal Effectiveness, Legal and Judicial Reform in Cambodia" at Indravitcha University (UI)
(Phnom Penh): Indravitcha University (UI), Phnom Penh, on Saturday afternoon, April 30, 2022, organized a seminar and opening ceremony on "Legal Effectiveness, Legal Reform and Justice System in Cambodia" for PhD students. Sixth, the first session of Indravitcha University (UI).
The workshop was chaired by Prof. Dr. Chiv Keng, Vice President of the Supreme Court and attended by Dr. Sum Chhum Long, President of the Council of Doctors of Science of Indravitcha University (UI), Dr. Chan Rainsy, Dr. Chhoeun Savorn, as well as More than 50 doctoral students were present.
On that occasion, the Deputy President of the Supreme Court stated that the Royal Academy of Judicial Professions is producing judges, prosecutors, clerks, bailiffs and notaries with high standards, while the Bar Training Center is also producing remarkably capable lawyers. . He added that the two institutions are continuing to find ways to produce judges, court officials, lawyers to meet the current needs of society.
According to Prof. Dr. Chiv Keng, the Code of Ethics for Judges and Prosecutors came into force on February 5, 2007. He added that the Disciplinary Council of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy has been strengthened and is actively working to discipline judges and prosecutors who have committed misconduct.
According to the decision dated April 25, 2022, it is also decided that "2022 is the year to strengthen the work discipline and ethics of officials in the judiciary." At the same time, the decision also stated that "the Ministry of Justice and the Supreme Council of the Magistracy must take strict and unanimous action to implement disciplinary measures against court officials who do not comply with the law."
Please note that the above workshop was held at the first floor of the Indra Vichea University (UI) building, located in Sangkat Toek Laak 3, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
