Labor Minister Plans to Continue Strengthening Labor Dispute Resolution Mechanism to Achieve Higher Recovery Rate
(Phnom Penh): In line with the spirit of the 136th Anniversary of International Labor Day, May 1, 2022, under the theme "Peace, Health and Occupational Security", Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, submitted a plan to further strengthen the labor dispute resolution mechanism. To get a higher recovery rate.
On the morning of April 30, 2022, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training organized this celebration with the participation of representatives of the International Labor Organization (ILO), employers' associations, union representatives and representatives of relevant ministries and institutions.
The Minister also informed the relevant partners, employers' associations, trade unions that in order to continue the spirit of International Labor Day May 1, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has already set out the work direction as set out in the work direction for 2022, which the conference Summarize the work of the Ministry, including:
1: Continue to strive to effectively implement the 10 recommendations of the Prime Minister.
2: Continue to strive to improve working conditions, strengthen the implementation of labor laws, continue to strengthen labor inspection mechanisms more effectively and transparently.
3. Strengthen the harmony of industrial relations, raise awareness of the rights, duties and responsibilities of workers and employers.
5: Promote the implementation of inspection mechanisms and modernize labor inspections through the information technology system and continue to strengthen inter-ministerial and institutional inspections by inspecting labor and risk levels of basic enterprises once a year to ensure the culture. Compliance ensures efficiency, quality and transparency in the provision of services by placing all the services of the Ministry in the information technology nursery.
6: Continue to strengthen labor dispute resolution mechanisms to achieve a higher rate of settlement in order to meet the needs of the parties to the dispute and launch a pilot process for resolving individual disputes by the Arbitration Council, as well as strengthen the implementation of professional freedom of association. According to the letter of national legal norms in force and international labor conventions that Cambodia has ratified.
7: Continue to transform an enterprise into a safe community of workers with full capacity, good working conditions, productivity, work attitude, social responsibility and harmonization of professional relations by the Ministry will provide certificates to factories and enterprises Adequate assets according to the criteria.
