(Phnom Penh): The National Committee for Clean City Evaluation on April 29, 2022 held a consultation meeting on the draft standard "Model Tourism Village" chaired by Mr. Chea Bora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Clean City Evaluation. With the participation of representatives of the Capital, Provinces, Department of Tourism, Capital and Provinces and leaders of various relevant ministries and institutions.
The purpose of this consultation meeting is to provide additional input into the draft "Model Tourism Village" standard, which aims to make this document more accurate and consistent with the realities of villages across Cambodia. .
Tourist villages are established based on the characteristics of each village, in connection with the culture-nature, environment, social heritage, archeology and traditional practices of each village.
The drafting of the "Model Tourism Village" standard is based on two initiatives: the first is the World Tourism Organization (UNWTO) and the second is in line with the National Tourism Policy for the development of agro-tourism in rural areas. Participate in improving the lives of local people, which is a strategic goal in the Royal Government's "Road Map" on the plan to restore and promote tourism in Cambodia during and after the Kovit-19 crisis.
1. Tourism product development refers to the promotion of domestic and international tourism markets, both in and after the Kovit-19 crisis.
2: Starting from the development of tourism villages, we can attract both domestic and international tourists to visit and enjoy the countryside, which can create more jobs and income for local people, which is a factor in reducing poverty. In rural areas, in line with the national tourism development policy.
3. The result of the development of "tourist village" is that people can contribute to the preservation of culture and nature.
4: Due to jobs and income from the agro-tourism sector, we can also succeed in efforts to protect the environment and biodiversity.
The results of this international competition enable us to promote Cambodian tourism by introducing culture, nature and traditions to the world. In addition, we can develop the local economy in villages across the country and will also promote on-site exports from Cambodian farmers directly, in line with the high recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. In the 6th Sea Festival in Kep province.
