Malaysia eases travel congestion to boost tourism
(Son Chey - Malaysia): From May 1, 2022, passengers who have been vaccinated against all 19 cases of Kovid, the Malaysian government does not require the Kovid 19 test before and after the trip, including children with Ages 12 and older and patients who had had Kovid 19 from 6 to 60 days.
Kovid 19 health insurance package for foreigners is also not required to be purchased in advance.
Passengers returning to Malaysia who have not been vaccinated in all doses are required to undergo RT-PCR testing two days prior to departure and professional RTK-Ag testing 24 hours prior to departure. Arrive in Malaysia and be required to perform a five-day permit (except for a 17-year-old passenger).
However, those who test positive for Kovid 19 may be allowed to leave the test site before the due date if the RTK-Ag test on day 4 is negative.
