(Phnom Penh): The National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDC) on the afternoon of April 29, 2022, signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) with PPE INIT in Cambodia to continue implementing the "1294" early warning system. Flood resistance and disaster response in Cambodia, valid for 3 consecutive years.
The MoU signing ceremony was presided over by Dr. Hang Samoeun, Advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on behalf of General Kun Kim, Senior Minister, First Deputy Chairman of the NEC. And Mr. Lukas Laube, Country Director of People Inc. in Cambodia, as well as the Deputy Secretary General, the NEC Advisors and some officials of People Inc.
The purpose of this Memorandum of Understanding is to strengthen the relationship and closer cooperation between the NCDD and PIPE INIT in Cambodia in order to continue to implement the "1294" early warning system, flood resistance and Emergency response to disasters in Cambodia. This Memorandum of Understanding will be valid for 3 consecutive years from the date of signing.
On behalf of Senior Minister Kun Kim, Dr. Hang Samoeun praised and appreciated PipalInnit in Cambodia for its close cooperation with the NCDD. From 2014 to the present, the "1294" early warning system has been expanded throughout the country and recognized as belonging to the National Committee for Disaster Management.
Taking the opportunity, Dr. Hang Samoeun noted with satisfaction that PPE INIT in Cambodia has signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia from 2009 to 2022. In addition, PPE INIT in Cambodia also signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the NCDD. From 2014 to the present.
