(Phnom Penh): On April 29, 2022, at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, chaired a meeting with representatives of development partners, including the International Monetary Fund. (IMF), the World Bank (WB) and the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to discuss and monitor the global economic situation, as well as the macroeconomic situation and economic outlook of Cambodia.
According to the latest preliminary assessment by the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Cambodia's economic growth in 2022 is projected to continue to pick up, driven by growth in domestic economic activity, including: production, services and general consumption, driven by Highly vaccinated across the country, allowing full socio-economic activity to reopen.
However, the recovery of Cambodia's economic growth in 2022 is expected to increase at a rate of about 5.2% to 5.4%, lower than the forecast for early 2022 is 5.6% due to the impact of Rising inflation caused by the war between Russia and Ukraine, slowing China's economic growth and the continued tightening of China's borders have added to the uncertainty of the flow of foreign investment and capital to Cambodia.
Overall, the development partners agreed with the results of the reassessment of Cambodia's economic growth and highlighted the ongoing risks, as well as made good recommendations on policy measures to continue the growth movement. Such as weight loss, negative impact on society and people's lives.
