(Phnom Penh): A book on the life of a young Cambodian politician, Mr. Hun Many, entitled "Hun Many Hope" has been published for the first time in 10,000 copies to share knowledge with the public, especially among the youth.
On the cover of the front page, "Hun Many Hope" highlights Hun Many's personality, his political activities and his involvement in social work as a Cambodian youth who continues to take turns maintaining peace. And the development of the nation now and in the future.
Leang De Lux, co-founder of the new e-newspaper and author of the book, said that the content of this book describes the focus of a political successor in initiating activities for the benefit of the nation and the people after Elections in 2013, when the political heat was hot and sharp by mobilizing youth to do humanitarian work, social work, work to promote national culture.
The author goes on to say that the perception that Hun Many is a potential politician in the future and that he is popular among the masses has led new media to decide to cover a publication. This goes on the reading market.
He said he spent two years, from 2020 to 2021, writing a book about Hun Many's vision, will and commitment to building a better homeland for the people. Follow and observe his activities since 2013, as well as interview Mr. Hun Many many times, as well as collect information about Mr. Many from people who know and work with him.
Ky Soklim, the founder of the new e-newspaper, considers the work of the author of this book to observe the work and statements of Hun Many since 2013, which is of historical value both now and in the future for the youth in Gaining knowledge in the field of book writing and starting political activities of successors in Cambodian society.
In front of many journalists, Mr. Ky Soklim stated that for the publication of the book "Hope Hun Many", the new media unit is the sole guarantor of the publication of this book, while the book was compiled and published. Some of them have already written and published two more books, "The Keeper of Angkor" and "Changing Thoughts for a Prosperous Life".
Mr. Leang De Lux also expressed his happiness and belief that the readers of this book must have known the spirit, ideas, love for the country and the people of the character of Mr. Hun Many, a politician who took turns clearly.
According to the author, "When you read this book, you will know about the character, the way of thinking of HE Hun Many, some of the life of the Prime Minister's family, especially the life of His Excellency Many. "
"Hun Many also lives under the pressure of criticism from many who view him only as the son of a privileged prime minister," the author said. "On the contrary, it is because of the son of this supreme leader that His Excellency Many has to work harder for the honor of his family and to be able to establish a foothold for himself as an influential politician."
