Article by: Cambodia-China Friendship Radio The Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) officially receives the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Japanese Self-Defense Forces
(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, officially receives General Yamazaki Koji, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Japanese Self-Defense Forces at the General Command on the afternoon of April 28, 2022.
On that occasion, General Vong Pisen welcomed General Yamazaki Koji and his colleagues to visit Cambodia to strengthen relations and cooperation for the benefit of the two countries' armies as well as regional and global security. .
General Vong Pisen informed that the situation of Kovid-19 disease in Cambodia has been relieved and manageable, which he stated was not a coincidence, but due to the wise decision of Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Of Cambodia to put in place timely prevention strategies.
General Vong Pisen highlighted the trade relations between Cambodia and Japan dating back to the 17th century and the diplomatic ties dating back to 1953, and Japan was involved in the process of ending the chronic war, participating in peacebuilding and helping to build infrastructure. In Cambodia.
He hopes that in the future, the two armies will continue to work closely to exchange information and expand cooperation at all levels, especially the two countries' armies.
In response, General Yamazaki Koji expressed his pleasure to visit Cambodia again to strengthen the cooperation between the two countries in a strategic partnership.
General Yamazaki Koji praised the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the successful fight against Kovid-19, calling Cambodia the most highly governed country in the world.
The General also thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces for allowing a Japanese naval ship to dock at the port of Sihanoukville in March 2022, and said that this was a gesture of strengthening the friendship and cooperation between the two armies. Both countries.
The General emphasized that in the future, Japan is happy to continue to assist Cambodia in the field of UN peacekeeping missions, disaster relief, as well as human resource training.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth: Reform of public financial management as a strategy of the Royal Government to support economic growth
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, on April 28, 2022, emphasized that the reform of public financial management is a strategic ground for the Royal Government to Long-term development to support economic growth, maintain macroeconomic stability and social equity.
This emphasis was made on the occasion of Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Chairman of the Steering Committee for the Amendment of the Law on the New Public Financial System and Relevant Legal Standards, presiding over a consultation workshop on the draft law on the new Public Financial System at Sofitel Phnom Penh this morning, April 28, 2022.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth stated that "Public Financial Management Reform is the strategic foundation of the Royal Government for long-term development by building a responsive, efficient, transparent, accountable and sustainable public financial system." "And use public resources as well as support economic growth, maintain macroeconomic stability and social equity."
Mr. Vongsey Visoth, on behalf of the Chairman of the Steering Committee for the Amendment of the Law on the New Public Financial System, stated that the draft law on the new Public Financial System is a basic legal framework for managing budgets, information, achievements, which are the key components of accounting. Achievement, as well as other work related to public finance in the modern era.
He said that in the process of drafting the law, there is a comprehensive study, citing lessons learned and international practice from many countries such as France, Thailand, Malaysia, etc., and integrated into the system and experience of Cambodia's practical implementation to bring this draft to life can be responsive to both Cambodian and global facilities.
In addition, Mr. Vongsey Visoth emphasized that in order to make this important draft law more comprehensive and cellular, flexible and easy to implement in accordance with the Cambodian environment for the long term, the Ministry Economics and Finance organized this consultative workshop to gather additional input and feedback.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth added that the reform of public financial management will also contribute to building Cambodia's resilience in the face of frequent crises in the future. At present, the world, as well as Cambodia, has been going through the aftermath of the Kovid-19 crisis, reflecting the urgency and necessity of establishing a stronger and more resilient public financial management system.
(Siem Reap): The Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, the Ministry of Commerce and the Council for the Development of Cambodia (FMCC) have jointly organized four important law dissemination seminars for businessmen, business leaders and students to raise awareness at the Regin Sea Angkor Hotel in Siem Reap. .
The workshop was held on April 27, 2022 and was chaired by Mr. Mao Thora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. Phan Oun Ladies and Gentlemen, Businessmen, Business Owners, Enterprises, Students and more than 100 related partners.
Mr. Mao Thora stated that the workshop, which was jointly organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, the Ministry of Commerce and the Council for the Development of Cambodia, was to disseminate four important laws to the business community for the students to raise awareness:
1: Investment Law of Cambodia 2: Law on Consumer Protection 3: Law on Competition 4: Law on Quality and Safety Management of Products, Goods and Services, which are important laws as traders, investors need to understand and apply To be in accordance with the law, to avoid being fined or punished.
