Businessmen and economists' views on Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway tolls (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Businessmen and economists in Cambodia see the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway as an economic lifeline. And the launch of this road will greatly benefit the transportation of goods, especially textiles and agricultural products to the port of Sihanoukville, which reduces both time and budget.
At the same time, economists urge companies and the government to discuss the pricing of services to use this road more actively.
Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, praised the preparations for the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, which will facilitate the transportation of goods and boost economic growth.
Meanwhile, Oknha Ly Khun Thai, Honorary President of the Footwear and Travel Products Association, said that the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway will greatly benefit shoe, bag and garment factories across the country as the sector needs roads. This speed to make it easier and save more time to export goods.
So far, the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway has completed more than 90% of the construction and is scheduled to test run in July. This road will reduce the travel time from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville Port from five hours to just two hours and help reduce the cost of logistics.
Dr. Hong Vannak, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, told Fresh News that the $ 12 that the company plans to charge in the first year is a reasonable price for people to travel and transport goods similar to neighboring countries. Side.
"Relevant companies and ministries should also consider this sale, as there should be market research in other countries, neighboring countries and China," he said.
Please be informed that the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway project with a length of 187.05 km was started in March 2019 at a cost of about 2 billion dollars. This road connects Village 1, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh to Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province. There are 4 lanes with a total width of 24.5 meters. Place.
