Reuters reports that the measure will apply especially to fruits and vegetables, which are subject to the minimum price requirements for agricultural products subject to quotas and other industrial goods for which tariffs will be waived until the end of the year. 2022. The repeal of the 2016 EU-Ukraine Free Trade Agreement also applies to fertilizers, aluminum products and automobiles.
The EU will also exempt Ukraine from protective measures imposed on steel imports and lift the anti-dumping duty currently imposed on Ukraine's steel pipes, rolled steel products and steel plates. The measure will need the approval of the European Parliament and the European Union Government to enter into force.
The European Commission, which oversees trade policy in the 27-nation European Union, said the unprecedented measures were designed to ease difficulties for producers and exporters. Ukraine in the face of Russian aggression
Valdis Dombrovskis, Vice President of the European Commission and Commissioner for Trade, said: "Since the beginning of the Russian invasion, the EU has given priority to the importance of keeping Ukraine's economy moving forward. "To help Ukraine win this war and for post-war economic recovery."
Last year, bilateral trade between the EU and Ukraine was more than 52 billion euros ($ 55 billion), double what it was before the 2015 free trade agreement. According to Reuters.
