(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on April 28, 2022, sent a letter to US President Joe Biden to thank and respond to his invitation to attend the ASEAN-ASEAN Special Summit. The United States on May 12-13, 2022.
"I would like to thank His Excellency the President for sending me an invitation to the ASEAN-US Special Summit to be held in Washington on May 12-13, 2022. I am pleased to attend this meeting.
I am confident that reaffirming your commitment to further strengthen US-ASEAN relations, especially on the occasion of the 45th Anniversary of the ASEAN-US Dialogue Partnership, will be a step forward. Take our partnership to the next level. In this regard, Cambodia fully supports the enhancement of ASEAN-US relations from a strategic partner to a comprehensive strategic partner.
As the chair of ASEAN in 2022, I would like to reaffirm Cambodia's strong desire to seek more opportunities to expand ASEAN-US cooperation in all areas.
I believe that this special summit is a good opportunity for us to discuss, promote cooperation and exchange views on issues of common concern and interest of ASEAN and the United States.
I look forward to meeting with you in person in Washington and preparing to work closely with you.
Please accept, Excellency, the assurances of my highest consideration. ”
