Ministry of Economy Releases Press Release on National Consultative Workshop on Cambodian Financial Technology Policy and Direction
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance has issued a press release on the National Consultative Workshop on Policies and Directions of the Cambodian Financial Technology Sector. This is according to the press release received by Fresh News on April 27, 2022.
Digital technology is an important part of daily life and provides opportunities for the creation of new, dynamic and innovative businesses, the statement said.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has been paying close attention to maximizing the benefits of digital technology in building the digital economy, which will be an important pillar for Cambodia's socio-economic development.
In the context of Kovid-19, digital technology has increasingly contributed to economic stability and activity, promoting economic diversification and job creation, as well as potential new businesses. In this sense, digitalization has become a trend and a powerful driving force in Cambodia's economic growth.
In May 2021, the Royal Government of Cambodia launched the "Digital Economy and Social Policy Framework of Cambodia 2021-2035", considering the digital economy as a key to new economic growth and as an ecosystem contributing to economic productivity in other areas.
Financial technology, commonly referred to as FinTech, is also an essential basis in shaping the digital economy.
However, the financial technology sector in Cambodia has been facing a number of problems, including: shortcomings and uncertainties in the regulatory framework, lack of support for digital implementation, lack of human resources and lack of technological innovation. Finance in sectors other than banking.
The workshop was chaired by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Digital Economy and Business Committee. , Development Partners, Financial Institutions, Banks and Non-Banks, Associations, Financial Technology Companies, Businesses and Innovators.
The workshop went smoothly and achieved the expected results, with interactive and lively discussions between the speakers and participants with a shared and attentive spirit.
Through this workshop, the Committee on Digital Economy and Business received a lot of good input from participants who are experts and experienced in the field of financial technology, as well as have a deeper understanding of the implementation, regulatory framework, challenges and Recent developments in the field of financial technology in Cambodia, as well as in ASEAN member countries, including Singapore, Thailand, Indonesia and the Philippines.
This national consultation workshop is a good starting point in the process of drafting policies that are cellular, sharp, comprehensive, flexible, efficient and environmentally friendly. However, it is necessary to continue to gather more and more good input from key stakeholders in key areas of financial technology in the process of drafting this policy.
