First, continue to strengthen the education system to be resilient and proactive in responding to the changing national and international environment. Continue to ensure quality education services with equity and environment, as well as enhance lifelong learning opportunities for all and address the learning losses of students and youth affected by Kovid-19.
Second, to build the system and develop the capacity of the education system through ensuring the leadership and management of education officials at all levels, including the reform of teacher training institutions, improving the efficiency of cooperation financing, policy development and development planning. Regular careers for educators and teachers.
Third, continue to develop digital education for the training of human resources in the context of digital social and economic development through the integration of digital technology at all levels. Video tutorials and digital content on core subjects for exam classes, as well as dissemination of these works.
Fourth, continue to be more active in the work of Scouts and youth by adhering to positive actions in society by inspiring the movement "good children, good students, good friends, good citizens" volunteer youth programs to help local communities with training Technical and soft skills for young people to respond in a timely manner to job opportunities in society.
