General Knowledge: The Largest Living Animal on Earth
When it appears on the surface of the water, the blue whale exhales through a hole through which air can be raised up to a height of up to 9 meters. Blue whales give birth every three years and usually give birth to only one.
Baby blue whales can weigh up to three tons and be up to eight meters long at birth. Newborn blue whales are often brought to the surface by their master to breathe for the first time. Blue whales drink 600 liters of milk a day and gain 90 kilograms daily for the first year.
Blue whales sometimes swim in small groups, but most often they travel alone or in pairs. They communicate with each other using different sound waves, while under normal conditions, blue whales can hear each other at distances of up to 1,600 kilometers.
* Blue Whale Conservation Status
Extremely active fishing activities during the 1900s by whaling hunters for their oil caused the endangered blue whales as hundreds of thousands of whales were killed. Killed. Finally, in 1966, the International Whaling Commission regulated the protection of blue whales.
