On the occasion of closing the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered an hour-long speech, the following are the main contents:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the development partners of national and international organizations and relevant institutions for their cooperation and support in terms of material, budget and technical support.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has always given priority to the development of human resources to promote and develop the education sector in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to continue to strengthen the education system to be resilient and proactive in response to the changing national and international environment. Continue to ensure quality education services with equity and environment, as well as enhance lifelong learning opportunities for all and address the learning losses of students and youth affected by Kovid-19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends the continued development of digital education for the training of human resources in the digital social and economic development environment through the integration of digital technology into all levels of curricula equipped with digital laboratories in capacity building institutions. Digital teachers produce instructional videos and digital content on core subjects for exam classes, as well as disseminate these work more widely.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to continue to be more active in the work of scouts and youth by adhering to positive actions in society by inspiring the movement "good children, good students, good friends, good citizens" youth volunteer programs to help the grassroots. Community with training of technical and soft skills for young people to respond in a timely manner to job opportunities in society.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to continue to be fully prepared to host the 2023 SEA Games in cooperation with all stakeholders in the development of the People's Sports Association, the Federation - Sports, training and training of national players and players. Intensive nursery to promote physical education and sports activities in educational institutions.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to continue to improve health and hygiene in educational institutions by continuing to implement the "3 do not and 3 prevent" approach and participate in preventing the entry into educational institutions, including increasing education on safety, health, education, gap, safety and food safety. To educators and students. Continue to support the mental and physical health of students directly or indirectly affected by Kovid-19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen spoke optimistically about the achievements of the conference and the key recommendations that I mentioned will be the basis and transparent and effective input for implementation in the Cambodian education sector in the new school year and subsequent years. .
