Stamp duty exemption on transfer of ownership or possession of real estate (all types of housing) under the following conditions:
1: Acquisition of ownership or possession of real estate worth equal to or less than 70,000 USD at the actual market price stated in the contract of sale from February 25, 2020 to December 31, 2022 And come to declare the stamp duty during this period.
2. Acquisition of ownership or possession of real estate (all types of housing) from a housing development company registered with the Ministry of Economy and Finance, past or present, as a regulator of real estate and mortgage business or through the Department of Economy and Finance.
3: All housing developers must make a proper sales contract based on the actual market price. If necessary, the General Department of Taxation may re-examine housing developers who have taken the opportunity to reduce the purchase price from the actual market, affecting tax revenue.
Mr. Chrek Soknim, President of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors (CVEA), said that the mechanism for the renewal of stamp duty exemption for home buyers under $ 70,000 by the end of 2022 will help the real estate sector continue to operate in More trading.
"For me, the mechanism for the renewal of stamp duty exemption is an important part of helping investors have the opportunity to invest in real estate, buy and sell at a profit, these factors are motivating and supporting," he said. The national economy as well as the revenue of the state.
Please be informed that in February 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced a stamp duty exemption for houses equal to or less than $ 70,000 for one year from February 2020 to January 2021. But now, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to extend the favor for another year until the end of 2022. Chinese Foreign Ministry: Parties should maintain calm and restraint to avoid Europe and the world paying more
