This Afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Closing Ceremony of a Meeting of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports
Meetings A meeting to review the work of the school year 2020-2021 and work directions for the school year 2021-2022 of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports was held for 3 days from 25 to 27 April. The conference reviewed and discussed a lot of work related to education in Cambodia, as well as raised many directions to improve education and training better in the school year 2021-2022.
At the opening of the conference on April 25, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, presented some important achievements that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has achieved in the academic year 2020-2021, in particular. In the context of Kovid-19, as well as in the phase of education reform.
Then, in 2015, the Education Conference launched the "Vision for Education Reform" based on five pillars, including: 1) - Implementation of action plans, policies, teaching partners, 2) - Inspection, 3) - Evaluate tuition fees, 4) - Improvement of curriculum and learning environment and 5) - Higher education reform.
At the same time, in 2015, the Ministry of Education introduced the second phase of education reform measures, namely school reform. Over the past five years, the Ministry has tried to implement school reform by establishing two reform models, including: First, the establishment of a new generation of schools at the request of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy. And finance.
The Minister of Education also highlighted the effective management of schools (SBM). According to Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, in order to effectively manage the school, the Ministry has focused on five principles, including: First: Accountability: Principals must be accountable to parents by establishing a school management committee and contracting performance. Annual, evaluation meetings, and self-assessments to achieve effective school standards.
The minister claimed that the ministry had selected 100 schools for the reform, and that almost all of the schools had achieved effective school standards and had an impact on nearly 300 network schools.
Minister Hang Chuon Naron also said that in 2022, the Education Conference decided to launch measures to reform the education sector in the third phase: system building and capacity development. In this spirit, the Ministry sets out a number of priorities, including:
1: Implement the results-oriented management approach towards systematic and sub-sectoral problem-solving Strengthening the education management system: by combining the review of functions and tasks, annual planning, Capacity development, implementation of career trajectories, strengthening of version implementation and monitoring and evaluation.
3. Strengthening the system and changing the way it works: By turning the implementation of projects into strengthening the system and developing policies and guidelines.
Mr. Hang Chuon Naron also said that although the teaching and learning process in the past two years has been interrupted by the Kovid-19 crisis, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has continued to implement the reform program and turned the Kovid crisis. -19 to be an opportunity too
According to the report of the Ministry of Education, in the school year 2021-2022, Cambodia has 18,430 kindergartens and general education institutions, both public and private. There are 3,083 community kindergartens, 13,681 public general education institutions and 1,666 private educational institutions.
The total number of students studying at the tertiary level was 198,363, 49.7 percent of whom were female.
