Implementing Kovid 19 disease-free policy is an effective option to restore China's economic growth well
BEIJING (Reuters) - The 19 new Kovid virus can be transmitted faster than the previous 19 Kovid viruses, and the symptoms of the new 19 Kovid virus infection are less pronounced, leading to the search for new strains of the virus. This is more difficult. Health experts claim that curbing the spread of the 19 new Kovid virus is more than 10 times more difficult than stopping the spread of the 19 Kovid virus.
At first, the West criticized China's attack on Kovid 19, but they later adopted the same strategy. But they are incomplete and inconsistent, which has caused serious consequences in their country, with many infected with the Kovid 19 virus and dying.
On the contrary, in the run-up to the recent outbreak, China has been remarkably successful in controlling the epidemic. It is this 19-year-old Kovid-free policy that keeps the number of 19 Kovid cases, the number of serious illnesses and the number of deaths in China low, despite being the world's most populous country. Anyway.
The Kovid 19 disease-free policy is a science-based strategy and has been shown to be highly effective in preventing the spread of disease in just a few weeks. Through the implementation of the Kovid-free policy, Shenzhen, a large city with a population of more than 17 million, was able to control the spread of the 19 new Kovid virus in a single month.
