Within the bilateral framework, the Deputy Prime Minister reaffirmed Cambodia's deep gratitude to the Italian Government for donating 1.56 million doses of Astra Zeneca vaccine to Cambodia, which was hosted by Samdech Techo Prime Minister on April 25, 2022, this aid shows the global solidarity in the fight against Kovid-19 disease.
The Deputy Prime Minister highlighted the excellent bilateral cooperation demonstrated through trade exchanges and the presence of well-known Italian brands and restaurants in Cambodia. The Kovid-19 crisis, bilateral trade volume has stabilized and continued to grow, and encouraged both sides to find more effective ways to boost trade volume.
He also thanked Italy for providing assistance to Cambodia in the field of culture under the APSARA Authority through the training of experts in the preservation of Khmer ancient temples.
In response, the Ambassador praised the excellent results of the vaccination campaign in Cambodia and thanked Cambodia for providing free vaccinations to Italians living in Cambodia and providing Good cooperation of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to you in fulfilling its duties.
Within the ASEAN framework, the Deputy Prime Minister briefed the Ambassador on the actual situation and challenges in Myanmar and the outcome of his first visit to Myanmar as the Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair on Myanmar. Both subsequent steps are aimed at promoting the implementation of the five-point consensus of ASEAN leaders.
