Cambodia, Italy vow to boost trade
(Phnom Penh): In the afternoon of April 26, 2022, at the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, paid a courtesy call on Mr. Lorenzo Galanti, newly appointed Italian Ambassador to Cambodia and his colleagues. To discuss the progress of bilateral economic and trade cooperation.
The Minister warmly welcomed the Ambassador and his colleagues and thanked the people and Government of the Italian Republic for their continued technical assistance and financial support to Cambodia, especially in the Kovid-19 facility. The country recently donated 1,056,000 doses of the Kovid-19 AstraZeneca vaccine to Cambodia.
Minister Pan Sosak briefed on the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to combat Kovid-19 through effective prevention measures and successful vaccination campaigns that allow Cambodia to fully engage in economic activity. In all areas and recently reached the exemption of wearing masks in public places across the country.
"As Cambodia moves forward in living with Kovid-19 on the new normal trajectory and the fourth industrial revolution, trade and investment have played an important role in the country's development, especially economic recovery," he said. Recovering from the Kovid-19 crisis.
In response, the Ambassador thanked for the welcome and acknowledged the pace of development of the country in all areas, especially recent developments in Cambodia's international trade. In addition, the Ambassador informed about the will and efforts of the Government of the Italian Republic in preparing to host the World Expo in Rome 2030.
