Ministry of Tourism announces exemption of mask duty in public places for tourists
(Phnom Penh) The Ministry of Tourism has issued a notification on the implementation of the waiver of wearing masks in public places throughout Cambodia to national and international tourists in order to promote and attract tourists, especially to contribute to making Cambodia Attractive and warm tourist destination.
This announcement is made in accordance with the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on April 25, 2022, in which all national and international tourists are exempted from wearing the mask duty in all public places throughout Cambodia. Includes open space destinations such as resorts, community tourism, golf courses and other open space attractions.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also gave an interview to the media regarding the current situation of road construction as well as other conditions on the use of this road. The senior minister said that the construction of the expressway is more than 90 percent complete and is scheduled to be put into operation in July. In particular, the official inauguration depends on the appropriate time of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The Minister of Public Works and Transport also explained some conditions and procedures for using this road. According to the senior minister, this road does not allow travel such as bicycles or motorbikes, and the speed limit of the Ministry is considering allowing up to 120 km.
Separately, the cost of transit, Senior Minister claimed that the Royal Government plans to discuss with investment companies below 10 cents per kilometer. So if you travel from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville for nearly 200 kilometers, the cost of travel can be close to $ 20.
Please note that this expressway has a high foundation and fences on the sidewalk to prevent animals from crossing. On either side of the road, there are settlements of the people.
To facilitate faster travel, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol suggested that drivers be able to use the lane between slow and fast lanes. That is, the slow lane is on the right and the fast lane is on the left.
However, the senior minister insisted that there would be no restrictions for trucks to travel on the expressway, depending on the driver.
