Mr. Hun Many Inaugurates New Library and Provides a New School Building in Kampong Speu Province
(Kampong Speu): On the morning of April 26, 2022, Mr. HUN Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Constituency, attended the inauguration ceremony of the Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship Library and Ping Pong Primary and Secondary School in Damnak Reang Commune, Oudong District, Kampong Speu Province.
The event was attended by Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu, Mr. Ly Son, Chairman of Udong District Assistance Team, members of Damnak Reang Commune, Udong District and many teachers and students.
In the report, Mr. Sreang Kimly, President of the Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association and Chairman of the Damnak Reang Commune Assistance Team, described the background of the construction, highlighting the opportunity provided by Mr. HUN Many to assist the Damnak Reang Commune, which is why His Excellency studied the situation and challenges that are lacking in the actual commune.
For these reasons, the team mobilized philanthropists to build a library building. Due to the shortage of buildings, the library is used as a temporary classroom to help address the actual shortage of school buildings.
After listening to Mr. Sreang Kimly's report, Mr. Vy Samnang expressed his satisfaction with the facilitation and development of education in Kampong Speu province.
He added, "My nephews are now lucky enough to carry pens and books to school. It is not as difficult to build a building on their own as it was when my uncle was a student. You are lucky to have a new school building and a library to study." "Study and self-study."
He also praised the team that worked hard to raise funds to build the library, and all these successes are under the auspices of the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In addition to inaugurating the new library building and seeing the actual condition of an old dilapidated building in the school, Mr. Hun Many requested the feasibility study team to build a new three-room building instead of the dilapidated building to Give as additional gifts to teachers and students, as well as people in Damnak Reang commune.
Please note that the construction of this library started in June 2020 and will be completed in June 2021. This library is called the Library of Youth Ship of Southeast Asia, Cambodia, with a size of 8.5 meters by 16 meters. The library cost about $ 30,000 to build.
3 Suspects Arrested in Drug Trafficking Case and Confiscated in Poipet City
(Banteay Meanchey): With the attention of Major General Sithi Loh, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner and implementing direct orders from Colonel Sao Saroeun, Poipet City Police Inspector, on April 26, 2022, Phsar Kandal Sangkat Police Force With Poipet City Anti-Drug Forces cracked down on drug trafficking cases and arrested 3 suspects in Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
The operation was led by Brigadier General Prem Sophal, Phsar Kandal Sangkat Administration Post Chief.
Please note that on April 23, 2022 at 15:30 pm, people reported to the administrative post of Sangkat Phsar Kandal that there was a case of drug distribution at a rented room in front of O'Neang Market in O'Russey Village, Sangkat O'Russey Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Immediately after receiving the information, the Phsar Kandal Sangkat Administration Post requested an order from Colonel Sao Saroeun, Poipet City Police Inspector, to go to the point where the villagers reported and arrested two suspects with the following names:
First name: Phan Saroeun, male, 29 years old, ethnic Khmer, living in Orussey village, Sangkat Orussey, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, Occupation: Laundry worker (room owner for rent).
Second name: Phan Sokly, male, 22 years old, ethnic Khmer, living in Orussey village, Sangkat Orussey, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, unreliable occupation.
According to the confession, all the exhibits belonged to Phan Saroeun, the owner of the rented room, and the drugs were bought from Touch Sieng, alias Leang, a 38-year-old man living in Prey Kob village, Orussey commune, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
According to Phan Saroeun's confession, on April 24, 2022 at 12:30, the Central Market Police Force, in cooperation with the Drug Planning Special Forces, continued to detain Touch Sieng alias Leang at Tuol Prasat Village, Poipet Sangkat. Poipet, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Phsar Kandal Sangkat Administration Police and Drug Enforcement Forces confiscated exhibits including: 1 bag of white gram (1 bite), 1 drug scale and 1 bag for drug port. The suspect confessed that the drug belonged to him and bought it from a resident of Phnom Penh, but did not know his name, so he contacted to buy it by phone: 097 44 48 744.
Currently, the three suspects and exhibits have been put together and sent to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police for legal action.
