Ministry is examining the possibility of rehabilitating the waterway along the Bassac River from Prek Ambel to Takeo to Kampot and Kep
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on April 25, 2022, led a working group to inspect the progress of the construction of TS11 multi-purpose satellite port of Phnom Penh Autonomous Port, located along National Road No. 5 km 6, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh and meet with Board, officials, staff, workers.
Speaking on that occasion, the Senior Minister confirmed that the Royal Government has allowed the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to study the restoration of the waterway along the Bassac River from Prek Ambel to Takeo, Kampot, Kep, a distance of 168 kilometers, and the Ministry of Public Works and Transport is working. Study the restoration of the waterway and check whether it is possible to build this waterway or not.
The Senior Minister emphasized that the planning of waterway rehabilitation and construction of additional ports is a very important direction in shortening the transport distance from all rivers to the Cambodian sea, reducing the time and distance of profit. Transport budgets reduce traffic accidents and road congestion pressures, as well as increase waterway transport activities.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol added that the redevelopment of the Tonle Bassac waterway, as well as the redevelopment of the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port, is a step that will greatly increase inland waterway transport. It is a big step to help increase water transport and expand Cambodia's logistics sector to be more efficient.
