(Phnom Penh): On the morning of April 26, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, announced the exemption of the duty to wear a mask to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia in public after the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia. Much relieved.
Citizens, traders, businessmen and government officials have expressed their happiness after the head of the Royal Government announced the exemption of wearing masks in public places from today onwards.
They also expressed their happiness and deep gratitude for the efforts of Samdech Techo, who sought to vaccinate the people all over the country, so that Cambodia could control the spread of the disease. Of Kovid 19 well and through the efforts of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and local authorities to control and prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
Please be informed that after receiving the opinion from the inter-ministerial meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen on April 26, 2022 announced the exemption of the duty to wear masks in public places throughout the country, but requires people to continue to wear masks in place. The closure has an air conditioner and so on.
The removal of the masked measures in public came after the government observed that the rate of 19 cases of Kovid was at an all-time low, despite the fact that Cambodia allowed the New Year to be celebrated with a large number of people. Without wearing a mask or keeping a gap.
However, the government encourages the wearing of masks in places of suspicion or crowded places. Places that used to comply with the ministry's standards, such as restaurants, must continue to follow the ministry's guidelines. Samdech Techo hopes that the Cambodian people will be freed from the hardships by spending money to buy masks instead of vaccinations.
