(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government is preparing to develop a policy document for the development of Cambodia's financial technology sector to support economic and social development.
This national consultation workshop was attended by civil servants of relevant ministries, institutions, embassies, development partners, financial institutions, banks and non-banks, associations, financial technology companies, business people and innovators.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, stated that Cambodia's financial technology development policy will be an important part of building financial technology infrastructure, attracting domestic and foreign investment. Promoting the creation of new businesses and financial technology companies, enhancing financial technology products and services, and promoting economic competitiveness.
The Deputy Prime Minister strongly hopes that representatives of relevant ministries, institutions, development partners, the private sector, both in the banking and non-banking sectors, associations, financial technology companies, business people, and innovators who have participated in this workshop will actively participate in Sharing knowledge and experience and providing input to be a valuable asset for the policy team to start the implementation process.
