On April 26, 2022, Ms. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, handed over a water sanitation facility funded by the Singapore Red Cross to seven target schools in Kampong Cham province.
The ceremony took place at Andong Ta Ong Primary School and Prek Krabao Secondary School in Kang Meas District, Kampong Cham Province, and was attended by HE Un Chanda, Chairman of the Kampong Cham Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross.
On the occasion of handing over and receiving, Mrs. Pum Chantyny brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all the people who always have sympathy and sympathy for students, teachers. Especially people who have difficulty accessing clean water.
At the same time, she said that these sanitation facilities are very important for the people and the seven schools, because these structures were built in safe places during the floods and schools. Priority requirements on hygiene and clean water.
Students, teachers and people who benefit from this sanitation project, we would like to express our deepest gratitude to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always thinks of the people everywhere. Clean water and regular hygiene and sanitation.
It should be noted that with the assistance of the Singapore Red Cross, the Cambodian Red Cross, the Central Level, together with the Kampong Cham Provincial Branch, built 2 motor wells, 8 hand washing stations, 1 newly built toilet, 3 rooms, 1 toilet repair, 4 rooms and installed. New 2000 liter water tank with 1 stand for 7 target schools in Kampong Cham province for 24,200 USD.
Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, stated that these sanitation facilities have been provided for students, teachers and teachers to use to improve health, hygiene and participate in preventing the spread of Kovid-19 disease in the community as well as the affected people. Flooded and evacuated to safety.
