Thai Ministry of Commerce to curb rising consumer prices amid rising cost of living
BANGKOK: The Thai Ministry of Commerce has vowed to do its utmost to curb rising consumer prices as the Thai government no longer sets diesel prices and allows them to rise on the first day. May. According to the Bangkok Post.
He said the ministry had analyzed the cost of the product and that despite the increase in diesel prices, this did not mean that the cost of each product would increase. He said it was necessary to consider whether the high pricing really reflected production costs.
He said that if the cost is really high, the price of the product can be allowed to increase. He said, however, that if the cost increased slightly, requests for an unreasonable price increase would be rejected.
"The Department of Internal Trade has analyzed the cost of all kinds of goods," he said. The ministry will closely monitor commodity prices. ” "If there is not too much impact on production costs, the company will be asked to bear the extra cost and not pass it on to consumers at this time," he added. "Most importantly, they must not take advantage of the situation and raise prices unreasonably."
