Cambodia's fresh fruit exports are facing challenges as shipping costs to China jump to $ 8,000 and to the US and Europe to nearly $ 20,000
(Phnom Penh): The cost of shipping fresh fruit in cold containers from Cambodia to China has tripled compared to last year, rising from more than $ 2,000 to about $ 8,000 per foot while exports Cross-continental has risen to nearly $ 20,000, affecting Cambodia's fresh fruit exports this season.
Exports of fresh bananas were also affected, but not as severely as mangoes, as bananas were in constant demand and orders as China and neighboring countries did not meet Chinese demand. Therefore, Cambodia can still export despite the high price of containers because the price of bananas is also high. Rice exports also rose in price, but were acceptable as prices rose.
Tycoon Sin Chanthy, president of the Logistics Association of Cambodia, also told Fresh News that the normal price before shipping to China was only $ 2,500, but this year it reached $ 8,000. The increase of about 8,000 is for regional shipping only, but transcontinental shipments, such as to the United States and Europe, jumped from more than $ 4,000 to nearly $ 20,000, and some destinations increased by $ 20,000. Another dollar.
"We are still normal, there may be some decline, but some areas are in high demand, there is an increase, overall there is still transportation, exports are up," he said. "And if we talk about the value of the economy, it hurts, and in the past we spent less, now we spend more."
