Cambodia joined WIPO in 1995 after committing to the adoption of a number of key laws, including national intellectual property laws and related regulations. After two years of participation, in 1997, the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to issue a sub-decree to establish the Department of Intellectual Property under the Ministry of Commerce.
After becoming a member, Cambodia always organizes Intellectual Property Day every year, and for 2022, tomorrow, April 26, the Department of Intellectual Property, Ministry of Commerce, Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and WIPO will organize the World Intellectual Property Day. Under the theme of intellectual property and youth "Innovation for a better future" at Aeon Mall Sen Sok City (3rd floor).
World Intellectual Property Day 2022 will be presided over by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the National Committee for Intellectual Property Management, with the participation of Dr. Phoeung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, Mr. Daren Tan, Director General of WIPO Representative of the US Ambassador to Cambodia, Representative of the EU Ambassador to Cambodia and stakeholders.
Please be informed that Cambodia currently has 4 laws related to intellectual property, including:
1. Trademark law and acts of dishonest competition, promulgated on 7 February 2002, clarify the duties of the Ministry of Commerce on trademarks. The Ministry of Commerce does not exclusively control all issues related to intellectual property.
2. Law on patents, useful models and industrial drawings is regulated by the Ministry of Industry, Mines and Energy. This law was promulgated on January 22, 2003, while the Ministry was preparing regulations such as sub-decrees or prakas for the implementation of this law.
3. The Law on Copyright and Related Rights, promulgated on March 23, 2003, is governed by the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts for the protection of this right.
4. The Law on Plant Variety Control and Plant Breeder's Rights was adopted on April 8, 2008 under the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Drug addiction is a treatable brain disease! Nationwide drug crackdown for April 25: 18 cases cracked, 49 arrested
