In a speech congratulating the 50th Anniversary of Artemisinin and the International Cooperation Forum for Building a Community of General Health for Humanity, this Monday, April 25, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen celebrated the 50th Anniversary of Artemisinin. And the International Cooperation Forum to Build a Community of General Health for Humanity.
Samdech Techo also announced his support for the activities and cooperation that have been implemented to build a community of general health for humanity, especially the eradication of malaria through the use of artemisinin.
In his speech, the Prime Minister said that Cambodia in the Greater Mekong Subregion had more than 170,000 cases of malaria and nearly 1,000 deaths in the 1980s. In 2021, however, the number of malaria cases dropped to 3,959 and there were no deaths in the last four years, despite the difficulties posed by the Kovid-19 outbreak.
Samdech Techo also highlighted that the effectiveness of the implementation of the national strategy is to connect with flexibility and flexibility in global and regional strategies, as well as learn from each other's experiences.
For the future direction, Samdech Techo announced that Cambodia will continue to strengthen cooperation with all stakeholders, especially China, through the Belt and Road Initiative, the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation and the South-South Cooperation Assistance Fund. China, for example, to eradicate malaria completely.
He also called on all stakeholders to continue to promote cooperation based on trust, partnership, people-centered and multilateralism in order to achieve the 2025 Malaria-Free World Vision.
April 25, 2022 is also the National Day of Cambodia in the fight against malaria. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also issued a message to celebrate the National Day Against Malaria.
In this message, Samdech Techo highlighted that malaria not only affects health, direct spending on treatment, job loss, loss of productivity and life, but also has a negative impact on social development. - Serious economy.
Although Cambodia has achieved good results in the fight against malaria, Samdech Techo requested the relevant parties to work to accelerate the eradication of malaria in accordance with the plan in the action plan to eradicate malaria. Defeat the second phase of 2021-2025, which is part of the National Strategic Plan for Malaria Eradication in Cambodia 2011-2025. In particular, we must work together to achieve three key goals, including:
In this message, Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, thanked all stakeholders, both inside and outside the country, including officials, health workers and all the people who have made Samdech Achievements successful in the fight against malaria in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to call on ministries, institutions, local authorities at all levels, the private sector, organizations, media, national and international community and development partners, especially all people, to continue to support and support the mission of the Ministry of Health in accordance with the National Strategic Plan. Eliminate malaria in Cambodia successfully and achieve the goal of the National Strategic Plan to eradicate malaria in 2025.
