Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of receiving more than 1 million doses of Kovid vaccine 19 with the help of Italy
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, April 25, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, received more than 1 million doses of Kovid 19 vaccine with the help of the Italian government and people. The handover ceremony took place at the Peace Palace.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech with the following main contents:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in Cambodia, the crisis of Kovid-19 has led to strict measures and reached the decision to close the border as well as close major economic zones on an unprecedented scale, but Cambodia's economy will recover in 2021 with a positive growth rate of about 3% after suffering a severe impact in 2020.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that this recovery reflects the active participation of the Cambodian people, national and international organizations, development partners and friendly countries with the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia. In particular, the National Vaccination Campaign aims to build community immunity across the country, which has allowed Cambodia to reopen the country and resume full socio-economic activities in all areas.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that, in fact, on March 17, 2022, Cambodia has taken further steps to live with Kovid-19 in a new normal path, with the Royal Government deciding to cancel the conditions. All requirements for foreign travelers who have been fully vaccinated in the tourism gateway destination, the last major sector that has yet to be restored.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that for the future direction, while Kovid-19 is still causing uncertainty, the Royal Government will continue to promote the national vaccination campaign, which provides expensive Kovid-19 vaccine from the people and the government. Italy today will also make a significant contribution.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has also been monitoring the development of the conflict between Ukraine and Russia, which has been creating many challenges, especially energy shortages, high crude oil prices and the rise of Inflation rates can negatively affect investment, trade, and regional and global production chains.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia also highly appreciates the promotion of cooperation between Italy-ASEAN and EU-ASEAN. As the chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia will continue to promote this cooperation in all fields to be stronger, and Cambodia would like to encourage the Republic of Italy as well as the European Union to continue to promote business and investment in Cambodia as well. More ASEAN.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterates his call for people to be vaccinated in the third dose, which is mandatory, with Cambodia remaining about 6 million people who have not yet been vaccinated in the third dose, while more than 1 million people have been vaccinated in the fourth dose.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech intends to remove the wearing of masks in public, but in closed places still continue to wear masks, but this decision will wait for a special meeting today, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth And the Minister of Health.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth and Professor Mam Bunheng to chair the meeting. Samdech wants the removal of the duty to wear a mask in public squares, but requires the wearing of a mask in a closed place.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that we must not only see health problems, but also the socio-economic situation. Wearing a mask is a huge expense for our citizens.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen awaits a meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth and Mam Bun Heng to remove health duties in some provinces or regions, but this removal will leave it up to the people to choose whether to wear a mask or not.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the future we will remove the measures to wear masks in public places, but keep the distance and wash hands, which Samdech predicted that wearing masks will cost Cambodians about $ 30,000 per Days.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that today Cambodia has only 12 cases, which is very low since after the New Year is below 20 people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers that the low rate of infection and death in Cambodia now due to community immunity caused by past vaccinations to the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that Kovid 19 vaccine will arrive in a row, with more than 20 million doses left, as promised by our friend, to be sent to Cambodia in the future while our warehouse remains More than 11 million doses.
