The "Global Security" initiative contributes to the "China Plan" for the protection and stabilization of global security in the new era.
(Beijing): Currently, although most countries are under the shadow of peace, some countries are suffering from war or insecurity, such as terrorism and the threat of cyber-attacks. Therefore, resolving security issues is the most urgent task in the eyes of countries.
In this regard, while addressing the 2022 annual meeting of the Boao Forum for Asia, Chinese President Xi Jinping outlined China's new "Global Security" initiative to contribute to the "China Plan" for Anchors the global security balance in the new era.
As we all know, if a society is insecure, people will be insecure in the long run, which will endanger national peace. In line with the evolution of the era, many insecurities, especially non-traditional security, have gradually increased, which has become a great hidden danger to the peace of the nation.
After all, the prerequisite for a country to have full security is the sovereignty and territorial integrity of the nation to be fully protected without any interference from any black hand. In this sense, countries must say "no" to the threat of hegemony under various pretexts, because the vast majority of countries are always on the side of truth, that is, under any circumstances, adhere to multilateralism. Is not in isolation.
According to the objectives and principles of the UN Charter, large and small countries must have equal rights, in this sense, small countries must not be the pawn of competition between superpowers or the capital of the country's political game. That superpower. The superpowers that embrace the concept of the Cold War, causing insecurity in other countries, will inevitably be left with a bad name in history and despised by society as a whole.
