The following is Samdech Techo Hun Sen's message: This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen received more than 1 million doses of 19 vaccines against Kovid with the help of Italy.
(Phnom Penh): On Monday morning, April 25, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, received more than 1 million doses of Kovid 19 vaccine with the help of the Italian government and people. The handover ceremony took place at the Peace Palace.
To contribute to the fight against Kovid 19 in Cambodia, the Italian government and people have provided 1,056,000 doses of the AstraZenica vaccine to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia. Vaccines from the government and the people of Italy arrived in Cambodia this Sunday morning, April 24, 2022.
Vaccination against Kovid 19 is a vital option in the strategy to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and protect the lives of people from Kovid 19 attacks. Based on this strategy, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Commander-in-Chief of the Battle of Kovid 19, promoted vaccination and vaccination as quickly as possible.
Under the strict order of Samdech Techo with the prompt action of doctors and relevant authorities at all levels, so far Cambodia has achieved vaccination of people from the age of 3 years more than 93% of the population. Citizens across the country. As of April 23, Cambodia has injected nearly 15 million people in the first dose, more than 14 million in the second dose, more than 8 million in the third dose, and more than 1 million in the fourth dose.
Achieving a large number of vaccination plans at this high speed is also due to Cambodia's availability of vaccines at a high speed. So far, Cambodia has received a total of more than 50 million doses of the vaccine, with nearly 10 million remaining in stock.
Through the implementation of this rapid vaccination plan, the Cambodian people have been able to overcome the 19 19 outbreak of Kovid and prevent the high mortality rate of 19 Kovid, and have reached the launch of social activities. Completed again in November 2021.
Despite strong resilience in the community, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to urge people to receive the recommended dose. Samdech Techo has launched a new plan that Cambodians of legal age will be allowed to receive at least three doses of the vaccine.
The remarkable results of the fight against Kovid 19 have led to national and international appreciation for the actions of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as the cooperation of the authorities and the participation of the people. Citizens.
