(Pursat): On April 23, 2022, at 2:00 AM, Mobile Area Customs Force, Area 4, in cooperation with Pursat Provincial Customs and Excise Officers, National Gendarmerie Officers and Pursat Provincial Gendarmerie Officers, with the coordination of Pursat Provincial Prosecutor cracked down on 2 duty-free luxury cars in Pursat Province.
The crackdown is on the recommendation of HE Kun Nhem, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister in charge of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, on the case of the expiration of the 10% import tax deduction for existing left-hand drive vehicles in the country. And with the indication of the Deputy Director General and the Director of the Department of Crime Prevention and Suppression.
Currently, the two vehicles have been handed over to the customs force of the Office of Investigation and Suppression of Smuggling in Area 4 to record the violation of customs rules and procedures.
