(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has claimed that the Royal Government of Cambodia is considering exempting some provinces or regions from the obligation to wear masks after observing that during the traditional Khmer New Year. Cambodia has a very low infection rate due to community immunity.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Prime Minister instructed the specialized committee to increase the third dose of vaccination for all citizens to achieve the reduction of obligations.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, so far, Cambodia has vaccinated more than 8 million people with the third dose of 19-dose measles vaccine, but more than 6 million people have not been vaccinated. Samdech instructed Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chairman of the Commission, to increase the third dose in crowded places such as workers, market vendors and informal economic groups.
Samdech stated that the reduction of some health measures, especially the three preventive measures that can remove the mask or reduce the gap or not, depends on the community immunity that we saw during the New Year. The past year has been a lot of contact, there is no infection.
Samdech also called on workers and people across the country to participate in the third dose as needed, which is part of the steps to ease health measures for the most part.
Samdech advised Ms. O Vandin to cooperate with all forces to inject the third dose to all workers and informal economic groups. Samdech urges the use and preparation of force, including the consideration of students and children who are about to give the third dose.
Please note that on April 10, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to put four provinces no longer required to wear a mask. The four provinces are: Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear. However, the government leaves it up to the people to decide for themselves whether to wear it or not.
