At the summit, the Prime Minister delivered a keynote address highlighting the importance of water as a necessary resource for sustainable development. In this regard, Samdech Techo Prime Minister stressed the need to work together to manage water sustainably for now and in the future through:
1. Continuing to promote the development and integration of infrastructure networks to support the management of water resources in the country at the regional and global levels.
2. Continuing to promote the development of responsible socio-economic activities and supporting green development, especially for agriculture, which is a sector that requires a lot of water.
3. Promoting and enhancing our digital cooperation to advance the development of digital technology in the efficient use and management of water resources.
4. Continuing support for programs, initiatives and activities to promote social sustainability in the use and management of water resources to ensure that people around the world have access to the water they need.
The Prime Minister reaffirmed Cambodia's strong commitment to co-operate with all stakeholders through mechanisms at both the regional and international levels to strengthen and enhance governance and management of water resources and the Mekong Basin. To be more efficient and effective in achieving the goal of "water for sustainable development".
Samdech Techo reaffirmed his strong belief that our high level of political will, efforts and joint actions will ensure the successful achievement of this goal.
