More than 400 Families in Prey Nob District and Khemarak Phoumin City Receive Donations from Cambodian Muslim Development Foundation and Kuwait Philanthropists
(Preah Sihanouk-Koh Kong): 200 families in Prey Nup district, Preah Sihanouk province, in Khemarak Phoumin city, Koh Kong province, 220 families received donations from Millie Internazonale of the United Arab Emirates through the Muslim Development Foundation of Cambodia and a Kuwaiti philanthropist. The ASEAN Foundation for Education and Development is co-organized by the Cambodian Muslim Development Foundation.
The distribution ceremony was presided over by Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and President of the Cambodian Muslim Development Foundation on April 24, 2022. Among them, 200 families in O Trav village, Andong Thmor commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province, and 220 families in Sangkat Dang Tong, Khemarak Phoumin city, Koh Kong province.
