He also recalled the many achievements that the Muslim community has received from the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Muslims have the opportunity to work for the state from the national level to the local level. 1,500 Khmer Muslim teachers have been included in the teaching framework of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
Muslim women can wear hijab (wearing a krama to cover their hair) to study at all levels of education and work in public institutions, private companies, NGOs, etc. In addition, the government has given the right to dress religiously for taking important documents such as ID cards, family books, passports and other administrative documents as required.
Mr. Osman Hassan added that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which ensured the harmony between race and religion in Cambodia, there was no discrimination, no racism and no religion. In addition, the Cambodian government is always involved in addressing the concerns and needs of the Cambodian Muslim community. Therefore, we must all thank peace and continue to support the Royal Government to maintain this peace for a long time to come.
Finally, Dr. Osman Hassan also reminded people to take care of their own health by following the rules of the Ministry of Health to avoid all kinds of diseases, especially Kovid 19.
It should also be informed that the donation received from the above organization for the people from the 420 Khmer Muslim families, with 200 families in Pren Nob district, each family received 25 kg of rice, 1 kg of sugar, 2 cans of milk and 1 bottle of syrup. Separately, for 220 families in Khemarak Phoumin City, each family received 25 kg of rice, 5 packets of noodles, 1 kg of sugar and 1 bottle of cooking oil.
