Cambodia-Indonesia trade ministers pledge to strengthen trade and economic cooperation
(Phnom Penh): The Ministers of Commerce of Cambodia and Indonesia have pledged to work together to further strengthen trade and economic cooperation between Cambodia and Indonesia.
This agreement was made during a working meeting between Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce of Cambodia and Mr. Muhammad Lutfi, Minister of Commerce of Indonesia on video on April 22, 2022.
In response, the Minister of Commerce of Indonesia has given his full support and is ready to provide closer cooperation to strengthen Cambodia-Indonesia trade cooperation, especially support for Cambodia as the chair of ASEAN in 2022.
Minister Muhammad Lutfi stated that he also agreed and supported the ASEAN Trade Promotion Mechanism in order to be able to use ASEAN trade to its full potential based on the ASEAN Middle East Principles.
(Kampong Cham): As the Chairman of the Party Working Group in Prey Chhor District and Batheay District, Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Pan Sosak constructed a series of CPP headquarters buildings in these two local communes to facilitate the work of Party members. .
On April 23, 2022, two new CPP headquarters buildings in Samrong and Trapeang Preah communes, Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province were officially inaugurated by Mr. Pan Sosak.
The event was attended by the chairperson, vice chairman and members of the 15 commune party working groups in Samrong commune, Trapeang commune, district party, local party committee, commune party committee, village party, commune youth and Many village youths.
On that occasion, Mr. Pan Sosak expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the Chairman, Vice Chairman and members of the party working group in Samrong and Trapeang Preah communes, as well as relevant authorities at all levels who took all the physical, mental and resource. Personally to serve the people and develop the commune to grow as it is now.
The Chairman of the Working Group also mentioned the value of peace to the members. "Peace is very valuable, so as a citizen, especially a member of the Cambodian People's Party, we must sacrifice everything, at any cost, to maintain peace in order to become a nation," he said. "We want to be a developed country and a high-income country in the future."
Mr. Pan Sosak also called on all people who have already registered to vote to be ready to vote for the Commune / Sangkat Council, which will be held on June 5, 2022.
He also called on all people to take care of the achievements that come from the efforts of the Cambodian nation to be stable. In addition, to participate in preventing and protecting themselves from the infection of Kovid-19 and other diseases by maintaining hygiene and implementing the "03 do not 03 prevent" measures consistently and to be vaccinated in all doses. In particular, all must respect the traffic law.
The Prime Minister made the remarks while receiving a courtesy call from Mr. Kabasima Ikuo, Governor of Kumamoto Prefecture and representatives of eight companies doing business in Cambodia and preparing to do more business in Cambodia. Discuss some work on Saturday evening, April 23, 2022.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, said that during this meeting, Samdech Techo welcomed all companies that have been doing business in Cambodia and are planning to invest in Cambodia in the future. . In this meeting, Samdech Techo allowed each company to mention its investment activities in Cambodia as well as future investment projects.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the improvement of the investment climate in Cambodia, especially the new investment law, which is much better for investors.
The Prime Minister also said that investment in Cambodia is an important contribution to further strengthening economic ties between the two countries.
Under good relations and cooperation, Japan is a country that has invested a lot in Cambodia. The report shows that Japanese investment in Cambodia from 1994 to 2020 amounted to 144 projects with a total capital of nearly 3 billion US dollars.
Trade between the two countries has also improved significantly. Cambodia is Japan's eighth largest trading partner in ASEAN. In 2021, the trade volume between Cambodia and Japan will reach about 1.7 billion US dollars.
Cambodia's exports to Japan include clothing, footwear, furniture, cosmetics, paper, stationery, leather, animals, metals, and more. In particular, the goods that Cambodia imports from Japan include: machinery, cars, meat, electrical appliances, furniture, paper, cotton, fabrics, all kinds of plastic products, sports equipment, all kinds of spare parts and so on.
