Here is the announcement: Do not let the happy days be sad because of your driving! One killed, seven injured in road accident nationwide
(Phnom Penh): According to the report of the General Commission of the National Police, on April 23, 2022, there were five traffic accidents across the country, resulting in one death and seven minor injuries.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on Saturday, April 22, 2022, inspected the quality of National Road No. 2 and No. 22, dragging the machinery to check the foundation and road concentration. During the inspection, he gave technical work to inspect the foundations and road concentrations in many places, and the results came out very disappointing: the foundations and road concentrations were not technically correct.
Dissatisfied with the technically incorrect construction and lack of quality, the senior minister also blamed the construction company and the technical inspection company.
Speaking to reporters on the occasion, the Senior Minister emphasized, "We have laid the foundation for a lot of testing. "Some places are stuck, but most fall below the standards of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport."
The senior minister claimed that he could not accept the construction.
The project to rehabilitate National Road No. 2 and National Road No. 22 started construction on February 11, 2020 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The road project with a total length of 72.17 km is scheduled to be completed in April 2022. But the construction company is slower than planned and has asked for an extension until August this year.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol does not expect the road to be completed in August. According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the construction was delayed because the construction company did not have enough machinery and manpower, not due to the Kovid-19 problem as claimed by the company.
Regarding road quality, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol instructed construction companies, technical inspection companies and technicians of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to work together to improve the road foundation. The senior minister emphasized that he could not accept the poor quality roads and was criticized by the people of that state.
Hansin of South Korea is also a company that the South Korean government is lending to build National Road 21 from the Takhmao roundabout to the Chrey Thom border. At that time, the company also built poor quality roads.
Mr. Sun Chanthol confirmed that he had referred the company's problems to the South Korean Embassy in Cambodia. Mr. Sun Chanthol warned that there would be talks that the company could be blacklisted for road construction in Cambodia.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Hansin does not have enough machinery for the construction, so the machinery is too old.
Public opinion: The South Korean government should review the work of this company to avoid damaging the honor of the government and the people of Korea from the company's laziness.
With the delay in the construction of this road, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol asked for understanding and tolerance from the people living on both sides of the road.
Please note that the project to improve National Roads 2 and 22 has a total length of 72.17 km. The section of National Road No. 2 from Takhmao roundabout to O Chambok is 62.56 km long and National Road No. 22 from O Chambok to Ang Ta Som is 9.61 km long in Takeo province.
