(Koh Kong): Darasakor International Airport, located in Botum Sakor District, Koh Kong Province, has started a seven-day technical flight by testing key equipment and flight techniques before launching a test run in July 2022. Coming soon. This is according to Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation.
Speaking to Fresh News on April 23, 2022, the senior official of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation confirmed that Darasakor International Airport is currently in the process of testing and measuring the installed equipment to ensure that both equipment. That meets the quality standards in accordance with the requirements of flight safety requirements.
"Before launching, it is necessary to test all equipment such as lighting systems, radio systems, landing navigation systems, communication systems, as well as fire trucks and other parts, as well as human resources that control the equipment," he said. That to ensure safety.
According to Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, the testing of key equipment and document preparation has achieved about 60% so far.
He pointed out that the airport is scheduled to launch a test flight in July this year, after testing equipment that meets technical and safety requirements. However, this project may require additional time (delay) to complete the technical procedures as well as obtain the certification / license for the commencement of the entire airport operation.
