He added that for Preah Vihear province, the malaria infection rate has decreased by 53.6% compared to 2021. This means that the malaria infection rate in Preah Vihear province, despite the epidemic of Kovid 19, can be controlled to see a significant decline.
He added that if we look at the goals and national strategic plan, we have reached the goal and he hopes to reach the goal of eradicating all malaria by 2025.
