BEIJING, April 21 (Xinhua) - Chinese President Xi Jinping wrote a letter to a former professor at the Beijing University of Science and Technology on April 21, expressing strong hopes for more high-quality human resource training and development. And innovations in the steel industry, low carbon and green development.
He wrote in the letter that the revival of the Chinese nation urgently requires the training of highly moral and highly capable human resources, and hoped that the professors would be able to continue to train high-quality human resources who contribute to building the nation to contribute more. Much in training human resources to build a strong country in science and technology and a strong country in production.
Recently, 15 former professors of Beijing University of Science and Technology wrote a letter to Chinese President Xi Jinping to report on the development achievements of Beijing University of Science and Technology during the 70th anniversary of the establishment of the University of Science and Technology. The past year has shown a strong commitment to training more and more high-quality human resources for the development of the high-quality steel industry.
