Researchers estimate that the new dolphin is just five days old and will be the second baby dolphin for 2022. Mekong dolphins are listed on the IUCN Red List as the most endangered species.
The results of the 2020 Mekong Dolphin Census by the Fisheries Administration and WWF show that only 89 dolphins are living in Cambodia's Mekong River.
To ensure that this baby dolphin continues to survive and evolve into a full-fledged adult dolphin, WWF calls on fishermen to take immediate action to prevent and stop all illegal activities, especially gear fishing. Mosquitoes and snails, in particular, need to work more closely to develop more effective conservation measures to protect dolphins from extinction.
