Duke Kouch Mengly Distributes Gifts to 400 Poor Families in Kampong Leng District, Kampong Chhnang Province
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Dr. Kouch Mengly and his family, including the management of Mengly J. Kouch Education Company, on the morning of April 23, 2022, went to distribute charitable gifts in the form of food to needy people in Kong Kep village, Chronok district. Kampong Leng, Kampong Chhnang province, about 400 families.
On that occasion, Duke Dr. Kouch Mengly expressed his great joy for contributing to the people and the development of the village where his ancestors went through hardships and hardships decades ago.
The Duke continued that after the situation of Kovid 19 in Cambodia seemed to improve, he and his family were able to return to the village to share gifts with the poor, while in previous years he always came. It has been since 2001.
For more than 20 years, the tycoon, known to many Cambodians for his sharp health and education advice, has stressed that his Meng Ly J. Kouch Foundation has donated more than $ 300,000 to the Frog Village. By including the provision of food to the people, especially the contribution of the construction of pagodas, schools and water wells to facilitate the lives of the people, as well as promote the education of children in the village.
Meanwhile, Thmor Kong Kep village chief, Mr. Chhem Sokhorn, expressed his happiness to see the Duke, Dr. Kouch Mengly and his family come down to distribute charitable gifts to the needy people in the village.
He added that the tycoon, Dr. Kouch Mengly, has been coming down to give charity donations and help build pagodas, schools and water wells to the frog village for many years.
