Director General of Accounting and Auditing: Proper accounting as a suffix leads to increased fiscal revenue
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Bou Tharin, Director General of Accounting and Auditing Regulator, emphasized that proper accounting records and preparation of financial statements in accordance with applicable standards will enhance the transparency and reliability of the Company's financial statements. And this is a suffix that leads to an increase in fiscal revenue.
This emphasis was made on the occasion of Mr. Bou Tharin's participation in the Outreach Workshop on "Accounting and Auditing Obligations and Related Regulations" for Enterprises organized by the Accounting and Auditing Regulators of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority in Phnom Penh Hotel on the morning of April 22, 2022.
The workshop was attended by the management and officials of the Accounting and Auditing Regulators, with a total of 280 participants from the owners or representatives of the enterprise. This workshop is designed to disseminate and raise awareness of laws and regulations related to accounting and auditing, especially accounting and auditing obligations to all business owners and stakeholders in Cambodia.
He added that currently the new laws and regulations that have been implemented include:
1: Law on Accounting and Auditing 2: Sub-Decree on Transitional Penalties for Violations of the Law on Accounting and Auditing 3: Prakas on the obligation to submit an independent audit report 4: Circulars for guidance and notification of submission of financial statements Independent audit and non-audit of enterprises and non-profit entities to online accounting and auditing regulators.
In addition, the Director General mentioned the following messages:
* Transparency in the management of financial resources, easy access to credit from banks or financial institutions, finding foreign investment partners, participation in the capital markets and the exemption from penalties from the competent institutions eventually.
* Maintaining accurate accounting records and preparing financial statements in accordance with applicable standards will enhance the transparency and reliability of the enterprise's financial statements and facilitate the enterprise in fulfilling its tax obligations. One leads to an increase in fiscal revenue.
The Speakers of the Accounting and Auditing Regulators presented an update on the accounting and auditing obligations and related regulations, which are divided into six main sections: 1: Accounting, 2: Preparation of financial statements, 3: Submission of annual financial statements for independent audit, 4: Interim penalties, 5: Non-recurrence or late payment of fines, and 6: Complaints.
Afterwards, Mr. KC Baneth, Advisor to the Ministry of Economy and Finance, presented a presentation on the financial statements model in accordance with the accounting standards for small and medium enterprises to the workshop. On that occasion, the workshop raised many questions to ask the speakers related to laws and regulations, accounting and auditing.
