Samdech Techo Hun Sen Shares Four Concepts to the Summit on Water Issues for Sustainable Water Resources Management (Video inside) (Japan): In the 4th Summit on Water Issues in the Asia-Pacific Region Held in Khemamut, Japan on the morning of Saturday, April 23, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that water is an important resource for development and quality of life.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen shared four ideas to solve the challenges leading to the destruction of water resources and to manage sustainably for now and in the future. The four concepts include:
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that the efficient and effective use of water resources is essential for sustainable socio-economic development. Indeed, in the UN 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development, water resources are set out in Goal 6 on "Sustainable Water Efficiency and Sanitation for All People."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, also highlighted that Cambodia considers water as "white gold" as a driving force for sustainable and sustainable socio-economic development and development. In addition, the Royal Government of Cambodia has always recognized the strategic importance and given high priority to the water resources sector in order to promote better water resources management and ensure water security throughout the country.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced Cambodia's position at the meeting that Cambodia will continue to cooperate with all stakeholders under regional and global mechanisms to strengthen and enhance governance and management of water resources and transboundary river basins. More effective in achieving the goal of "water for sustainable development".
It should be noted that the 4th Asia-Pacific Water Summit was held under the theme "Water for Sustainable Development: Excellence and Successors".
The meeting also aims to promote further collaboration and partnership to use quality infrastructure to support quality growth.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen delivered a keynote address at the summit, focusing on the importance of water and water-related issues, as well as the need to work together to manage this vital resource. By sustainability.
