The following is a press release obtained by Fresh News: Dispute resolution between protesters and NagaWorld has not been agreed yet, May 4 will resume.
(Phnom Penh): The settlement of the dispute between the protesters and NagaWorld has not yet reached an agreement reached by the representatives of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on April 22, 2022, with all parties to continue to meet. On May 4, 2022, more.
According to an earlier statement from the Ministry of Labor obtained by Fresh News, on April 22, 2022, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training continued to mediate joint labor disputes at NagaWorld in accordance with its role in The law is in force as well as in accordance with the wishes of the representatives of the workers who want to negotiate with the company.
According to the statement, during the meeting, both sides raised the following comments:
Opinions of unions and workers' representatives:
1: The application option is the same, asking for 200 workers who have been laid off to join the work and exchange with about 300 workers who are currently working and voluntarily resign. The company can hire all 200 workers, giving workers 50% off shifts in the first month, 70% in the second month and increasing until there are full shifts.
2: Through the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, request to drop the charges against all NagaWorld workers' representatives, to reopen the union office and to request the use of telephones, computers and other equipment for communication. In addition, ask the company to provide options for the workers to be fair.
Comments of NagaWorld Representatives:
After vigorous discussions, the two sides agreed as follows: 1. The two sides have not yet reached an agreement. 2. Set a date for the next meeting on Wednesday, May 4, 2022. 14:30 to give both parties a chance to reconsider the possibility of mutual concessions that could lead to an end to the dispute.
