The launch of the Air Passenger Risk Assessment System will boost the growth of international tourists and air passengers, in the first three months of this year, air passengers increased by 150%
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, said that the introduction of the Air Passenger Risk Assessment System (GTAS) will help boost the number of international tourists to help. Restoring tourism during and after the outbreak of Kovid 19.
He said this during the ceremony to officially implement on behalf of the Royal Government the use of air passenger risk assessment system on the afternoon of April 22, 2022.
The GTAS system introduced by the Royal Government today will not require a fee from tourists, which is to reduce the cost of Cambodia's tourism package and contribute to the roadmap on rehabilitation and upgrading plans. Cambodia's tourism sector during and after the 199 epidemic.
At the same time, this system helps to increase the efficiency of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, to prevent cross-border crime at international airports, and to promote legal trade facilitation.
Dr. Mao Havnall, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, said that the current implementation of the GTAS system is an appropriate time for the response to a return to normalcy in the air transport sector. .
He said that after the lifting of travel restrictions on air transport in the first three months of 2022, reached about 37% compared to 2019 before the outbreak of Kovid. Compared to the same period in 2021, in the first three months, passenger transport increased by 150%.
"We hope that the normalization of air transport from 2023 to 2025 or early 2026, as predicted by international aviation institutions," he added.
Based on past experience and progress, Cambodia may be able to expand the scope to fully implement the GTAS system project on all airlines operating inbound and outbound activities in the Kingdom in the second half of 2022.
