Japan and Russia have not signed a peace treaty since the end of World War II, as territorial disputes coupled with the war in Ukraine have been hampering peace talks. In its 2003 annual policy report, the Japanese Foreign Ministry called the disputed archipelago with Russia "Northern Territory" and Moscow called it the Kurils.
In a statement on Friday, the Japanese Foreign Ministry described the disputed archipelago as "illegally controlled" by Russia for the first time in nearly two decades. "The most worrying issue between Japan and Russia is the northern territories, which are now illegally under Russian control," the statement said.
The Japanese Foreign Ministry also acknowledged that the war in Ukraine could hamper peace talks with Russia after Moscow announced its withdrawal from the talks in March. To Japan, which joins the West in condemning and imposing sanctions on Russia.
NEC: Draw to determine the order of political parties on ballots completed in 1,652 communes / sangkats
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Duch Son, Member of the National Election Committee (NEC), confirmed that the draw to determine the order of political parties on the ballot has been completed in 1,652 communes to compete. For the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on the morning of April 22, 2022, the election to determine the order of political parties on the ballot, Mr. Duch Son, Commune / Sangkat Election Commission. The lottery ceremony was organized according to the procedures set out in the NEC regulations and procedures.
Mr. Duch Son stated that in order to announce the posting of the official list of candidates at the Commune / Sangkat Election Commission (CEC), a lottery was held to determine the order of political parties on commune ballots and the distribution of ballots. Voter information in villages in communes.
He said that the official results of the registration of candidates of political parties for the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022, there are 17 political parties participating in the election and a total of 86,092 candidates in 17 parties. That number was 27,813 women.
Mr. Duch Son stated that the distribution of voter information cards must be done in the villages in the commune from April 17 to May 16, 2022, and if the remaining cards are distributed to the NEC. To share.
At the same time, he added that the distribution of voter information leaflets was to help voters know the names, data, numbering, polling time and location of polling stations, as well as to help the polling station commission to find voter names quickly. .
The Voter Information Card Distribution Team consists of one or more CEC members, one or more Commune / Sangkat Councilors, one or more members representing an association or NGO, one or more members (if any) and the village chief. Or relevant village assistants as members.
