Readers' Perspectives: Cambodia and the Sino-US Geopolitical Competition
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia is a country that is in competition between the two superpowers, China and the United States, and despite many controversial issues that affect Cambodia's interests in terms of economy, politics and security and Mixed with concern, Cambodia, now chairing ASEAN for the third time, remains influential in its role as a sovereign country.
So far, what benefits has Cambodia gained and what challenges has it faced from the power struggle between the two powers?
From the beginning, relations between small countries and superpowers, especially now, the two superpowers, China and the United States, have been inseparable in terms of trade, investment, politics and security. Developing countries that need to have relations with those countries are essential to boosting their economic growth.
Relations between Cambodia and China have been steadily advancing. China has become the country that has invested more than any other country in Cambodia. Cambodia-China bilateral trade volume reached more than 11 billion US dollars in the first 12 months of 2021, up 37.28% compared to the same period in 2020, of which more than 9,000 Million dollars is the value of goods that Cambodia imports from China.
Cambodia-China trade volume for 2022 could be further enhanced by the implementation of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement (CCFTA) and the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) and acceleration The pace of negotiations, procedures between the two sides on the benefits of Cambodia's agricultural exports to the Chinese market.
We observe that trade cooperation between Cambodia and China, despite the imbalance of exports, but with the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement (CCFTA) and the Economic Partnership Agreement Regional Corner (RCEP) Cambodia will definitely be able to increase its export volume by increasing domestic production.
* Investment cooperation
Chinese investment in Cambodia increased significantly in 2021, despite the negative impact of the 19 Kovid outbreak, which really reflects the confidence of Chinese investors in the Cambodian business environment.
* Political and security cooperation
Relations between China and Cambodia have continued steadily, despite the fall of the dark Democratic Kampuchea regime. The improved relations between Beijing and Phnom Penh are evident in the frequent exchanges of visits between the two countries' leaders and senior officials, as well as China's assistance to Cambodia.
On December 9, 2021, Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Wang Wenbin reacted immediately after the United States decided to impose additional sanctions on Cambodia by restricting the sale of arms and military equipment to Cambodia. December 2021 and called the US decision a plot to break Sino-Cambodian relations and eventually the United States will fail.
The strategy focuses on activities such as strengthening bilateral security alliances, establishing a broad-based military presence, participating in regional multilateral mechanisms, expanding trade and investment, and promoting democracy and human rights. This is not only to achieve US strategic interests and values, but also to counter Chinese influence in Southeast Asia.
During a meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, during Derek Chollet's visit to Cambodia on December 10, 2021, Derek Chollet reaffirmed that ASEAN is at the heart of US foreign policy in the Indo-Pacific region and looks forward to working closely with Cambodia as chair of ASEAN in 2022.
We observe that Cambodia's political and security cooperation with China and the United States is now in the most complex context, one being liberal and the other communist. The geopolitical rivalry of the two powers can be both profitable and dangerous for Cambodia.
Overall, in the context of the power struggle between the two superpowers, China and the United States, although Cambodia has received some pressure from the United States and some support from China, both countries Contributed significantly to the promotion of national economic growth and development to Cambodia just by using different means and strategies.
