(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhuon Makara, Deputy Secretary General of the National Committee for Clean City Assessment (NCPC) and Director of the Department of Management, Transport Agency and Tourism Guide of the Ministry of Tourism, confirmed that in 2022, Cambodia expects Will receive between 600 and 700,000 international tourists, while in the next five years, Cambodia is expected to receive between 7 million foreign tourists.
This statement was made during a roundtable discussion on "Cambodian tourism in the context of Kovid 19" organized by the Royal Academy of Cambodia this morning, April 22, 2022.
"For international tourists in 2022, we expect to receive only between 600,000 and 700,000 people. Previously, we expected 800,000 people, but now fall due to the war crisis (Ukraine)," said Chhuon Makara. "And Russia) and other crises, especially the European and US markets have experienced war crises in Ukraine and Russia."
For domestic tourism, it could be fast, meaning it could be in V-shape. For 2022, Cambodia could receive about 8 million domestic tourists just during the traditional New Year. Khmer for 3 days, including Sunday, Cambodia has 5.17 million tourists. Therefore, it is expected that in 2023, Cambodia will receive about 11 million tourists. This is according to Mr. Chhuon Makara.
The official of the Ministry of Tourism pointed out that under the current situation, Cambodia took only three years to recover the number of tourists as before, the outbreak of Kovid 19. Statistics alone in 2022 until February, there are 95,145 tourists, so Cambodia will strive to achieve the target of 600 to 700,000 foreign tourists as planned.
