(Phnom Penh): More than 3,000 troops have been deployed and mobilized to vaccinate workers against 19 doses of measles, urging workers at factories in Phnom Penh to increase workers' health protection from the 19 19 measles outbreak.
On Friday morning, April 22, 2022, General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chairman of the Vaccination Committee of the Ministry of National Defense, inspected the vaccination process in some factories. Phnom Penh.
Through the inspection, it was found that the vaccination team from various units under the Ministry of National Defense has been working with great care to provide the vaccine to the people. Separately, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, as well as the management of each factory also cooperated to provide opportunities for workers to receive this booster dose.
General Ith Sarath emphasized that on April 12, Samdech instructed the Commission on Vaccination to increase the dose given to people across the country, especially in factories after the injection. Slow speed.
General Ith Sarath said that after receiving the recommendations and orders, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, organized a team of 3,484 people to be vaccinated, including 106 teams of doctors. Deploy vaccination operations in factories in Phnom Penh.
According to General Ith Sarath, this vaccination was given by Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh and instructed all vaccination team to move to the factory and to cooperate with the factory so as not to affect the work of Workers.
General Ith Sarath confirmed that the vaccination was going well with the cooperation of the Commission on Vaccination, the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and factory management.
General Ith Sarath also confirmed that after the injection is given to the workers, the vaccination team of the Ministry of National Defense will continue to mobilize people in the backyard or in the town to ensure that they Increased dose to protect health from Kovid 19.
The Chairman of the Vaccination Commission of the Ministry of National Defense, General, emphasized that the mobilization of the army to vaccinate the people is a demonstration of the high consideration and attention of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen. For example, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh and all national leaders on the well-being of the people and prevent the recurrence of Kovid 19 disease, which leads to difficulties in society as a whole.
During the inspection of the booster dose at the factory, it was found that all the workers started the fourth booster dose, but some of them had just received the first and second doses and some had given the third dose. Workers who have just injected the first or second dose claim that in the past she was pregnant and had just given birth.
It should be noted that Cambodia has been well controlling the outbreak of Kovid 19 after vaccinating the people in 2021. Currently, the Royal Government is continuing to promote the injection, especially the third and fourth doses.
According to the report, Cambodia achieved more than 8 million doses for the third dose and more than 1 million for the fourth dose.
