The 136th Anniversary of International Labor Day, May 1, 2022, is celebrated under the theme "Peace, Health and Occupational Security", which Cambodia has been celebrating since 1979.
In this message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the context that our whole nation is participating in preventing and combating the spread of Kovid-19 disease, the Royal Government would like to make the following recommendations:
2. The Ministry of Information must introduce the public and private media, social media to disseminate the circular and message of Samdech Techo Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia on the occasion of the 136th anniversary of International Labor Day, May 1, 2022.
3: All relevant ministries, institutions, capital and provincial administrations and factories must select suitable locations such as main streets and factory locations, enterprises, workplaces and farms to make banners and slogans according to the following content:
- Congratulations! Kingdom of Cambodia
- Celebrating the 136th Anniversary of May Labor Day
- Peace, health and occupational security
- Volunteer to give Kovid-19 vaccine in both basic and booster doses for health and work.
- Respect the labor law and the union law to ensure the common rights and interests of workers and employers
- Develop a social security system for social welfare - Develop professional skills for productivity and competitiveness
- Occupational security is the driving force of environmentally and sustainably developing
Occupational security is the foundation of a just society, productivity and environment.
4: The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training shall prepare documents and monitor the organization of this event to report to the Royal Government.
The Royal Government calls on all civil servants at all levels, employers, workers, Cambodian and foreign to join the celebration of the International Labor Day on May 1 in a happy atmosphere, solidarity and fraternity to be worthy of our national holiday and implement. Adhere to the "3 protection and 3 do not" measures.
