17 Cambodian workers arrested by Thai authorities after cheating brokers
(Banteay Meanchey): Only 3 days after the end of the Khmer New Year, 17 Cambodian workers were arrested by the Thai authorities in Yang Nam Yen district, Sa Kaeo province, while these 17 workers cheated the brokers out of money. 500 baht. This story happened at 9 pm on April 20, 2022.
At around 9 pm, the Sa Kaeo Provincial Police Force inspected a black Toyota car with license plate BOK-8711 Sa Kaeo in the area of Houay Krai Tai Village, Top Prich-Vang Nam Yen Road, Khlong Hat District, Sa Kaeo Province. The body of a 53-year-old man named Lam Duan Anusi, a Thai broker, was stopped and inspected.
Sa Kaeo provincial police further confirmed that after inspecting the car, they found 14 more Cambodian workers, including 5 males and 9 females and 3 boys, a total of 17 boys.
After being questioned by Thai authorities, the 17 workers confessed that they all wanted to work in Thailand, so they relied on a broker to pay them 500 baht each. The broker handed it over to Lam Duan Anusi in a car in Vang Nam Yen district. The 17 Cambodian workers had to pay an additional 5,000 baht per broker to deliver to the workplace in the Thai market.
The 17 Cambodian workers and a Thai broker, after questioning, the Thai authorities sent all Cambodian workers to professional forces to deal with the law. Achievements in Kampong Cham and Stung Trang districts are scheduled to be officially inaugurated in early May under the presidency of Dr. Hun Manet
