KUALA LUMPUR: Hundreds of Rohingya refugees from Myanmar fled a detention center in Malaysia on Wednesday after a riot erupted, leaving six dead on the highway as they fled. Escape. This is according to the release by AFP on Wednesday, April 20, 2022.
Many Rohingya have arrived in Malaysia by boat after enduring months of sea travel. Those arrested are often sent to detention centers, which rights groups say are cramped and dirty.
Most were recaptured quickly, but 176 were still missing, a large number as of Wednesday afternoon, according to police.
After the riots broke out, the refugees broke through the gates and barricades at the center by 23 guards who were on guard but could not control the situation.
Six detainees, including two men, two women, a girl and a boy, died as they tried to cross a highway after escaping, police said.
The cause of the riot and the explosion is under investigation, police said.
Malaysia, which is predominantly Muslim, is a major target for Rohingya fleeing persecution in their home countries or refugee camps in Bangladesh.
