Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces he will not run in the election and calls for a better environment for the election (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) Vote for the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election and call on the relevant authorities to create a good environment for the election campaign and the election by avoiding any violence.
The 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election will be held on June 5, and the election campaign for political parties will be held on May 21 for 14 days. The election campaign is an important time for registered political parties to campaign for popular support.
On the occasion of presiding over the inauguration of the achievements of the flood protection and drainage system improvement project in Phnom Penh, Phase 4, on Wednesday morning, April 20, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that on the opening day of the campaign During the election campaign, Samdech will travel to Davos, Switzerland to attend the World Economic Forum.
In addition to announcing that he will not be campaigning for the election, Samdech Techo, the head of the largest political party and who is leading the Royal Government, also called on all relevant authorities to work hard to create a conducive environment for the election campaign. By providing equal opportunities for all political parties in accordance with the law and striving to avoid violence.
"A neutral political environment is absolutely necessary at the stage of campaigning, in which authorities at all levels must qualify all political parties for equal rights," he said.
"The ruling party and the non-ruling party have the same rights," he said. This is called the neutrality of the civil administration in the election phase. "How to have a calm election environment, a challenge for continued governance at the grassroots level."
Samdech Techo, President of the Cambodian People's Party, also called on the relevant authorities to create a good environment for the people to participate in the election of Commune / Sangkat Councils of the fifth mandate freely and fairly in accordance with the election law. Samdech Techo appealed, "Call on all places to maintain efforts for the people to participate in the election and choose freely, love any candidate to vote for that candidate."
Despite not campaigning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects voters to have a fair judgment on the values and merits of the political party he or she has voted for.
It should be noted that the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election, which will be held on June 5, 2022, has 17 political parties competing. According to the National Election Committee (NEC), a total of 11,622 commune councilors will be elected in 1,652 communes across the country.
