He added that since the 19 cases of Kovi, it is very difficult to earn money because there are not as many foreign tourists as before. In the past, if you sold a CD, you could earn 20,000 to 30,000 riel per person, just to support your family. He said that because Kovid makes the life of this disabled band difficult, there is a lack of morning and evening.
Mr. Pokny continued that he knew how to play music since he was young because he had previously played in village music and had been visiting Ta Prohm for 19 years. His band is crippled by landmines.
With this, the band for the disabled at Ta Prohm temple hopes that soon more tourists will come to visit as before so that the band can earn a decent income to support the family. For every day, some days I get money for my family, but some days I don't even get a hundred riel.
