OPEC + oil production falls in March as sanctions hurt Russian output
Russia produced 10.08 million barrels a day in March, about 300,000 barrels lower than its target, the report said.
Compliance with OPEC + cut oil production rose to 157% in March from 132% in February, the highest level since OPEC introduced austerity measures. Unprecedented production was about 10 million barrels per day in May 2020 to counteract the impact of the epidemic on demand.
