BANGKOK: The Bank of Thailand said on Monday it had eased further foreign exchange (Forex) regulations to allow easier capital movements and risk management as the baht depreciated to a new low. Two weeks against the dollar. According to the Bangkok Post.
The latest changes to the rules include measures to reduce restrictions on remittances, facilitate hedging and remove the requirements for supporting documents, the Bangkok Post reported, citing a central bank statement. .
These measures are similar to last year's, when Forex measures were relaxed to encourage capital outflows and withstand strong exchange rate fluctuations.
Restrictions on annual lending to non-affiliated companies, which are currently limited to $ 50 million, will be lifted and restrictions on overseas property purchases will be lifted, the statement said. Must also be removed.
The measure, which will take effect after being published in a government circular, also allows for remittances for other purposes and removes conditions requiring prior approval from the Central Bank of Thailand.
Thai companies will be allowed to buy foreign currency for domestic transfers as needed. Previously, transfers were only allowed through foreign currency deposit accounts.
Companies doing business in Thailand will be allowed to manage their foreign exchange risk to a greater extent, such as hedging against foreign exchange risks arising from local payments for commodities. Is linked to the global market.
The Bank of Thailand has said it will require fewer supporting documents in foreign currency transactions to reduce costs and paperwork.
"This will enable exporters, importers and companies in the supply chain to more effectively manage the risk of their foreign exchange fluctuations," the central bank added. Driving! Two killed, nine injured in nationwide road accident on April 19
