At least nine people have been killed and dozens more injured in a fire that engulfed more than 70 homes in southern Pakistan.
ISLAMABAD: At least nine people, including children, were killed and several others injured when a fire engulfed more than 70 homes in Pakistan's southern Dadu district. This is according to the release by Xinhua on Tuesday, April 19, 2022.
The blaze broke out in three villages of Dadu district after spreading from villagers' stoves due to strong winds in the area on Monday night, the report said.
The source added that the fire that broke out from a family's wood-burning stove spread to three different places as more than 70 houses were engulfed.
Among the dead were at least five children who were sleeping indoors during the blaze.
