New normalization trajectory and win-win cooperation have kept China's economy steady and contributed to global economic recovery
BEIJING: In the context of Kovid-19, countries have been trying to adapt to a new normal life, trying to recover everything after the effects of the global pandemic crisis. Although Kovid-19 has not yet been completely overcome.
Remarkably, the digital economy flourished after the global health crisis, which contributed significantly to the normalization of international trade during the Kovid period. Countries have introduced policies to boost the digital economy in order to increase competitiveness in international markets and access new development opportunities.
Although it is not possible to trade "face to face", it is also not possible to block the steps of economic and trade cooperation between countries, whether bilateral or multilateral economic cooperation. Consult and sign online forms, a new form of collaboration to meet the needs of the new era and in the context affected by Kovid.
After all, China, the world's second-largest economy and the first country in the world to recover economically in the context of Kovid-19, has become the "core" of the world. Expect and see how this "global economic stabilization anchor" will play a role in rescuing a struggling global economy.
Since entering a new normal course after the outbreak of Kovid-19, China has been striving to revive its economy through the introduction of new policies, while others have been cooperating win-win with partners. Its cooperation that adheres to shared and environmental development.
From the outside, China has enjoyed win-win economic and trade cooperation with partners around the world. In the first quarter of this year, the total trade volume between China and ASEAN reached 1.35 trillion yuan, China and the European Union reached 1.31 trillion yuan, and China and the United States reached 1.18 trillion yuan. ASEAN continues to be China's number one trading partner.
The spread of Kovid-19 is not over, and China's distribution of vaccines to countries in need has not stopped. The world situation is getting more complicated and uncertain, China has put in a series of positive forces to help stabilize the overall situation. Despite the changing nature of the world, China has always adhered to the one-community initiative of one humanity.
