Please see the picture below: Preah Thong Neang Neak or the origin of Khmer territory
(Phnom Penh): In the history of Khmer, according to the legend, Preah Thong and Neang Neak were the parents, the ancestors, the creators of the first Khmer nation. Most of us Cambodians do not know this history. Documents about the history of Preah Thong Neang Naki ”are found in almost all Khmer genealogies prepared by various authors.
(Khmer history, legend)
* Buddha Prophecy
When the sun goes down and the moon begins to rise in turn, the Buddha and Ananda go to rest under the lotus tree. The devas who take care of the lotus tree have prepared a place to receive him and all the devas who will come to worship the Buddha.
King Phu Chong Neak, who came out to the pavilion at Toul Deum Thlok, saw the Buddha as a human being and brought his entourage to worship the goddess Jin Srey and asked him to give a sermon to heal all the dragons. At the same time, Indrakosi, gods, sons, devas, fairies and demigods from all over came together to worship the Lord Buddha.
History of Preah Thong
At that time, in the kingdom of Indopot, there was a king named Atichvong who had five sons. The fourth son, Preah Thong, was in charge of the southern province. As for the fifth son, who was the youngest, he was left to live with him in the royal palace.
Know this when the youngest brother asked for permission from his father to visit you. When he met you, he knelt down and worshiped, which surprised and amazed Preah Thong. After listening to your explanation and understanding all the ways, Preah Thong realized his mistake and told you to ask your father for forgiveness on his behalf.
One day, Preah Thong and the Cham king named Aschai Jayaraj had a quarrel and a war broke out. Preah Thong won the victory to defeat the Cham king who fled and hid in Champasak, now Laos. Now Preah Thong has ruled the mainland alone. He named the kingdom "Nokor Kok Thlo".
Many people, scholars and scholars, came to live in crowded places in the mainland. He ordered scholars to translate the Sanskrit script into the Khmer script for use. The preparation of Phum Nokor district in agriculture and economy is also actively considered. In terms of religion, they also see the presence of many Buddhist temples in the kingdom of Kok Thlok.
During the seven days between the two lovers, Preah Thong had to prepare all kinds of gifts and greetings and wait at the same place. As for Thearavattey, when she arrived at the Dragon Temple, she told all the stories along the way to her father and mother. King Phu Chong Neak did not understand the objection. He agreed to the request of his son.
In his reign, according to Khmer chronicles and other documents, except for the chronicles of Samdech Veang Chuon, the Cham king, who had previously defeated Preah Thong, raised a large army to attack the mainland. The Cham king Asjai Reach, with five sons as his assistant commander, raised an army from Champasak.
The Khmer king, Preah Komreach, appointed the son of the Cham king, Suryavarmin, to rule Traing district, located on Phnom Bayongko. To rule Tbong Khmum district and Preah Santravarmin to control Stong district.
Preah Thong and Neang Neak had many sons and daughters, whom he divided the duties of appointing to the ranks and assigning their respective missions to control the kingdoms of other countries.
Therefore, in the Khmer view, Preah Thong Neang Neak has become a symbol of creating a family, descendants, descendants.
If we talk in the field of literature, we observe that there are many legends that simultaneously tell the story of the crocodile or the battle of Preah Thong or our Khmer grandfather.
3: Some other documents, except for the genealogy of Samdech Veang Chuon, indicate that Preah Thong or Samdech Komareach and Preah Bat Tevong Aschar are the characters of the same Khmer king.
Thus, we find that the origins of the Khmer are much more ambiguous if we refer to the inscriptions at Mason and to the testimonies of Chinese travelers. But what we see left as a tradition, a literary tradition and a statue of Kong Vong to this day is Preah Thong Neang Neak. As we have already mentioned above, Preah Thong Neang Neak is a symbol of the Khmer family and nation.
