(Preah Sihanouk): On the morning of Saturday, April 15, 2022, which is the 16th day of the Khmer New Year, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, preside over the inauguration ceremony of the statue of Preah Thong-Neang Neak.
Ly Raksmey, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, said that the statue of Preah Thong-Neang Neak was placed at the roundabout at the intersection of Chumteav Mao Blvd. and Ream Beach Boulevard in Sihanoukville to show their identity. Khmer in Sihanoukville, a modern city and there is little to distinguish the Khmer identity.
It is for this reason that the Coastal Management and Development Committee, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, has decided to build a statue of Preah Thong-Neak, a statue of Vishnu and Princess Uma Pheakvati, also known as Uma Mahasvara and Siha Reach.
The statue of Preah Thong Neang Neak, made of copper, weighs a total of 60 tons, 21 meters high from the king to the top of the crown, placed on a throne 6.34 meters high, will stand tall in the center of the circle of Preah Thong Neang Neak. 99 meters in diameter and facing towards the Ream Sea. The statue of Preah Thong-Neang Neak is a symbol of the birth of Khmer territory, culture, civilization, traditions and customs.
The talented young architect also confirmed that the statue of Preah Thong-Neang Neak was built in a medieval style, which is characterized by a high crown and body ornaments. Different from the Angkorian or pre-Angkorian style.
He also stated that there are many documents that are used as reference documents to build this statue, such as paintings in the Royal Palace and costumes in Khmer classical dance.
However, Mr. Ly Raksmey admitted that no one knew the faces of Preah Thong and Neang Neak and did not know how his body was decorated at that time, but the team tried to clean up. This statue does not fit the context of Khmer life.
As one of the next generation of Cambodian architects, Mr. Ly Raksmey expressed his pleasure and pride in contributing to the architectural work through the construction of infrastructure and statues in Sihanoukville as a legacy for the next generation of Cambodians. Next.
Please be informed that the statue of Preah Thong-Neang Neak will be married on Saturday, April 16 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
According to historical documents, the lands along the lower Mekong River and in the delta of this river were believed by a group of Cambodians to believe in dragons, or that their ancestors were descended from dragons. Lived for a long time.
Mr. Kaing Thai said that in the morning, he went to the temple to worship, suddenly saw the magic bow like a dream. With such a dream, he traveled by sea to the mountain kingdom, following the angel's instructions in the dream.
Arriving at the mountain kingdom, King Hun Tien fought with the capital of this state, which Kaing Thai called Liu Yi. Princess Liu Yi, who led the army to attack King Hun Tien's ship first. By the power of the magic bow, he defeated the local lord Liu Yi by shooting her ship from side to side.
Seeing that King Hun Tien was so powerful, Princess Liu Yi agreed to defeat him, and he has been marrying her since then.
Another source describing this event is the Cham inscription in Myeon (658 AD), which states that King Hun Tien, as the Chinese call him, was named Kaundin, while Princess Liu Yi was named Soma, the son of the moon. On the other hand, the royal genealogy of the Kingdom of Cambodia is called Preah Thong and Neang Neak, which has left a lot of traditional heritage to the life of Cambodian society to this day.
As for the name of the kingdom, it was probably from that time that it was called Nokor Phnom because according to Chinese documents, it is clear that the emperor of the mountain kingdom had the title Kulong, which is now the city that means king. On the other hand, according to the Chinese tradition, they often use the same name or word to identify the country, the people, the capital, or the title of the leader.
Therefore, the word Funan, which the Chinese call, may be called by the title of emperor, Funan, and Funan is the Chinese accent of the Khmer word Funan or mountain. The fact that the emperor of the mountain kingdom has the title of Funan is probably from the mountain where the emperor went up to meet Iso.
Chinese documents state that the deity often descended from Mount Matan, often taking it there to unleash his greatness. The emperors received blessings from him, and the people prospered as a result. The capital of the Phnom Kingdom, named Vyathapura, is probably located around the mountain, about 200 kilometers from the sea.
