Khmer Civilization Expert: What does the deity of the year Kal, named Kirini Devi, holding a "gun" mean?
Therefore, for the deity of the New Year, the year of Karl, Kirini Devi, the fifth daughter of Kobil Mahaprabhu, corresponds to this Thursday in the Vedic scriptures of Brahmanism, the deity representing Jupiter as the deity associated with fire.
Thus, the "gun" in the Sanskrit language "gun or gun" is a ray of fire or a piece of fire or lightning, a treasure of angels in the form of fire, called "gun" to be aware of the natural phenomena that occur from Rise in heat, wind, storm, flood, lightning, according to the predictions of the great astrological astrology.
In the 10th century Khmer art, the Vachrayan sect was a treasurer holding a jewel, who had a fierce face and was ready to fight. Today, the oldest deity, originally from Phnom Trop, is housed in France at the Gimmet Museum in Paris.
Mr. Rath Sandab stated that this is the case for the New Year deity named Kirini Devi, the deity representing Jupiter, the deity in relation to fire, representing Thursday, which is the weekly day on earth where she has a celestial paradise.
He sits in a chariot with his right hand holding a whip and his left hand holding a gun, which always comes down to guard the subcontinent at the time of Sankranti on Thursday. : Jewelry, gems, jewelry, He wore emeralds, green gems * Food: Eat beans and sesame.
