Sambo District Police Force 3 Cars Arrested Village Defenders Following Complaint of Fishmongers Involving Injuries
(Kratie): Police in Sambo district, about 3 vehicles, raided 3 village guards in Kampi village, Sambok commune, Chit Borei district, according to the complaint of the fisherman for causing injuries. The police force operation to arrest the village guards took place on Wednesday evening, April 13, 2022.
The operation also sparked protests in the village. Tuy Sovanna, chief of Sambok commune, told Fresh News At around 2 am on Wednesday, April 13, a group of village guards patrolling the Mekong River spotted a group of fishermen and filmed their activities. In the fight, the fishmonger hit the knife of the people, protecting the seam between the seams.
According to the commune chief, the fisherman complained to the village guards about causing injuries to the Sambo district police force.
The commune chief said that the village guards who were arrested by Sambo district police were 28-year-old Khvek Ravi, 35-year-old Kum Thoeun and 37-year-old Kum Thi. Separately, the group of shockers who complained was named Muong Hoeun and Kan Soknin, who live in Sandan commune.
Mr. Tuy Sovanna claimed that the defenders of the village who were sued were people who worked to prevent fishing activities in the Anlong Phsoth area, a protected area. He confirmed that the village guards did not have any allowances, but they worked from the bottom of their hearts and always patrolled to prevent the shock.
Mr. Tuy Sovanna confirmed that the electric shock at Anlong Phsoth occurred permanently and that this defender was the one who volunteered to help prevent the electric shock and often caught the electric shock group.
The commune chief expressed his dissatisfaction with the arrest of the three village guards. He considered that this would lead to discouragement of the village guards, as the perpetrators of daily fishing were forced to escape the law.
