Fire burns 6 houses in Toul Kork, destroys a lot of property, authorities use 62 cars
(Phnom Penh): At least six houses were completely engulfed by fire and many properties were destroyed, but no one was killed or injured.
This incident happened at 9:30 AM on April 13, 2022, at the intersection of Street 247, House 54, Village 10, Group 27, Sangkat Boeung Salang, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh. This is according to the report of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, which was obtained by Fresh News.
According to the report, the fire was started by the owner, Un Kruy, a 78-year-old housewife. Causes of electric shock. Caused a fire on a rock under 4 meters by 16 meters and damaged a large number of materials.
In this case, it spread to five neighboring houses, causing a complete fire.
