The following is a message from the World Health Organization (WHO) Representative in Cambodia:
I would like to wish all Cambodians peace, safety, good health and glory on the occasion of the traditional Khmer New Year!
The New Year is a special occasion after the global epidemic of Kovid-19 more than two years ago. On behalf of the World Health Organization in Cambodia, we are very excited to join in the celebration of the New Year with all Cambodians, and we clearly understand the importance of reuniting with people. Dear, this is an important occasion.
Khmer New Year is an important celebration and I am really excited to be in this wonderful country on the occasion of this special Khmer New Year 2022. Show love and respect to our families by ensuring that we are protecting them from Kovid-19 while enjoying this well-deserved holiday.
The virus continues to spread in the community and could lead to more infections if we are not careful. Do everything we can to celebrate Khmer New Year in a safe way while we can enjoy the people we love the most.
