Please watch the full video below: Senior official of the Ministry of Justice: Campaign to solve the case to help nearly 20,000 individuals out of prison by reducing prison overcrowding (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry Justice said that the campaign to solve the congestion in the capital-provincial courts has helped nearly 20,000 individuals get out of prison, contributing to reducing prison overcrowding.
A senior official of the Ministry of Justice said this on April 12, 2022 at the meeting to review the work of justice in 2021 and work direction in 2022 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Kim Santepheap said that there are a number of criminal procedures that can help reduce overcrowding in prisons, such as:
* 1: Decision not to be remanded in custody and not to be placed under judicial supervision * 2: Issuance of a closing order to acquit * 3: Decision to be acquitted * 4: Ordinary suspension * 5: Suspension of probation * and 6: Release of prisoners serving their sentences.
He said that according to data collection and summary of court reports across the country during the 395 days of the campaign, prison overcrowding was reduced by:
Number of persons released from prison: 19,430 * Number of persons to be released approximately 7,087 * Number of persons decided not to be detained approximately 4,020 * Number of persons released Referred to drug rehabilitation centers instead of charges and sent to drug rehabilitation centers by the authorities, about 8,764 people.
According to the Ministry of Justice, the 395-day campaign to resolve congestion cases at the capital-provincial courts has contributed to reducing overcrowding by a total of 39,301 individuals.
