Siem Reap Sankranti Celebration of Khmer New Year has started from April 12
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Sankranti event, co-organized by the Siem Reap Provincial Authority and the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, began on the morning of April 12, 2022 at the Chao Say Tevta temple, beginning with a traditional flag-raising ceremony.
From more than 8 am, the Siem Reap Sankranti event management committee from various institutions came together to raise religious flags, with five monks chanting blessings and blessings as a sign to start the ceremony from now on.
In Siem Reap on April 12, there are a lot of people unusual than usual. Meanwhile, around the Angkor area and on some of the roads leading to the Angkor resort, the staff of the APSARA Authority are trying to clean up the environment of garbage in the parks around the ancient temples, and there are water trucks on the streets. Also, for attractiveness and happiness, good luck, waiting for the new year angel to come soon.
Events in Siem Reap, such as the drumming concert, river cruises, will begin on the afternoon of April 12, while the Sankranti Village Dance in Angkor Thom will begin. From April 13 onwards.
