Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Leads a Working Group to Visit the Remnants of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army
(Kampong Cham): On the morning of April 12, 2022, Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, led a delegation to visit and talk with the troops of Prey Chhor District Military Operation Area and the Vietnam Volunteer Army Mortuary Search Force.
Major General Ho Pov, Commander of Kampong Cham Provincial Military Operations Area, said that the troops of Kampong Cham Military Operations Area, together with local authorities, cooperated well with the Vietnam K70 Volunteer Corps Search and Rescue Team in the search operation. The remains of Vietnamese volunteer soldiers who sacrificed their lives during the war in Kampong Cham province have been in operation for 21 years.
Meanwhile, the K70 remains have been located in the Prey Chhor district military headquarters since 2018 due to the large number of tombs being searched in the area. But for 2020-2021, the K70 crematorium was inactive due to the outbreak of Kovid 19. And the resumption of the search for the remains on February 22, 2022 until now, the team found six remains.
Mr. Un Chanda took the opportunity to thank the local authorities and the Prey Chhor District Military Operations Force for their cooperation with the K70 Force to complete the mission successfully and would like to continue to support the work of the team. K70 work to get good results in Kampong Cham province.
