Wing Bank Provides Additional Support to Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association for Free Medical Services to Poor Communities Across Cambodia
The Memorandum of Understanding was presided over by Dr. Hun Manet, Chairman of the Board of Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association and Duke Kith Meng, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Wing Bank, and attended by Dr. Pech Chanmony, Vice Chairman of the Board of Youth Volunteer Doctors Association. Samdech Techo and many other distinguished guests.
Through this memorandum, Duke Kith Meng, Ms. Mao Chamnan and her family will donate $ 50,000 annually through Wing Bank to support the charity work of Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association.
Dr. HUN Manet expressed his deep gratitude to Duke Kith Meng and his wife for their strong commitment to support the charity work of Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association.
Dr. stated that this partnership shows that the commitment of the working group of Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association is to be recognized more and more by the public and more and more people are willing to join in the process. Community issues.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association was officially established in December 2012 under the initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and under the leadership of Dr. Hun Manet and Dr. Pich Chanmony for the purpose of providing medical services. Free to poor communities across Cambodia, especially people in remote areas to contribute to poverty reduction and promote the participation of young volunteers in social work.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng also thanked the team of Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association for their dedication and hard work for the community. Doctors, nurses and volunteers of the Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association have played an important role in helping to protect the community during an epidemic. We sincerely respect all of you selfless contributions.
During the past two years of epidemics, doctors, nurses and volunteers of the Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association worked day and night away from their families to keep people safe through Providing treatment to 25,842 patients, vaccinating 300,505 people in Phnom Penh and collecting samples from 871,786 people.
Please note that Duke Kith Meng and Mrs. Mao Chamnan are active supporters of the Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association for charity work to solve the challenges facing the community. In March 2021, the duke donated US $ 50,000 to the Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association for its strong efforts to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 virus in the community.
