Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) and Electricité du Cambodge (EDC) organize a solidarity meal for troops and families at Intervention Brigade 14
(Pursat): Starting from the sentiments of respect for the heroism of the army, on behalf of the Solidarity Unit, EDC and the Electricity Authority of Cambodia brought donations and organized solidarity meals for the troops and families in the 14th Intervention Brigade unit in the area. Bai Khleah, Tnaot Chum commune, Krakor district, Pursat province, to celebrate the traditional New Year, which will come from April 14 to 16, 2022.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of Electricite du Cambodge and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Krakor and Kandieng Districts, and Mr. Yim Viseth, Chairman of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia and Deputy Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group. Help Phnom Kravanh district.
The lieutenant general said that EDC and the Electricity Authority of Cambodia have never forgotten the army and their families, despite their busy efforts to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease, and continue to provide material and financial support, especially during traditional festivals.
With the support of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) and the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, as well as Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Commander-in-Chief of the Army, the troops were stationed along the rocky border and the military base decided to build strategic infrastructure along the border. Strong in defending the territorial integrity in Pursat province, achieving peace, stability and better.
Mr. Keo Rattanak expressed his heartfelt appreciation for the dedication of all officers, deputies and soldiers who have worked hard and sacrificed everything in the cause to protect the integrity of the territory and the people, even in hand. Prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
He said that in addition to providing food to the army and families, it also contributes to the construction of many infrastructures that are indispensable in the military, such as housing, office buildings, water and electricity.
In a situation where the society is affected by Kovid 19 disease, let the army and family implement the measures of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia "3 protect 3 do not" and must pay attention to training to increase the skills of the army ready to intervene when There are cases that happen by accident and involved in farming and animal husbandry.
He also reminded officers, deputies and soldiers to adhere to the position of loyalty to the nation, religion, the King by being united and supporting the candidacy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to continue as Prime Minister.
The Minister of Health requested the Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear provincial authorities to advise the public in their geographical areas about the exemption from the obligation to wear masks.
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission for Combating Kovid-19, on April 12, 2022, issued a letter to the provincial governor on the exemption from the obligation to wear a mask. In four provinces, including Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear.
In a letter received by Fresh News, the Minister of Health stated that the Royal Government has decided to waive the obligation to wear masks in Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear provinces.
In order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of this Royal Government decision, the Ministry of Health would like to request the Kovid-19 Disease Control Commission and the Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear provincial authorities to introduce to the public in the geographical area. Within its jurisdiction regarding the waiver of the duty to wear a mask and the continuation of the following necessary measures:
1: All people living in Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear provinces and people traveling from other capitals to four provinces are no longer required to wear masks, all people can choose by Yourself from continuing to wear a mask or not wearing a mask. However, the obligation to wear the mask continues to apply to Kovid-19 patients and those associated with Kovid-19 positives.
2. People who travel from the four provinces who are exempted from wearing the above mask duty, as well as all people living in other capitals and provinces, must continue to apply the mask duty which is in the health measures. 3 Protect and protect "persistently until a different decision.
