PM Samdech Techo Hun Sen Reminds People to Continue Implementing Health Measures on the Occasion of New Year (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Reminds People Across the Nation Health measures to be consistent, especially during the traditional New Year, which will take place from 14-16 April 2022.
Such concern for the Cambodian people was made on the occasion that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, together with the Ambassador of the Republic of India to Cambodia, Ms. Tevyani Udom Cobra Gade, received the Kovid 19 Vaccine with the assistance of the Government and the people. India on the morning of April 12, 2022 at the Peace Palace.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo said, "I would like to remind the Cambodian people to continue to implement health measures consistently, especially on the occasion of the traditional New Year on April 14, 15 and 16, 2022. This.
Please be informed that recently, the Head of the Royal Government also laid down three adherence points to the people all over the country on the occasion of the upcoming National New Year:
First, to implement the "3-protection, 3-do" measures, adhere to wearing a mask, keep the gap clean with alcohol properly, especially to carry a vaccination card with you every time you go out, because some places require guests In addition, the Ministry of Health also encourages people to get vaccinated at the resort if it is the third dose (boost dose).
Second: Must adhere to the traffic law in driving to travel to the destination and return home safely.
Third, to adhere to constant hygiene to prevent infection, especially Kovid 19 (Omikrong).
Samdech Techo Prime Minister also prayed to the New Year Angel to bless Samdech, Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, Ladies and Gentlemen, as well as the people of Cambodia across the country for the glory, happiness and prosperity.
