General knowledge: In World War II, which countries were the most devastated?
(Phnom Penh): World War II began on September 1, 1939, with German troops invading Poland, Italian troops invading African countries, and Japanese troops. First stage in Korea and China.
Until the end of the war on September 2, 1945, many countries in the world suffered heavy casualties, even those involved in the war and those involved in ending the war suffered considerable damage. Human life, wealth, infrastructure to the point of a complex socio-economic crisis.
Asia, on the other hand, suffered the same tragedy when the Imperial Japanese Army marched on China and clashed from 1937-1945. The Sino-Chinese war has caused a catastrophic disaster, killing 7 million civilians and 2 million Chinese troops, but official Chinese reports say the war has left scores dead. Wings up to 20 million people.
The Japanese invasion of China in 1937 was also a barrier between Japan itself and the real enemy, the Soviet Union. At that time, China did not have a central government, and much of this vast territory was ruled by generals, including the Kuomintang Republic, led by Zhang Kai-shek, and the Chinese Communist Party, led by Mao Zedong.
