Royal Government sets 6 strategic directions in Mondulkiri Tourism Development Master Plan
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has set out six strategic directions in the Mondulkiri Tourism Development Master Plan (2021-2035), which was officially launched on April 11, 2022.
The first strategic direction: to identify priority areas for tourism development in Mondulkiri, including:
Strategic Goal 5: Addressing the development of inter-sectoral infrastructure to support the development of tourism, including:
2: Supply and use of clean water: * By 2030, people living in urban and rural areas will have access to clean water. * Preserve existing water sources and find new water sources. * Learn more about reservoirs. And a water filter in Sen Monorom.
3. Electricity supply and use: * Attract local and foreign investors to develop and build electricity infrastructure. * Facilitate and support the study, exploration and development of clean or green electricity sources.
4: Preservation of indigenous culture: * Study and organize at least one indigenous museum in Sen Monorom city or at any important location. * Organize an indigenous community cultural village in Dak Dam commune, Oreang district. * Study the possibility of establishing a culture and fine arts school for indigenous peoples.
7: Small and medium enterprises and handicrafts: * Study to establish a training school or technical training institute in Mondulkiri province.
8. Support for medical and health services: * Strengthen the infrastructure and modernization of the medical and health sector in Mondulkiri province in accordance with national and international standards. * Prioritize investment and development of the health sector through the establishment of international standard hospitals in the province. Mondulkiri.
9: Promoting the development of technology, innovation and innovation: Sen Monorom should be studied to develop as a smart city (Smart City) and integrate smart technologies.
The sixth strategic direction: is to connect, facilitate travel and integration within the national and regional framework, at which point it is further explained that this travel connection is in three ways:
1: Air connection: Currently, the Royal Government is implementing the construction of Mondulkiri Airport, which not only connects domestic airports but also connects with neighboring countries such as Vietnam. Laos, Thailand and so on. According to the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, the construction of the airport will be completed by the end of 2023.
2: Waterway connection: Because in Koh Nhek district there is the Srepok River which connects with the Mekong River, so in the future Cambodia can connect the waterway tourism network from the point of Chaktomuk River, Tonle Sap area, coastal area and will be built There is a floating airport for tourism.
Mr. Aun Porn Moniroth said that the preparation and launch of the Tourism Development Master Plan for Mondulkiri 2021-2035 will allow Mondulkiri to be the destination of Cambodia's tourism diversification in the form of ecotourism, ecotourism and agriculture as well as tourism. Indigenous cultures that will contribute to making the Northeast region the fourth economic pole, with Mondulkiri as the core, in line with the long-term vision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Mr. Thong Khon said that this master plan will be an important strategic document to promote the development of tourism in Mondulkiri province as well as the whole northeast, especially contributing to make the northeast become the fourth economic pole of Cambodia. Representative of Mr. Thong Khon brought alms-giving to 6 pagodas in Tnaot Chum commune, Baray district and distributed some gifts to teachers and students
