Mr. Som Aun: Union activists must continue to disseminate Samdech Techo's 10 key recommendations effectively in line with the motto "A factory, an enterprise, a peaceful community"
(Phnom Penh): With the permission of Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Chairman of the Union Committee, this morning, April 11, 2022, Mr. Som Aun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and a member of the Union Movement Invited to preside over the social gathering and dinner to celebrate the upcoming Khmer New Year.
The event was organized by the Cambodian Confederation of Workers 'Rights (CCWR) with the participation of the leaders of the Confederation of Trade Unions - Associations that are members of the Cambodian Workers' Rights Union, as well as with the honorary participation of the President and Vice Presidents of the National Assembly of the Cambodian Confederation of Unions.
* First, continue to strengthen the implementation of the law on the minimum wage and encourage all factories to implement the payment of wages and open twice a month, which we have seen in the past to help improve the quality of life. Workers reduce the problem of strikes and demonstrations.
* Second, continue to strengthen the implementation of the social security system for health care for workers, especially workers of small and medium enterprises, by encouraging small and medium enterprises to make workbooks and ID cards of Cambodian workers to record the movement. Employees, seniority, skill level, ability, roles and achievements and occupational disease history of workers, as well as to be the basis for registration with the CPC.
* Third: Continue to monitor the implementation of 120% of wages and leave for 3 months during childbirth of workers.
* Fourth: Continue to provide allowances to workers during childbirth, both in the system and outside the system by providing one child 400,000 Riels, two children 800,000 Riels and three children 1.2 million Riels and additional budget 5 million Riels from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit himself.
* Fifth, continue to disseminate the party's attention to providing health care to workers and continue the policy for employers to pay 100% social security contributions for health care on behalf of workers, and strengthen the implementation of safety and health conditions. Work (OSH) in factories, enterprises.
* Sixth: Continue to cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions at the sub-national level in connecting electricity and water in rented houses at reasonable prices, implementing the special lease law (rental room law) to facilitate the lives of workers in and Informal, especially in areas where there is an outbreak of Kovid-19 disease.
* Seventh: Continue to strengthen the implementation of the social security system on occupational risk for public officials and launch the social security system on pensions in the first quarter of 2022.
* Eighth: Continue to encourage workers and employers to use internal negotiation mechanisms to determine the exact procedures and dates for payment of seniority benefits and to resolve labor disputes in accordance with the status of their factories, enterprises and businesses to maintain Occupational sustainability and harmony in professional relations during the outbreak of Kovid-19 disease.
10th: Continue to strengthen cooperation with partner countries, including Thailand, Malaysia, Korea, Japan, Hong Kong, Singapore and other countries to provide employment opportunities for workers, protect the rights, interests, honor and dignity of workers, as well as qualify you to receive Transfer of social security and recognition of skills upon return to the motherland. Kampong Cham Provincial Administration Shows Off Pagodas and Recreation Areas for Kovid Vaccination for New Year
