The following is the Royal Decree of the King: Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth: Mondulkiri Province will become the fourth economic pole by providing many benefits from tourism to the country (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia on On April 11, 2022, the Master Plan for Tourism Development of Mondulkiri Province 2021-2035 was officially launched.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Committee for Tourism Development, presented the benefits that Cambodia will receive after the official launch of the Mondulkiri Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035. .
He added that the identification of key priority areas for tourism development in the master plan will encourage Mondulkiri to make full use of its rich potential through eco-tourism conservation. And indigenous development and multi-sectoral linkages.
"Mondulkiri has great potential in agriculture, especially the development of flower, vegetable, fruit and industrial crops such as coffee," he said.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth added that success will move forward depending on the close cooperation, deep cooperation and responsibility of all stakeholders, especially the partnership between the state, citizens and the private sector, as well as the participation of Official Development Partners.
Dr. Thong Khon stated that at the same time, through the preface of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in approving the Master Plan, the Royal Government also agreed to set six key priorities to be kept for development and to determine the scope of investment activities. And develop these areas clearly, including:
1: Ecotourism and ecotourism corridors of the 5 wildlife sanctuaries. 2: Busra-Dak Dam cultural and ecotourism corridor. 3: Sen Monorom city. 5: Urban area of Koh Nhek district. 6: Integrated tourist area along the border.
In this regard, the main purpose of the master plan is to promote the development of Mondulkiri, an international eco-tourism destination and an important province in the supply of flowers, vegetables, fruits and meat to meet domestic demand and reach exports to foreign markets. .
