Commentary: Promoting the spirit of the Beijing Winter Olympics, urging people of all countries to move forward together
BEIJING, April 8 (Xinhua) - Chinese President Xi Jinping delivered a keynote speech at the General Assembly on April 8, praising the results of the Beijing Olympics and Winter Olympics. Strongly pledged to the international community in every way and providing a simple, safe and spectacular Olympics to the world.
More importantly, in a world that has been in turmoil, the Beijing Winter Olympics have promoted cultural learning among each other and sowed the seeds of unity and friendship. Countries together for the future. Cambodia will strengthen cooperation with ASEAN members to address regional and global challenges on economic recovery
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance of Cambodia, in its capacity as chair of the ASEAN Finance Ministers' Meeting, is committed to closer cooperation among ASEAN members to jointly improve the implementation of relevant activities to address these challenges. Regional and global, such as promoting trade and investment facilitation.
At the same time, Cambodia will deepen ASEAN financial integration with its partners, accelerate the implementation of regional cross-border payment systems, and promote sustainable finance to mobilize additional financing for economic recovery and development. Sustainable regions, ensuring regional financial stability and bridging the development gap in digital finance and sustainable finance.
This is according to the press release on the 26th ASEAN Finance Ministers' Meeting, the 8th Joint Meeting between the Finance Ministers and the Governor of the ASEAN Central Bank and the relevant meeting hosted by Cambodia on 7-8 April 2022, which was just published on April 11.
The meeting reviewed and exchanged views on the regional and global economic and financial situation and perspective, focusing on risks, challenges, opportunities and policy measures to respond to the progress and further direction of ASEAN financial cooperation. Aims to ensure deeper financial integration and continue to build the resilience of the regional financial system.
In discussions with international financial institutions, ASEAN finance ministers and governors noted the growth of the world economy at 4.4 percent (forecast by the IMF) and the ASEAN economy at 5.1 percent. Percentage (forecast by AMRO) in 2022.
At the same time, the meeting also noted some risks that are negatively impacting the acceleration of the regional economic recovery, such as the continued spread of new viruses of Kovid-19, supply chain disruption, war problems. In Eastern Europe, high inflation and climate change.
