Mr. HUN Manet emphasized the important meaning in terms of participating in the Ramadan meal together today:
* First, it is a testament to the harmonization of religion in Cambodia and a contribution to respecting the values, religions, customs and traditions of the Muslims.
* Second: Demonstrating unity under the umbrella of one leadership and on behalf of the same Cambodian people as a reflection of the culture of sharing love, giving.
* Third: Providing opportunities to learn about each other, especially the sacred meaning and benefits of Ramadan for Muslims in terms of faith, religion, society and health.
He also praised and thanked the leaders and colleagues, as well as the Muslim youth, as well as local authorities at all levels for co-organizing this meaningful gathering in the spirit of unity as one great Khmer family. In addition, the program also contributes to the promotion of the implementation of religious teachings and the spirit of determination, patience, along with kindness, understanding and mutual respect.
