(World): Among the many wonders that Mother Nature has created, it is certain that sand dunes are one of the most fascinating phenomena on our planet. Sand dunes are defined as places that do not suffer from or suffer the least amount of weather, such as rain and snow, throughout the year. This makes them difficult places for animals, plants and even humans to live.
When talking about the desert, most people probably think of the arid region, which is nothing but sand. It is true that most deserts are like this, but there are also cold deserts. On the contrary, this type of desert is more unfavorable for life and survival than the hot desert.
However, whether hot or cold, some desert areas can extend over the largest area. For the 10 largest desert areas, which will be described below, are larger than many countries on earth.
10: Chivoan Desert
9: Great Basin Desert
8: Syria Desert
7: Patagonia Desert
6: Galilee Desert
5: Gobi Desert
4: Arab Desert
3: Sahara Desert
2: Arctic Desert
1: Antarctic sand dunes
