This traditional Khmer farmer festival is organized by the Cambodian Peace Forum in collaboration with the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and Kampong Leng District Authority, with the participation of Mr. Suon Serey Ratha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development and President of the Cambodian Peace Forum, Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province. And SOSYOK youth leaders, as well as many provincial leaders.
Mr. HUN Many expressed his pleasure to participate in the Dar Lan Festival, a traditional Khmer farmer. He warmly welcomed the members of the Cambodian Peace Forum who cooperated and joined with the local authorities in organizing this significant event in preparation for the upcoming Khmer New Year.
At the same time, Mr. HUN Many also thanked all the people, government officials, youth groups who came to participate in this day, and he also sent a message to all young men and women on the occasion of the upcoming New Year. Create a dance program to entertain people with songs such as choreography, choreography, Saravan, Lam Leav, Chok Kampus, etc. in order to preserve our national tradition.
He also claimed that according to the study of documents and studies from the elders as living documents, we know that the Dar Lan festival has three main purposes that the original Khmer ancestors left to the next generation to celebrate this festival. :
First, the farmers came together to strengthen the bonds of solidarity and exchange experiences with each other, and on the other hand, they participated happily after working hard to grow crops for a long time.
Second: To educate farmers to love rice like the rich, because rice in our ancient ancestors considered "God", so they love rice like their parents and life.
