(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Sunday, April 10, 2022, decided to place four provinces no longer required to wear masks. The four provinces are: Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear. However, the government leaves it up to the people to decide for themselves whether to wear it or not.
In a voice message to his compatriots, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that this decision was made after a thorough discussion with the leaders of the Royal Government and relevant officials. Samdech Techo also stated that the people who enter this province are not required to wear the mask, but the decision to wear or not to wear depends on themselves.
Samdech Techo, the Prime Minister, stated, "People in the four provinces choose to wear their own masks or not?" People who go out to visit in the four provinces choose themselves to wear a mask or not? It is up to the individual to decide. "But after leaving these four provinces, it is obligatory to wear a mask as part of a three-pronged and three-pronged health measure."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this decision is a test of resilience and resilience in the community, which Cambodia has successfully implemented in the past.
Samdech Techo added, "We are not testing the lives of the people, but we want to know about the resilience of our communities, both urban and rural." "The provinces that we have implemented are non-communicable provinces, and if there are, there are very few in the past."
Despite the decision not to implement the duty of wearing a mask in the four provinces, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to advise people who leave the four provinces to strictly implement the duty of wearing a mask. As a result, the possibility of transmitting the virus from these four provinces to other provinces is limited.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that this instruction will be implemented from now on. Samdech Techo instructed Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, to prepare guidelines and additional measures for this new decision.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed the authorities in the four provinces to pay attention to this work and also to prepare for the rapid test in case of any need. Samdech Techo also called on people in the four provinces to take a quick test in case of doubt about their health.
