(Kampong Chhnang): The Cambodian Peace Forum, in cooperation with the Kampong Leng District Administration, on April 9, 2022, yesterday held a Krong Pali Sen Pren Ceremony to ask for happiness during the Dalan Festival of Khmer Farmers in Damnak Koh Village, Po Commune, Kampong Leng District.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Suon Serey Ratha, President of the Cambodian Peace Forum and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, with the participation of Ms. Born Sophy, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, Mr. Yem Leakena, District Governor of Kampong Leng and the working group of local authorities as well as local people. The commune village as well.
Mr. Yem Leakena, Governor of Kampong Leng District, said that the traditional festival of Khmer farmers will start on April 10 for another day with the participation of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration under the chairmanship of Mr. HUN Many, Chairman of the 7th Commission. Of the National Assembly and also the President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia.
The event is planned to be attended by about a thousand people, as well as a film screening of the General Department of Bayon Radio and Television and a bassac performance for the public to watch at night and many other popular games. .
In the sermon on April 9, the monks who were the preachers in the above Dalan festival, it was confirmed that this traditional Dalan festival of Khmer farmers in some areas is called Bon Poun Phnom Srov or Bon Phum Chea village festival. Originally, however, the ceremonies were in the same order.
This Dalan festival, according to the documents of our Khmer ancestors, said that the Dalan festival is a reminder of the merits of the Khmer ancestors who left the land for their children to farm for a living until today. On the other hand, this festival is held to apologize to the land of the land where our farmers have plowed, cultivated, built houses and defecated on the land, which is not appropriate.
(Phnom Penh): With only about 4 days left, the traditional New Year festival, the year of Karl Chatva Sak 2566, will arrive. After a two-year ban on New Year's Eve gatherings due to the 19-year outbreak of Kovid, this year Samdech Techo Hun Sen, head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has allowed people to gather and play. Have fun again.
Allowing for gatherings and entertainment during the New Year is due to the Royal Government overcoming the Kovid 19 epidemic, reducing the spread of this global virus. As the date of the New Year approaches, it is observed that Cambodians who have moved away from the country to work or study in Phnom Penh are gradually starting to travel to their hometowns. .
Some people use motorbikes, bicycles and cars to get to their hometowns. Both motorbikes, tricycles and cars are packed with suitcases and luggage. Some also have drinks, cakes, and some snacks for family and relatives in their hometowns.
It is also observed that no matter what means are used, each citizen shows a happy face as they return to reunite with their grandparents, parents, family and relatives after being away from work to support themselves and their families. Find knowledge, etc. in Phnom Penh. Family reunion time is a very happy time for Cambodian family life.
