(Kunming): Trade between China and countries along the Mekong River has continued to grow despite the impact of the Kovid-19 pandemic and the slowdown in the global economic recovery. According to China's Xinhua news agency.
As a result of extensive cooperation in efforts to fight the new virus and boost economic growth, trade between China and five other Mekong countries has grown to a record high, according to the official Xinhua news agency. Nearly $ 400 billion in 2021, an increase of 23% compared to 2020.
This figure was revealed in the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation 2020, which launched on Thursday.
In 2016, the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation Mechanism (LMC) was launched by six countries, including China, Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam. The name of this cooperation is derived from the name of the river called Lanchang in China and the Mekong in five other countries.
Since then, the LMC mechanism has become an important model of regional cooperation and continues to inject energy into regional development. Xinhua News Agency: Mr. Eang Sophalleth: Teachers are the founders of the future of the nation and the world.
