Commentary: Don't let the fun of Khmer New Year turn into sorrow
(Phnom Penh): The traditional New Year, the year of Karl Chatva Sak, Buddhist era 2565, which falls on April 14, 2022, will be celebrated in the framework of the whole country, where the Cambodian people are ready to participate in the festival. This comes after a two-year hiatus due to the Kovid-19 outbreak.
Khmer New Year is an important national holiday for the people of Cambodia, the Royal Government has allowed civil servants, workers, people to take time off from work to visit their hometowns, travel to various tourist attractions, play Khmer folk games and have Opportunity to perform rituals at pagodas and so on.
On the occasion of the Khmer New Year, Her Excellency Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Kovid-19 Vaccination Commission throughout the country, encouraged all people to continue to implement necessary measures for health. Including transmission of Kovid 19 virus.
She added that at present, the presence of Kovid 19 virus is not over yet, as the disease is still spreading around the world, region and Cambodia.
Voice: "In order for a fun trip to avoid the spread of various diseases, especially the disease of Kovid 19, please remind and urge all people to continue to work together. Take precautionary measures to be very careful, especially to learn to live with the presence of Kovid-19 virus by continuing to be vigilant and living a normal life in a new normal, by continuing to implement 3 measures to prevent and 3 not to be serious. Most.
In this regard, Mr. Oung Vuth, a resident of Phnom Penh, supported this guideline and will implement this measure well. He considered that the Royal Government has opened the organization of the Khmer New Year, a traditional Khmer festival, it is very good for him as well as other people to take a break to reunite with their families and go for a walk.
In conclusion, in order for our Khmer New Year trip to be peaceful, safe and happy, all people must obey the instructions of the Ministry of Health, obey the traffic law, increase high awareness of fire and other accidents, do not be happy Forget it, otherwise our happiness will turn into misery.
