(Preah Sihanouk): A suspect was arrested by Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police under the direct command of Major General Chuon Narin after stealing a car minutes in Village 2, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville Province. Sihanoukville on the night of April 8, 2022.
Immediately after receiving the information, the specialized force of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police conducted a thorough search and cooperated with the Prey Nup District Inspectorate until 1:00 AM on April 08, 2022. The vehicle was found at O'Chamnar village, O'Oknha Heng commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province, and a suspect was arrested and taken to the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police for questioning.
The suspect is currently being investigated by the Sihanoukville Provincial Police Office of Minor Offenses to be sent to court for further proceedings.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch: Samdech Techo Hun Sen leads Cambodia firmly with a long-term vision and creates a good environment for business people
(Phnom Penh): Speaking to business people at the celebration of the 10th anniversary of the Indian Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has led Cambodia firmly with a long-term vision. Far away and create a good environment for business people.
The Senior Minister also expressed his congratulations on the 70th anniversary of the historic relationship between Cambodia and India, which he was confident would bring further improvements in active participation in trade and business.
The Senior Minister told the ceremony that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister, has strong leadership with a long-term vision, brings peace and stability, and has established policies to provide a lot of opportunities and support. Investing for business people and investing in Cambodia.
With this talented leadership, Cambodia has had more than two decades of domestic production of Kenling, whose basic products are agriculture, intimate investment, increased labor force, small and medium enterprises, and access to Southeast Asian markets. And so on.
