Samdech Heng Samrin: Sharing culture enables Cambodia to overcome all obstacles, especially Kovid-19, and is appreciated everywhere
(Tbong Khmum): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, stated that the culture of sharing enables Cambodia to overcome all obstacles, especially Kovid-19, and be praised everywhere.
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin and Samdech Thamma Visoth Vongsa presiding over the inauguration ceremony of achievements in Wat Sovanmoly called Wat Koki Chrap in Koki Chrap Village, Leang Commune, Tbong Khmum District, Tbong Khmum Province.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei congratulated and congratulated the Chief Prelate of Wat Preah Theranut Thera, all the leaders at all levels and all the benefactors near and far, especially the team that has contributed significantly. Donate material, budget, physical and mental strength to achieve many achievements in both the realm of the empire and the Buddha.
Samdech stated that the churches and achievements that are preparing for the Passover and inauguration now are a true reflection of the value of participation and unity of the people and leaders at all levels. In the cultural spirit of sharing.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin continued that the culture of sharing is very valuable in all circumstances, especially in times of disaster or emergency. By working diligently to protect and assist victims in the fight against the human enemies of the Kovid-19 epidemic, the art of sharing among the highly respected and respected Cambodians is evident. .
He stressed that the virtues of Cambodia under the leadership of the People's Party, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Party President and Prime Minister, are recognized and respected by the world for the fight against Kovid-19. Seek help in purchasing vaccines from other countries and treating Kovid patients until they are cured. Providing and vaccinating in Cambodia without racism, caste, or free of charge.
On the occasion of the upcoming National New Year, the President of the National Assembly called on the people to be very careful by adhering to the three measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and must Drive with respect to traffic laws and be tolerant of each other.
