Mr. Neth Pheaktra: Green Sankranti is not only an event to celebrate the traditional Khmer New Year, but also an opportunity to cultivate the people's spirit to respect the environment and natural resources more
(Kampong Speu): "Green Sankranti is not only an event to celebrate the traditional Khmer New Year and show the culture and art, but also an opportunity to cultivate the people's spirit to respect the environment and natural resources more and participate. The Royal Government to create a local economy, create jobs and increase income for the livelihood of local people through eco-tourism and other occupations.
This is the statement of Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment on the afternoon of April 8, 2022, on the occasion of his participation in presiding over the opening of the "Green Sankranti" event organized by the Youth Volunteers to help the Green Variety community.
The opening ceremony of the Green Festival at Peam Lvea Dam, Trapeang Cho Commune, Oral District, Kampong Speu Province was also presided over by representatives of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Ministry of Information, the Ministry of Tourism, Kampong Speu Province and a number of well-known artists. Entertain the local people and inspire them to participate in promoting national culture and preserving natural resources, forests and wildlife.
Secretary of State Neth Pheaktra emphasized: “For the people in Tampaing Chor commune, there is a natural heritage, Boeung Peam Lvea, a community forest surrounded by mountains, which is a valuable natural resource that can benefit from the endless nature of eco-tourism. Create new jobs for local people.
On that occasion, he also called on the people to join in protecting and conserving the natural resources of the forest and wildlife in this area, how to preserve the natural beauty of this area from being lost to the source of income from eco-tourism.
In the "Green Sankrant" event, there is a stall showcasing the community's products to show the participants the kinds of food and other products that Trapeang Chor commune has. In addition, there is an exhibition of works of art made from recycled plastic waste and other attractive waste, as well as an exhibition of traps, guns, chainsaws, which are tools to destroy natural resources, forests and wildlife.
Mr. Tan Kimsour, Project Manager of Green Sankranti Event, said that this event is organized in a deep sense to contribute to the promotion of culture and conservation of Cambodia's forests, as well as to celebrate the traditional Khmer New Year.
Mr. Tan Kimsour stated that the Green Sankranti event is a movement of connecting people and people, human and nature, people and arts, culture, Khmer traditions and cultivating the consciousness of young people to love, preserve and develop natural resources, national cultural heritage.
Speaking at the opening ceremony of the Green Sankranti event, Mr. Sar Putra, Deputy Governor of Kampong Speu Province, praised the Green Sankranti Initiative, saying that the event has been transforming the area from the sound of chainsaws to deforestation. A fun place.
He added that on behalf of the Kampong Speu Provincial Administration, he would like to support any initiative to promote Boeung Peam Lvea as a more attractive tourist destination.
At the same time, representatives of the Ministry of Information and the Ministry of Tourism, Ministry of Culture also expressed support for this green Sankranti event.
