Highlights to know about the French presidential election this Sunday
The election will also decide whether caretaker President Emmanuel Macron will have another chance to lead the country or whether France will have a new leader. Here are the important things to know about the French presidential election:
* When will the election take place? Elections in France are held every Sunday and the presidential election is divided into two rounds. The first round will take place on Sunday, April 10 to select the only two presidential candidates who will run in the second round, which will take place on Sunday, April 24.
* Who are the presidential candidates? In order to run for the French presidency, a candidate must gather 500 votes from about 42,000 elected officials, and this support must pass certification. By the Constitutional Council and the French Supreme Court before March 4. There are 12 French presidential candidates in 2022:
In addition, Makrong will still be able to defeat Le Pen in the second round of the French presidential election to be held on April 24 with 54 percent of the vote to 46 percent.
