Duke Kith Meng urges ASEAN Finance Ministers and Central Bank Governors to work together to reduce business costs and help SMEs
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, on the occasion of participating in the ASEAN Business Advisory Council and ASEAN Finance Ministers' Meeting, which was held online, requested the Minister Finance and the Governor of the Central Bank of ASEAN work together to reduce the cost of doing business and help SMEs with challenges.
Speaking on the occasion of this meeting, Duke Kith Meng, Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, informed of the support of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council on the ASEAN theme, which Cambodia co-chairs ASEAN: "Solve all challenges. Each other.
The Duke also reported to the meeting on the key recommendations of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, which focused on three key points:
1: Rehabilitation of the business sector severely damaged by the global epidemic and the main obstacles that occur to business, especially for micro-enterprises, small and medium enterprises
2: Closer cooperation in laying the groundwork for a sustainable future and green growth
3: Strengthening cooperation between the state and the private sector under the framework of the meeting of the Minister of Finance and the Governor of the ASEAN National Bank
Duke Kith Meng called for joint efforts to reduce the cost of doing business at both the national and regional levels, and to find ways to make the supply chain more resilient in times of crisis. Global Challenges and Support Training for micro, small and medium enterprises on credit mechanisms, risk management and disaster preparedness based on past global experience.
He added that micro, small and medium enterprises (SMEs) are still facing difficulties and are trying to find easier ways to access banking and insurance through technology nurseries that require the construction of a cross-border credit ecosystem. Which is usable and highly effective.
In addition, Duke Kith Meng called for financial infrastructure readiness to take advantage of new markets and opportunities, especially from the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP), which will help boost the economy. Resilience to crises and protection from obstacles caused by geopolitics and other risks.
The meeting was also attended by the ASEAN-Malaysia Business Advisory Council on the economic challenges posed by geopolitics, the EU-ASEAN Business Council intervention on green and sustainable finance, and US-ASEAN Business Council Intervention on the Future of Digital and Data Perspectives.
In addition, ASEAN finance ministers and governors from other member countries also intervened in response to the business council requests and raised the status quo in their respective countries.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Co-Chair of the ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Finance and the Governor of the Central Bank of ASEAN, commended the active participation of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council and considered All recommendations made by the ASEAN Business Advisory Council.
