Minister Thong Khon Leads a Delegation to Distribute and Distribute Donations to Troops at the 4th Military Command
(Siem Reap): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, on the morning of April 8, 2022, led a delegation led by officials and officials of the Ministry of Tourism, accompanied by Mr. Long Kosal, Deputy Director General of APSARA, Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Association. Cambodian Tourism holds talks and distributes gifts to officers, deputies, and soldiers under the 4th Army Command in Prasat Bakong District, Siem Reap Province.
Lt. Gen. Pov Heng, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the 4th Army Command, reported to the delegation from the Ministry of Tourism and the APSARA Authority on ensuring security and order to the people's leadership and Tourists, territorial integrity protection, border protection, as well as participating in past and present Kovid 19 epidemic prevention and vaccination campaigns.
Mr. Thong Khon brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who always thought about the well-being and life of the officers. Deputy soldiers and soldiers.
At the same time, the Minister praised the heroic and heroic spirit of the officers, deputies and soldiers under the command of the 4th Army Division to ensure security, order, protection of territorial integrity and participation in Campaign to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and a successful vaccination campaign.
Minister Thong Khon also mentioned the reopening of international tourist destinations, as well as the socio-economic activities that have boosted tourism and aviation.
Minister Thong Khon also requested Lt. Gen. Pov Heng, as well as officers, deputies and soldiers under the 4th Army Command to continue to maintain security and order for the people and tourists. Even better, especially during the traditional Khmer New Year and during the reopening of Cambodia under the concept of "Cambodia is a safe and cozy tourist destination."
Cambodia and the United Nations continue to promote good cooperation today
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Ms. Pauline Tamesis, UN Resident Coordinator in Cambodia, today expressed satisfaction over the good cooperation between Cambodia and the United Nations. And have the same commitment to further strengthen good cooperation.
The Deputy Prime Minister also commended the UN agencies in Cambodia for providing invaluable assistance, including financial, technical and operational assistance, as well as a large number of vaccines through the COVAX mechanism and other medical devices. To help Cambodia fight the 199 Kovid epidemic.
The Deputy Prime Minister highlighted Cambodia's pride in ranking second in the Asia-Pacific region for successful vaccination, which has allowed the Royal Government to reopen the country since November last year.
The Deputy Prime Minister also mentioned the strong support of the UN. Assist Cambodia in implementing its commitment to climate action and in drafting laws and policies, as well as technical guidelines to enhance the performance of public institutions and the implementation of human rights.
Ms. Pauline Tamesis praised the socio-economic development, the significant contribution to Cambodia's international peacekeeping efforts, Cambodia's success in the fight against Kovid-19, which led to the reopening of the country, and highlighted From the strong support of the United Nations for the formulation of strategies and policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia towards its Sustainable Development Goals.
She also expressed appreciation and gratitude for the cooperation, support and coordination provided to the UN agency in Cambodia by the Royal Government, especially the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
In a report on Friday, the Vietnamese Ministry of Health also announced 35 new cases of Kovid 19 disease.
