ASEAN foreign ministers issue condolences over civilian deaths in Ukraine (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): ASEAN foreign ministers issued five condolences on April 8, 2022. To the death of an innocent person in Buja, Ukraine.
1. We, the ASEAN Foreign Ministers, extend our deepest condolences to the people of Ukraine on the reports of civilian killings in Ukraine. We all mourn with the families of relatives who have lost their loved ones in conflict.
2. We support the UN Secretary-General's call for an investigation into allegations of atrocities against innocent civilians, including in Bucharest, to prevent a recurrence. And for justice.
3. We also emphasize the importance of the humanitarian corridor, which allows for the safe transport of humanitarian aid to Ukraine.
4. We call for the full efforts of all stakeholders and the international community to stop and avoid any fighting and to diligently end it, not to escalate the conflict and bloodshed. Each.
5. We reaffirm our call for an immediate ceasefire and resume all-round political dialogue that will lead to lasting peace in Ukraine.
Ministry of Education and JICA to Inaugurate Buildings and Achievements at Battambang Provincial Pedagogical Institute on April 11
(Battambang): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, in collaboration with JICA, will inaugurate the buildings and achievements of the Battambang Provincial Teacher Training Institute, which will take place on April 11, 2022 at the Battambang Provincial Teacher Training Institute. Battambang Province.
The project has built five new buildings, including an administration building, a school building, a library building, and a multi-purpose dormitory, as well as providing essential facilities for science laboratories, computer labs, and music and art rooms to support learning. And teach better.
In addition to this grant, JICA and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports are also implementing technical assistance projects to build the foundations of the two pedagogical institutes by developing detailed curricula for undergraduate education, teaching and examination materials, and systems. Management of the institute, as well as the development of strategic documents for the promotion of teacher qualifications.
The project also focuses on developing the capacity of trainers, including the ability to conduct research, education and develop curricula and scholarship programs to study for a master's degree in Japan.
This good collaboration will actively contribute to the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports as its staff, as well as development partners, in responding to the priority needs for teacher education reform in Cambodia. .
