Watch the full video below: The National Council for Social Protection in collaboration with Oxfam and six civil society organizations organized a campaign on social protection
(Phnom Penh): Oxfam, along with six civil society organizations and the National Council for Social Protection (NSPC), has jointly organized a nationwide outreach campaign on social protection with financial support from the German Federal Ministry for Cooperation and Economic Development. (BMZ) through GIZ.
The campaign focuses on the importance of equity cards, cash support programs for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age, and the Health Equity Fund, which is being disseminated through all possible means, such as local radio, online news, and online news. Telegraphic society, face-to-face meetings in the community.
To provide information to people in the most remote areas to ensure an indigenous environment, radio interview programs are also available in local languages such as Phnong Kreung, Koy, Tampoun and Jarai.
According to an assessment conducted by Oxfam on the level of awareness and access to information on social protection projects among Cambodians, October 2021 is available on Oxfam Cambodia website. Such programs as cash support for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age and the Health Equity Fund are not yet widely known to Cambodians.
According to the study, 54% of respondents were aware of the cash aid program and 41% were aware of the Health Equity Fund.
Phean Sophoan, director of Oxfam, said that social protection is an important tool for reducing people's vulnerability to economic, environmental and social impacts throughout their life cycle. Social protection has shown the potential to support individuals living in poverty or those facing recession.
She said it was urgent and necessary to coordinate multilateral cooperation to address the lack of knowledge and understanding.
The UN General Assembly on Thursday voted on a US-initiated suspension of Russia membership with 93 votes in favor, 24 against and 58 abstentions.
According to Reuters, in the run-up to the election, Russia warned countries that voting in favor or abstention would be considered "hostile gestures" and would have consequences for bilateral relations with Russia. Russia's suspension of elections comes after the Russian army was accused of committing war crimes by massacring hundreds of Ukrainian civilians, especially in the city of Buja.
