Calmette Hospital, in collaboration with the National Blood Transfusion and Vital Center, organized the 8th Blood Donation Program
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of April 8, 2022, Calmette Hospital, in collaboration with Vital Drinking Water Company and the National Blood Transfusion Center, organized a voluntary blood donation program under the theme "Together donate blood today to save maternal life" at In the conference hall of Techo Santepheap Building of Calmette Hospital.
This program is the annual program of Calmette Hospital, which aims to inspire the voluntary blood donation movement to contribute to the blood supply to patients in need of blood in hospitals.
The program was held in the presence of Prof. Chheang Ra, Director General of Calmette Hospital, Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, General Director of OneFreighty (Vital), Dr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, and the presence of leaders, civil servants, staff and philanthropists of the three institutions. Receiving more than 250 blood donation volunteers.
Mr. Sok Po said that on behalf of the National Blood Transfusion Center of Cambodia of the Ministry of Health, all civil servants and staff, we are very honored to work with Calmette Hospital and Vital to promote voluntary blood donation. The aim is to ensure a safe supply of blood in sufficient quantities in a timely manner to save the lives of all victims, patients who need blood urgently and in an emergency.
He continued that the campaign "Together to donate blood to save maternal life" today is a meaningful topic for all of us and has two main objectives, including:
* First, establish the habit and culture of voluntary blood donation and encourage the general public to participate in activities with the National Blood Transfusion Service throughout the country to ensure adequate blood supply for maternal patients in need. Blood in all hospitals without discrimination, regardless of race or religion.
* Second, link the activities of voluntary blood donation to good humanitarian activities in society.
He added that the National Blood Transfusion Center has booked this important event and would like to express its sincere gratitude for all the support for the humanitarian cause and called for continued support in all its forms in future campaigns. Face.
Prof. Chheang Ra said that this is the eighth time that Calmette Hospital has organized a voluntary blood donation program of leaders, civil servants, staff and philanthropists due to the Kovid Crisis. .
With social conditions returning to normal, coupled with the vaccination strategy of the head of the Royal Government, the hospital has made a responsible decision to reorganize the voluntary blood donation of Leaders, civil servants, staff and philanthropists at Calmette Hospital follow the new normal trajectory.
He also thanked Vital Company and the National Blood Transfusion Center, which are always eager to promote and collect generous blood everywhere to meet the need for blood throughout the country.
Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, General Manager of OneFreternity (Vital) Company, thanked the management of Calmette Hospital and the National Blood Transfusion Center for their continued support and full operational cooperation with Vital from the beginning.
She added that the program comes at a time when the world has not yet completely recovered from the Kovid-19 crisis. At the same time, Cambodia, as well as the world, is going through a rapidly evolving trend of many trends that create endless challenges and risks, and what is remarkable is that the demand for blood in Cambodia is increasing. Up.
It should be noted that Vital, which has a fund of 25R, has continued to maintain the basis of support in all activities and campaigns of voluntary blood donation from all institutions. Botum Sakor District Governor Meets 34 Commune / Sangkat Councilors and Provides Some Clothes and Budget
