This outreach training is designed to enhance the effectiveness of investigative work on the notion of money laundering offenses by identifying measures to determine the source of the investigation, the techniques of the investigation in analyzing and evaluating the effects of the offense to reach Build a case to be sent to court, the content of this standard operating procedure focuses on the following points:
* A. Understanding the source of the offense: Judicial police officers must understand the source of the offense that results in the offense so that the judicial police officer has a basis to investigate money laundering offenses.
* B. Prerequisites for the investigation of money laundering offenses: Judicial police officers must analyze and evaluate the notion of money laundering offenses based on the offenses of the source of the above offenses, requiring pre-operational asset research and asset determination. And so on.
C. Techniques for investigating money laundering: Judicial police officers must understand the techniques of the investigation, including the investigation of suspects, the beneficiaries of the offenses, the determination of the consequences of the offenses, the determination of assets and the techniques for Get information to support those investigations.
* D. Action on the property of the suspect: Judicial police officers, after identifying the property of the suspect, must take immediate measures to take action on those assets, such as the seizure of evidence, the suspension of account transactions by the investigation unit. Cambodian finance and so on.
* E. Case building: After gathering information that may be based on the assessment of money laundering offenses, judicial police officers must make a synthetic report and send the case to court. In case the judicial police officer is not able to gather enough information, the judicial police officer can attach additional request with the synthesis report to the prosecutor to issue an order to temporarily detain the property suspected to be the result of a crime.
