Political party president wants to see people use social media with dignity, not pollute society
(Phnom Penh): The President of the Khmer National Unity Party, Mr. Un Chim, expressed his desire to see all people use social media with accuracy and dignity, that is, not to pollute society.
Speaking to Fresh News on March 7, 2022, Mr. Un Chim supported the authorities who had in the past called some social media users who used obscene and insulting words to guide and educate. However, he wants to see the authorities act more strongly so that those bad activities do not affect society, especially the younger generation.
Un Chim always sends a message to his supporters to live in a peaceful and dignified society. The politician also considered a man nicknamed "dwarf teacher" who ate cow dung to attract the attention and interests of his group as an act of social pollution.
"Please support the authorities in Kandal province to arrest and educate the polluters," he said. But this is a tiny corner crack. "There are still social polluters, cultures and religions that are polluting online."
He continued, "I would like to ask the Ministry of Information, the Ministry of Culture and the Ministry of Cult to shut down their page and crack down on social polluters, such as magicians, astrologers, sex sellers, tonics sellers and those who talk about shame." "Open because all these stories are published in public, it affects children and boys very much."
