Heavy rains cause flooding in Sydney, flooding roads and forcing thousands to evacuate
Sydney: Australian authorities on Thursday said heavy rains were pounding the country's east coast, leading to flash floods in Sydney. Instructed residents to evacuate at some locations, warning of more rain throughout the day. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Thursday, April 7, 2022.
Residents of a nursing home were evacuated overnight as emergency services urged 5 million people in Sydney to avoid unnecessary travel and prepare for evacuation. So far, Sydney rainfall has risen to 1,226.8 mm, more than the annual average of 1,213 mm.
The Australian Meteorological Agency has confirmed that Bondi, the most popular tourist destination in Sydney, has recorded about 170 mm of rain in the last 24 hours and in the next 24 hours. In Sydney it could rise to 180 millimeters.
Summer on Australia's east coast is dominated by La Nina, which is usually associated with a two-year rise in rainfall.
