(Phnom Penh): 38 roads and some other infrastructure in Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province, built under the national budget of about 150 million US dollars were officially inaugurated under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. April 4, 2022 ago.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the 38 roads and infrastructure in Siem Reap are the result of the peace and efforts of the whole Cambodian nation, and these roads and infrastructure were built by pure Khmer ideas, skills and strength. Budget.
The 38 roads, infrastructure and improvement of the Siem Reap River will not only become a new energy for tourism in this province, cultural tourism, historical tourism, but also become a life force for the people of Siem Reap. People in Siem Reap from all walks of life expressed their happiness, smiles and closed their mouths.
They expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for deciding to give a large historical gift to the people of Siem Reap. The people of Siem Reap also thanked Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara and Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and all the construction team who worked together to build these achievements to make Siem Reap more beautiful. .
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, said that the 38 road construction projects with a total length of 108.74 km were built in accordance with each type of road:
* Type 1 road: A road in a tourist area with a lot of roads and good pavement, repaired by paving concrete, AC rubber, thickness from 5 cm to 7 cm.
* Type 2 road: A road in a tourist area with a lot of bad roads, was rebuilt by pouring 20 cm thick reinforced concrete and 7 cm thick AC rubber concrete.
* Type 3 road: It is not in the area with many tourists, it is rebuilt with 20 cm thick reinforced concrete.
* Type 4 road: It is an inter-city road with the road section with the best road body being repaired and paved with AC rubber, while the road section with bad road structure is rebuilt by reinforced concrete pavement. 25 cm thick.
The project was technically inspected by an inter-ministerial working group for monitoring and evaluation, and nine other inter-ministerial technical teams stationed at the site. The project cost nearly $ 150 million as a national budget package approved by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
These 38 roads are designed with meticulous standards, technical specifications and roadmaps, and the distribution of priority lanes in accordance with the urban landscape, which is consistent with urban water and forest and ancient temples. In line with the Siem Reap Municipal Land Use Master Plan and the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan Vision 2035.
In addition, the project also added flood protection systems to prevent flooding in the city, sidewalks, lighting poles, traffic lights, cable networks, transmission lines, sidewalks, roads for the disabled, bicycle lanes, parking lots, signs. Traffic, security cameras, gardens and tree planting on the streets.
In addition, through this new infrastructure, Siem Reap will be the most suitable destination for major national festivals and important international meetings. Watch the video! Help to Cure: DC-Cam Project "Promoting the Rights and Rehabilitation of Khmer Rouge Survivors" (Video inside)
