(Phnom Penh): Currently, according to the report of the General Department of Immigration, there are 46 cases of refugees and asylum seekers, 80 people are living in Cambodia.
The report presented at the meeting to review the work results in 2021 and the direction on April 6, 2022 confirmed that among the above people, there are 37 cases of refugees, 64 people. (15 females) of 8 nationalities and 9 cases of asylum seekers 16 people (8 females) of 6 nationalities.
In addition, there are 8 cases of asylum seekers who have been demoted as Vietnamese Montagnards, 12 people (2 females) living in Cambodia. While the Asia Foundation staff are Afghans and their families are staying in Cambodia, there are 46 families, 195 people (101 females).
It should be informed that due to the economic crisis, there is a movement to flee to safer places and places to get a better life. Although Cambodia was not the destination of the refugees, they chose Europe as their final destination, but Cambodia was still the first destination to receive refugee status for the next destination.
Therefore, the General Department of Immigration has always taken strict measures to monitor information on the refugee movement in the world as well as in the region in order to prevent and deal with foreigners who wish to seek asylum in Cambodia.
