Ministry of Labor: Negotiations between protesters and NagaWorld have not yet reached an agreement, April 21 meeting resumes
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training issued a notification on the progress of joint labor dispute resolution at NagaWorld on April 6, 2022.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor, obtained by Fresh News, the Ministry has continued to mediate joint labor disputes at NagaWorld in accordance with the roles set out in the law, as well as in the spirit of the workers' representatives. Employees who want to negotiate with the company.
1: Hope that there will be a light for resolving this dispute and still maintain the position of claiming to return to work.
3. Request the Labor Inspector to explain the termination of joint employment in accordance with Article 95 of the Labor Law.
5. Request the relevant institutions to waive the charges against all workers' representatives.
1: Thank the Chairman of the meeting, officials of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and officials of Phnom Penh Capital Administration and all members of the meeting.
2: For today's meeting, the company would like to officially respond to the letter of the union submitted to the company on March 23. The company maintains the same position as stated in the previous meeting. The company reads the contents of the company's official response letter to the union requesting that the company reinstate the remaining 200 workers.
3. The company submits a response letter to the union side and copies it to the General Secretariat of the Commission for resolving strikes and demonstrations in all areas.
4: The company still maintains a position of resolving disputes amicably with the union, and the company requests that the union should come up with a solution that is more feasible than its current proposal for the company to consider and study whether the company can accept or not. In addition to the response of the representatives of the employers, the Labor Inspector explained the principles and contents of Article 95 of the Labor Law to both parties again.
After vigorous discussions, both sides agreed as follows:
1: The two sides have not yet reached an agreement.
2. Set the date for the next meeting on Thursday, April 21, 2022 at 14:30 so that both parties have the opportunity to reconsider the possibility of mutual concessions that may lead to the conclusion of this dispute.
The Ministry also stated that although no agreement has been reached, the Ministry will continue to work to mediate and set the next meeting date in accordance with the role set by law as well as the demands of the parties.
Once again, the Ministry requested the two sides to have a high level of understanding in resolving this labor dispute, to continue to work closely with the competent authorities and relevant parties peacefully, and to maintain security and public order.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng orders to strengthen the control of foreigners and immediately expel all nationalities in case of illegal entry
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, reminded as well as ordered the special immigration police force along the border to strengthen control over the entry and exit of foreigners and in case of entry without a permit or stay without The custom is to arrest and deport immediately, regardless of nationality.
In the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results in 2021 and raise the direction of the General Department of Immigration on the afternoon of April 6, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng affirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia in general and the General Department of Immigration. Successfully carry out the work of confiscating illegally held documents from foreigners, so that illegal residence must not be recurred.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated, "Strict measures must be taken regularly and no one should be allowed to live illegally in Cambodia." This is a very important issue, we have launched a campaign to solve this problem, so we assume that those who come without paperwork is illegal. If it is illegal, we must arrest them according to Cambodian law. ”
At this point, Prince Sar Kheng stressed that all officials must not conspire with all illegal immigrants and must apply equally to all nationalities, that is, illegally, must apply the same law. . In addition, the prince also advised all officials not to leave this problem until it leads to difficulties in solving it.
Samdech Krala Hom stated, "Let the border authorities, the border police commissioner, the border police inspector, adhere to this principle so that we know how many foreigners are living in our area legally and if there are any illegal ones." "It must be dealt with according to the deportation measures from Cambodia in accordance with the procedures in force."
At the same time, Prince Sar Kheng expressed his happiness when foreigners received permanent residence permits and expired. Samdech emphasizes that in the case of those who have received a residence permit and expired, it is the same as living illegally, so legal action must be taken, such as eviction.
According to the report of General Kiet Chantharith, Director General of the General Department of Immigration, foreigners who have applied for recognition and permanent residence permit until the deadline (June 30, 2019), the census campaign And confiscated 28,945 families of 89,786 irregular administrative documents.
