Citizens Criticize Some Individuals Who Parked on Siem Reap Riverside Park
(Siem Reap): Some Siem Reap residents have criticized and expressed dissatisfaction with the actions of some individuals who took vehicles such as motorbikes and parked them on a newly prepared park at the foot of the Siem Reap River.
A few photos were posted on social media showing youths and motorbikes on a sidewalk in the middle of a park in the Siem Reap Rock River Bridge area. These activities upset some members of the public, claiming that the roads and parks, which were inaugurated on April 4, were used by motorcyclists to disrupt the environment.
Ny Thayu, a resident of Siem Reap City, said that doing so would be detrimental to the beauty and asked for vehicles to be parked at the parking lot provided by the authorities. He said that this act shows the lack of awareness of the people that they should cooperate with the authorities to organize the environment, order and hygiene in Siem Reap and maintain those properties for a long time.
This issue also has a reaction from the Deputy Governor and President of the Union of Youth Federations of Siem Reap. Mr. Prak Sophoan wrote on his official Facebook page: "The river in Siem Reap is already beautiful and there is no need to add decor. Please join to keep the walkway as planned."
It should be noted that in the past, the Siem Reap Provincial Authority has made great efforts to organize this environmental order and has set up a working group to implement this work. For example, people have been instructed not to park their vehicles on bicycles and park on the sidewalk that is not a parking lot. However, there is still chaos, street vendors are still numerous, especially in the Old Market area, as people are not yet aware of this problem and the lack of strict procedures.
