* Fourth: Promoting the implementation of safe village, commune and sangkat policies. The 7th Anti-Drug Campaign Plan and the Royal Government's Campaign Plans, especially the Implementation of the Inter-Institutional Plan (Interior-National Defense-NEC) on the Protection of the Annual Voter Registration And elections from 2022-2024
* Fifth: Continue to strengthen the management mechanism, lead the force and monitor the professional work in their respective jurisdictions, in which the principles of enhancing the capacity and quality of the law enforcement force must be implemented, with the encouragement, support, as well as strengthening Discipline, ethics, work attitude in serving the people
* Sixth: Continue to strengthen and expand cooperation with ministries, institutions, competent authorities and cooperation partners both inside and outside the country.
Chhay Sophal's study: Phnom Penh residents use Facebook for political participation and elections
(Phnom Penh): At the Royal Academy of Cambodia this morning, August 6, 2022, candidate Dr. Chhay Sophal presented the results of a study on the influence of Facebook in Cambodian politics. The case study was conducted in Phnom Penh (between 2008 and 2021), with the first results focusing on "the use of Facebook by Phnom Penh residents for political participation and elections."
Please note that the study also found answers on the quality of Internet and mobile services in Phnom Penh, including coverage, speed, stability of supply and price.
To be gender-based, the study also selected 30% of the global target population who live and live in Phnom Penh, and they are 18 years of age and older and have a primary education level. To Ph.D. This is according to the presentation of the PhD candidate.
Regarding Facebook as a arena for competition between politicians and politicians, the results show that the global target model is up to 71.4% or 357 people and the correct answer. In addition, the global target model is 86.8% or 434 people, and people have stated that Facebook is a bridge between politicians and citizens or voters. In addition, 60.8% or 304 people received political messages through Facebook.
In addition, the majority of Facebook users are 55.2% or 276 people, and 38.6% or 193 people like to follow the country's political affairs, and the number of occasional followers, which means more than half of Facebook users. Likes to follow politics in the country.
Candidate Dr. concludes that due to the influence of Facebook, politicians have used it as a platform to compete for popularity and seek support from voters, while voters in Cambodia have also changed their attitude to participate in politics, especially political debates. Understanding the value of the ballot and going to the polls to elect a leader they trust.
At the same time, PhD candidate also urged Facebook users, especially those in political interests, including political supporters, political activists and political leaders, to adhere to and strengthen political ethics without using Facebook as a battlefield. Dead or alive.
