The report also called on Cambodia to diversify its economy to promote sustainable growth.
He said Cambodia, which used to focus on the production and export of garments, travel and footwear, could benefit from the diversification of light industries such as bicycles, electronics and wiring products. "This diversification will make the economy more resilient to crises of foreign demand."
