General knowledge: Which doctor found the antidote for rabies?
(World): Rabies is a terrible infectious disease for the previous generation because it often makes patients suffer more and more until they die of asphyxia and there is no cure. It was not until the end of the 19th century that a doctor in Europe discovered the antidote for rabies to be used for effective treatment. * Do you know which doctor discovered the most important drug? This?
The doctor named Louis Pasteur (Louis Pasteur) since the discovery of many achievements in the field of medicine, especially the discovery of drugs against rabies, he became a famous French doctor. He is also known for his research on microorganisms and as a scientist in chemistry.
Since then, Louis Pasteur has gained a reputation throughout Europe, since the successful rescue of the above child masters. Despite this fame, Pasteur worked in the laboratory until old age because he was eager to save the people of the world.
On Pastor's 70th birthday, many European scientists traveled to Paris to pay their respects. Two years later, Louis Pasteur died on September 28, 1895, at the age of 72.
Denmark expels 15 Russian diplomats for espionage
During a meeting of the Council on Foreign Policy on Tuesday, Danish Foreign Minister Jeppe Kofod announced the expulsion of 15 Russian diplomats, accusing them of being "intelligence officials." "Secrets." This is according to the release by Xinhua on Tuesday, April 5, 2022.
According to a press release from the Russian Embassy in Denmark, Vladimir Babin was previously informed of the dismissal of "intelligence officers working at the Russian Embassy in Copenhagen, Denmark".
The Danish Ministry of Foreign Affairs has stated that the expelled officials have 14 days to leave their country.
The Russian embassy in Denmark has denied the allegations, claiming they were aimed at further damaging relations between the two countries.
