Readers' views: What are the real intentions of the former NagaWorld employees?
It is known that the cause of the labor dispute is due to the crisis of the spread of Kovid 19 disease, which requires the company to reduce the number of employees to maintain the social safety gap in accordance with health rules and to solve the financial crisis in the company. Also.
After the company laid off workers on the workers' side, some female union leaders, including those who revolted, demanded that the dismissed employees return to work, despite being rejected by the company due to the company. Agreed to pay compensation according to the decision of the Arbitration Council, but the protesters are still protesting to the implementation of the rule of law.
What is the real intention of the NagaWorld protesters to continue to gather illegally and illegally on such public streets?
Although the order was not binding, the former NagaWorld employees, especially the union leaders, did not honor their contracts and even expressed their intention to disobey the law and used the strike to force the company, the Ministry of Labor and the authorities to The authority accepts its terms unilaterally.
The illegal leadership of the demonstration movement was assessed by analysts and saw the hypocrisy and political character of the protesters as follows:
1: Refusal to accept the decision of the Arbitration Council is the malicious intent of the former employees of NagaWorld to raise disputes and unwillingness to resolve labor disputes.
2. The continuation of illegal demonstrations shows the intention to push the problem bigger to serve political interests rather than to accept a solution in accordance with the principles of law and also shows non-compliance with its contract.
3. The leaders of this anarchic demonstration movement also admitted that they had received financial support from some local civil society groups to support the demonstrations. In addition, according to information leaked on social media, the protesters were training foreign protest tactics, including pro-foreign demonstrations.
4. Illegal protesters have created violent clashes with the intention of distorting public opinion by accusing the authorities of abusing the protesters.
5. Illegal demonstrations also aim to tarnish the image of the Royal Government, while Cambodia is chairing the ASEAN rotating presidency for 2022. Moreover, the continuation of the demonstration is also intended to intimidate tourists not to come to Cambodia, while the head of the Royal Government announced the normal reopening of the socio-economic.
6: This illegal demonstration movement may also be the intention of anti-government politicians to use the protesters to undermine the stability of the 5th mandate Commune / Sangkat Council elections scheduled at the time. In the near future, these politicians will accuse the election environment of being so threatening, gloomy, and insecure that they can use various excuses to criticize the election process.
In general, the dispute between the company boss and a small group of former employees is almost settled under the labor law, and if the remaining protesters do not succumb to the incitement of some union leaders, they should be. Benefit by receiving appropriate compensation in accordance with the labor law and the opportunity to move to a new workplace to better support the family.
Finding a new job or a new job is actually better than being enslaved by illegal demonstrations, serving the leaders of pro-political unions and opposition politicians, who often use the sweat of workers' blood as a political treadmill by inciting workers to anger. Only their power ambitions.
