90 Infantry Visits Koh Thmor Document Center, Tbong Khmum Province
(Tbong Khmum): The Victory Monument team led 90 trainees of the Army to visit Koh Thmor Document Center, Tbong Khmum Province on April 4, 2022.
To begin with, Mr. Long Dany, Director of the Koh Thmor Documentation Center, told the participants that the Koh Thmor Documentation Center was established on the initiative of General Nem Sovath, Special Adviser to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and Director General. General Department of Politics and Foreign Affairs, Ministry of National Defense and Mr. Youk Chhang, Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia.
The Koh Thmor Documentation Center was launched to the public on June 20, 2020 under the close collaboration between the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Ministry of National Defense and the Documentation Center of Cambodia for the following purposes:
As a follow-up, Mr. Long Dany led the participants to visit the photo exhibition left over from the 1960s to the 1990s. The photos include photos of historical events in Cambodia, starting from Koh Thmor, Tonlong commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province and Snuol district, Kratie province.
Photograph of the Democratic Kampuchea regime (1975-1979), which killed an estimated 2 million Cambodians. Some photographic evidence of the Khmer Rouge's crimes against the Cambodian people. The painting depicts the road to the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot on June 20, 1977, and lastly, the photograph on the beginning of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy in the 1990s and its acceptance. Full peace was achieved in 1998.
Mr. Pheng Pong Rasy, Director of the Genocide Education Program of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, also presented key historical events during the Democratic Kampuchea regime (1975-1979), the definition of genocide, crimes against humanity, and war crimes in order to prevent crime. Cruelty is happening again in Cambodia and around the world.
At the end, Mr. Pheng Pong Rasy screened two documentaries for the trainees to watch: a documentary on Comrade Hun Sen's trip to Vietnam to mobilize forces to fight against the Pol Pot genocidal regime in June 20, 1977 and another film, The Heritage and Establishment of the Cambodian National Salvation Front on December 2, 1978.
Mr. Pheng Pong Rasy also explained to all trainees the importance of preventing genocide and the effects of genocide as an individual, family, community and society as a whole.
Brigadier General Khem Bona, Deputy Chief of Staff of the Army, said that when he came to visit this great historical study, seeing the concrete evidence and photos of this history made him excited and heartbroken to remember the merits of Samdech Techo Hun. Sen who used his life as capital to liberate the country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Similarly, Lieutenant Chun Sothy, who works at the 5th Infantry Division, expressed his excitement at visiting the Koh Thmor Documentation Center, a military historical site that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and four other comrades had visited. Leave for Vietnam to gather strength and seek help from Vietnam to liberate our country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Lieutenant Chun Sothy was also pleased that the Victory Monument team and the Documentation Center of Cambodia organized a welcoming and clear presentation of a series of photographs and the road to the overthrow of the Pol Pot genocidal regime on June 20, 1977 Kandal Provincial Governor Visits Students and Donates Humanitarian Donations to New Smile Association of Children's Hope in Kandal Stung District
