National Institute of Science, Technology and Innovation signs MoU with Thak Global Institute to enhance technological capabilities and growth of the digital economy
(Phnom Penh): The National Institute of Science, Technology and Innovation has signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with Thak Global Institute under the chairmanship of Prof. Dr. Chhem Keat Rithy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary of State, Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation.
The MoU is a joint venture between 1: Thak Global Institute student internships, 2: Digital literacy initiatives, and 3: Future collaborations that enhance technological capabilities. And the growth of the digital economy.
In the near future, Thak Global Institute will also have undergraduate and postgraduate courses focusing on the latest technological innovations.
To achieve this vision, Thak Global Institute has also partnered with educational institutions and private companies to integrate into the field of technology and innovation in order to expand across Cambodia and the region. So far, Thak Global Institute has a total of 15 public and private partners and intends to cooperate with 22 more institutions in 2022-2023.
There are two types of partners of Thak Global Institute, the first type is public and private institutions that focus on internships, job opportunities for students, partners in technology, ecological partnerships and sustainable partnerships. Another type of partnership is educational institutions that focus on joint diplomas, joint curriculum development, and general cooperation.
The Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation was authorized by Royal Decree dated March 26, 2020 to fulfill the mission of the Royal Government on the leadership and management of the science, technology and innovation industries, including handicrafts. And clean water of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Thak Global Institute was established in 2019 with the support of a group of Japanese businessmen and managed by young Cambodian intellectual leaders, with the support and guidance of senior individuals from the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation. As well as the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
