(Phnom Penh): Telecom Cambodia on April 5, 2022 issued a notice to the public on the failure to provide services to customers using mobile phones and Internet in the northeast corner of the Olympic Market due to an unknown person. Stealing and destroying the FTTH network of Telecom Cambodia.
According to the announcement, the failure to provide services was caused by an unknown person who immediately broke into the telecommunications FTTH network. In order to ensure the efficiency of the supply of telecommunication services, Cambodia has repaired and replaced some equipment to reconnect the network to customers.
The case of hacking and destroying the telecommunication cable network of Cambodia is an act that violates the law, causing damage to Telecom Cambodia and customers failing to earn national budget.
Telecom Cambodia would like to ask all customers to cooperate in providing information and providing pictures on the theft of cable network so that the authorities can punish the perpetrators according to the law in force. Please contact: Mr. Hun Pros 012 873 121, Mr. Sothy Soth 017 597 576 and Mr. Tep Kosal 089 662 356.
Read the full Telecom announcement: Senior Minister Ly Thuch shares his experience and leadership in the field of mine action in Cambodia to the Philippine Mine Action Delegation
(Phnom Penh): On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Action Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Action Authority, this morning, April 5, 2022, shared his experience and leadership in the field of mine action in Cambodia. To the Mine Action Delegation of the Philippines and Stakeholders at the Philippine Mine Action Stakeholder Workshop hosted by Cambodia.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Senior Minister informed the workshop that Cambodia, with its Mine Action Authority as its staff, is strongly committed to this cooperation and is ready to support mine action efforts in the region. Not only during this year, which is the year of Cambodia's ASEAN chairmanship, but at all times.
The Senior Minister said that in 2012, Cambodia, as the chair of ASEAN, initiated the idea of establishing an ASEAN Regional Center for Mine Action, recognizing that maintaining human security is an important part of the ASEAN Community-building efforts. Strive to ensure that all ASEAN Member States and all sectors of society benefit from this process.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister commended the commitment of all stakeholders to provide greater cooperation in the region and work closely with the continuation of the mine action mission to promote safety and help the vulnerable. Affected by explosive remnants of war.
