(Tbong Khmum): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen has generously donated the suffix for the completion of the temple at Wat Baray and also painted in this temple at Wat Baray to be considered an achievement in Buddhism, which is the building of merit. Every Buddhist.
It should be noted that Wat Baray is located in Baray village, Chhouk commune, Krouch Chhmar district, Tbong Khmum province. The temple of this pagoda was built since 2016 and until 2020, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen also joined in to complete the construction of this temple. To date, the construction of the temple at Wat Baray has been completed, but the painting of the temple is not yet complete.
On the occasion of his visit to his hometown on April 3, 2022, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen also visited Ampovorn pagoda, also known as Wat Svay Damnak, to pay homage to Venerable Teng He, Preah Balat, Tbong Khmum province. And already the chief abbot of Wat Ampovan. It is this village that has left behind the memories of the young and educated age of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, the humanitarian mother of the Khmer nation.
At the same time, the Chief Bishop of Wat Ampovan also had a decree on painting in Wat Baray Temple, located in Baray Village, Chhouk Commune. Currently, additional suffixes are needed to complete the painting. The pagoda workers and the Buddhists at Wat Baray also have a priest requesting Samdech Kittipritthbandit to help in this work in a generous way.
In the atmosphere of a beautiful resort, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen also offered additional suffixes through Teng He to participate in the painting in Wat Baray to be considered an achievement in Buddhism and for the people. It is easy for Buddhists to celebrate various festivals in pagodas as well as in temples.
Venerable Vinh Teng He said that the suffix, which is the generosity of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, is for painting on the ceiling of Wat Baray, which has a total area of 325 square meters.
The abbot of Wat Ampovan said that the suffixes used for the completion of the temple and the painting in the temple of Wat Baray totaled 100,000 (one hundred thousand) dollars.
