Giant Doll Project to Hold Parade on April 13
(Siem Reap): The giant toy project organized by the Governor of Banteay Srei District is planned to hold a parade on April 13 during the upcoming New Year.
Banteay Srei district administration official said that the giant toy project is scheduled to officially hold a parade on April 13, 2022 on the road in Preah Dak village to show to the public.
Earlier, Mr. Khim Finang, Governor of Banteay Srei District, announced that this giant toy was organized by the district administration and the team. The giant puppet project was originally planned to celebrate the 24th National Cultural Day and International Women's Day. But the project was halted due to the outbreak of Kovid.
The giant doll is made of rattan, bamboo, colored paper and has built-in lights inside, as well as a wheelbarrow for the parade. The dolls come in a variety of shapes, including a tiger representing the Year of the Dragon, a puppet show, the perfect woman of Banteay Srei, an endangered whisper, a lizard, a dragon, a noodle seller, a palmist and Sweet cucumber fruit.
According to Khim Finang, these giant puppets are artistic comics with gestures that create a happy atmosphere for the audience.
