Cambodian-Vietnamese police agree to crack down on all kinds of crimes at the border and provide information to each other, especially drug offenses
(Mondulkiri): The Mondulkiri Provincial Police and the Dak Lak Provincial Police of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam held a meeting to review the Union and the results of cooperation in the prevention and suppression of crime at the border in 2020-2021 and to set further directions. .
The meeting was held on April 4, 2022, with the Cambodian side led by Major General Lor Sokha, Mondulkiri Provincial Police Commissioner, on behalf of General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, and the Vietnamese side led by Brigadier General Le Vinh Quy. Dak Lak Provincial Police Commissioner. The meeting took place at the Mondulkiri Provincial Police.
At the beginning of the meeting, Lt. Gen. Lor Sokha opened the meeting and allowed Lt. Col. Mom In, Director of the Office of Consolidation and Analysis, to read a brief report on cooperation in crime prevention along the border between the two provinces. From Mondulkiri and Dak Lak provinces: Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
In 2020 and 2021, with the outbreak of 19 cases of Kovid, the rapid and complex evolution of our entire world, in part, greatly affected the crime prevention cooperation between the police commissioners. Mondulkiri Province and Dak Lak Provincial Police.
The two sides agreed to continue to effectively implement the annual cooperation plan between the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia and the Ministry of Police of Vietnam, signed by the leaders of the two ministries, and to continue to strictly implement the content of cooperation, prevention and Crack down on crimes in the border areas agreed upon by the two provincial police commissioners.
Continuing the exchange of information on the security situation, border order, such as leverage activities and international business organizations, as well as the activities of each country violating the law. Illegal areas, economic crimes, trafficking in women and children, and transnational drug trafficking crimes in the past.
According to the report, the two sides cooperated well with the relevant authorities, the owners took control of the relevant situation, found in a timely manner and informed each other in a timely manner about the crime situation in order to cooperate effectively in the prevention and suppression. And on time.
After that, Brigadier General Le Vinh Quy agreed to the request of the Cambodian side and mentioned the bonds of solidarity and cooperation between the Mondulkiri Provincial Police Commission and the police officers of Dak Lak Province (Socialist Republic of Vietnam). The two have always had a good relationship with each other in preventing crime along the border line between the two provinces, which are also villagers.
In an atmosphere of closeness, solidarity, friendship and mutual understanding, the two sides continued to discuss and agree on 12 cooperation points for 2020-2021 in the cooperation between the two commissions. The police of the two provinces and some other remaining issues and plan to do so in the future.
