Samdech Techo Hun Sen Recommends 5 Points to Promote Support for Cambodian Products: Preserve the National Economy
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Honorary Chairman of the National Committee for the Promotion of One Village, One Product, made five recommendations for relevant ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations and the people to continue to work together to promote Use Khmer products. This is according to the message of Samdech Techo, which was received by Fresh News on April 4, 2022.
The five recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen include:
First, the National Committee for the Promotion of One Village, One Product Movement, the Ministry of Commerce and relevant ministries and institutions must continue to cooperate and coordinate with each other smoothly in order to promote the use of Cambodian products, continue to widely disseminate Cambodian products and continue to provide skills. To manufacturers on the production process, quality improvement, product safety, processing and packaging to meet the domestic and foreign markets.
Second, the National Committee for Promoting the Movement of One Village, One Product, the Committee for Promoting One Village, One Product, the Capital-Provinces throughout the country and the Ministry of Commerce must cooperate with the private sector to organize online marketing to help Cambodian products to buy, sell and present at product exhibition events. Both at home and abroad and at Cambodian representative offices abroad.
Third, the National Committee for the Promotion of One Village, One Product Movement and the Ministry of Commerce must cooperate with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation so that the Cambodian representative abroad can promote Cambodian products at various events, especially linking the work to promote the One Village One Product movement. A product in Cambodia within the framework of regional cooperation under the coordination of the ASEAN Secretariat.
