(Phnom Penh): A group of more than 60 former students of Prek Pra Krom Primary School, led by Mr. Prum Sros, organized a meeting for teachers during the 80s-90s who used to teach them from a young age to commemorate the teachers who Has worked hard to teach from a young age. This program was held at Prek Pra Krom Primary School in Sangkat Prek Pra, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh on April 3, 2022.
On this occasion, Mr. Prum Sros, Team Leader, said that he misses and appreciates all the teachers who used to teach them when they were young, which is a strong pillar for them to learn and teach. Having good morals, good children, good children, good students and growing up with different abilities and skills, so he had the idea to gather all the friends who used to go to school together at that time to organize gatherings and sponsor food and budget. .
At the same time, the classmates who came to participate, including: Mr. Nil Borey, Mr. Kuon Neang Rith, Ms. Ros Sokhom and Ms. Mak Srey Mom shared the same interest around thanking the teacher who is their second parent and wanted Set a good example for all young people and the younger generation to know the value of teachers and be grateful to them with kindness.
At the same time, Mr. Sieng Hok and Ms. Hoeung Ly also expressed their surprise and excitement that the alumni who taught them were grateful and appreciative of the teachers who worked hard to teach them from a young age. The good spirit of our Cambodian children will be a great example for the next generation of students.
