Access to Finance for SMEs and Women Entrepreneurs Launched
The launch of this program aims to target 50% of women entrepreneurs to receive financing from participating financial institutions and capacity building, including training on working capital management, especially understanding of microfinance financial statements. And medium. In addition, entrepreneurs participating in this program will receive technical assistance in preparing financial statements and developing the financial system.
Oknha Pech Bolen, Executive Vice President of the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association, stated that the program will contribute to increasing access to quality official financial services and support better access to financing for micro, small and medium enterprises, and especially women entrepreneurs in Cambodia. Cambodia.
He said that today's program will be a forum to connect financial institutions, small and medium enterprises and especially women entrepreneurs to meet and discuss the needs related to the program access to finance.
"We need to work together to support entrepreneurs, including the approximately 350,000 women entrepreneurs in Cambodia, to address the challenges they are facing, especially the lack of collateral to obtain loans," she said. .
She said women entrepreneurs in micro and small enterprises should be more focused.
Dr. Chea Serey, Assistant Governor and Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the "Access to Finance" program will definitely contribute to improving the financial environment for micro-enterprises, which are the backbone. Of the national economy.
She encouraged banks and financial institutions to focus on lending to small and medium enterprises, considering the possibility of repayment rather than collateral.
