(Siem Reap): Mr. Tek Reth Samrech, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers, emphasized that the current Siem Reap Airport will be suspended after the new airport opens at the end of 2023.
Responding to a question from a reporter from Fresh News on Sunday morning, April 3, 2022, Mr. Tek Reth Samrech, who is the Chairman of the Orientation Committee for the Construction of Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport, said that Siem Reap Airport is being used. Currently, it is only about 2,500 meters from Angkor Thom. This distance is a bad consequence and also threatens to endanger the ancient temples.
According to Tek Reth, the International Committee for the Coordination of the Protection and Development of the Angkor Historic Site (ICC-Angkor) has expedited the construction of the new Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport. Old Airport.
Currently, under the investment of a Chinese company with a capital of about 880 million US dollars, Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport is under construction on an area of about 700 hectares in Kriel Pong village, Popel commune and Praval village, Tayek commune, Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province. . The airport is about 50 km from downtown Siem Reap and 40 km from the Angkor site, which does not affect the heritage site.
Regarding the location of the airport has an impact on the temple or not, Mr. Tek Reth Samrech confirmed that "this site we discussed from the beginning in 2004, 2005 to the UNESCO archeology experts that the place can be done. So we set up that place.
Mr. Tek Reth Samrech confirmed that the construction process of Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport will be completed as planned without any obstacles. Regarding passengers entering and leaving the airport, Mr. Tek Reth Samrech expressed his expectation that in addition to tourists, there are also investors coming to invest in Siem Reap.
On the occasion of inspecting the progress of the construction of Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport on the morning of April 3, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen called the presence of the airport on the battlefield as a result of peace and fruit. From the good cooperation between Cambodia and China.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also praised the investment of Chinese companies as a very beneficial investment for Cambodia, Samdech likened the Chinese investment to the use of flour to make cakes for Cambodians to eat.
According to Tek Reth, in addition to investing in the airport, the company will also invest in a commercial area near the airport, and the project also includes the construction of an expressway for access to Siem Reap. The Deputy Prime Minister also expects that through the investment in the construction of the airport, it will attract local investors to invest in the area around the airport, which will turn this quiet area into a vibrant commercial area.
