(Siem Reap): After spending many hours traveling by car from Phnom Penh to Siem Reap on Saturday afternoon, April 2, 2022, under the incessant rain, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia Inspected 38 roads in Siem Reap, an achievement built with a national budget of about 150 million US dollars.
The procession inspected by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, accompanied by Deputy Prime Minister Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Minister of Defense, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, and Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport. Transport, as well as a number of other government officials, traveled along the prepared roads from one road to another for many roads.
The rehabilitation and improvement of the Siem Reap River is carried out in accordance with the standards and regulations of UNESCO and the International Committee for the Coordination of the Protection and Development of the Angkor Historic Site (ICC-Angkor).
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also inspected the construction of a port on the banks of the Siem Reap River, which is a place for boating, and also met with the community of boat operators, carrying about 91 boats and provided some funds. They, too.
It is noteworthy that during the visit to inspect the infrastructure system in Siem Reap, the presence of Samdech Techo was warmly welcomed by the people living on the streets in Siem Reap. They handed out greetings with a smiling face as a sign of joy and happiness for the high presence of Samdech Techo, the national leader, who always holds high for the destiny of the nation and the people.
The construction of the 38 roads has received high attention from the construction team and has worked day and night to achieve the planned plan in just one year. In addition, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara and Senior Minister Sun Chanthol regularly inspected the construction process to ensure that the construction went as planned and ensured the quality of construction.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the construction of 38 road infrastructure projects in Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province, including the construction of paved roads with reinforced concrete, paved roads with concrete (AC), sewerage system, rainwater - sewage. Pavement and granite flooring work is 100% completed as planned from December 29, 2021.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also said that with the construction of this road, the Ministry has also set up a large wastewater treatment system with high capacity to filter wastewater. At the same time, Samdech Techo Prime Minister allowed people to connect 12,299 sewage system from rainwater and sewage from home with the main sewer system of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport for free as a precious bond. To the people of Siem Reap.
Please be reminded that this project to improve road infrastructure in Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province, 38 lines with a total length of 106.42 km, using a total national budget of more than 149,216,595 US dollars. Of that, 9 million US dollars will be spent on the construction of rainwater and sewage systems outside the construction of 38 roads.
