(Pursat): Pursat Provincial Administration held a meeting to disseminate the decision on the establishment of a sub-committee and working group to prevent and suppress fisheries crimes in the flooded forest area of Tonle Sap Lake in Pursat province. The meeting was chaired by Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Pursat Province.
Provincial Administration Director, Director of Provincial Environment Department, Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, Director of Finance, Director of Inter-sectoral Management, Krakor District Governor, Kandieng District Governor and Bakan District Governor are members. The Director of Fisheries Administration is a permanent member, the Director of the Office of Legal Affairs and Public Safety is the secretary.
In that, 3 working groups were formed to investigate, prevent and suppress fisheries crimes in the flooded forest area of Tonle Sap Lake, the first group led by Mr. Liv Seng Him, Krakor District Governor, the second group led by Mr. Chhay Kimmong Kandieng District Governor and the third group led by Mr. Pay Leng, Bakan District Governor.
In addition, Mr. Chiao Tai asked each team to inspect, research and prevent fishing crimes that use all kinds of illegal equipment. Investigate and identify the perpetrators of the crime and send them to court according to legal procedures. For equipment sellers, the first offense: must be disseminated, second: the introduction of the contract and the third: must follow the law.
