(Phnom Penh): The Samdech Mey Library welcomed the new Ambassador of the French Republic to the Kingdom of Cambodia, Mr. Jacques Pellegrini, and Mr. Michael Kelly, Head of the Office of the French Ministry of Foreign Affairs, on the morning of April 1, 2022.
Samdech Mey Library is a Khmer house built during the French colonial period. The library contains documents from many sources, including a collection of documents in French. These French-language documents serve as an important resource because they are records of pre-war, post-war, and post-war events that require researchers to have knowledge of the French language in order to understand and gain access to them. All this information is complete.
His Majesty the King granted the use of his name as the name of the Samdech Mey Library, which is part of this luxurious building. The King expects that one day this building will appear.
During the visit, the distinguished guests and the Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia discussed a wide range of topics related to transitional justice and the functioning of the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia and what to do next. It should be recalled that the French Republic was a co-signatory to the establishment of the Khmer Rouge tribunal, which served as a fact-finding and justice mechanism for millions of survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime.
