Home Ministry Police Send Man to Court Over Land Fraud
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pov Socheat was arrested by the police force of the Ministry of Interior and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on Saturday morning, April 2, 2022. Mr. Pov Socheat was arrested by police on April 1 on charges related to fraud in a case of buying and selling two plots of land in Trapeang Mean village, Sangkat Kraing Thnong, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
According to a complaint filed with the Prosecutor's Office on December 16, 2021, on July 14, 2019, Pov Socheat used a ploy to buy land by lying that he had money. All amounts for the purchase of land in these two places.
The complaint states that after paying the deposit, Pov Socheat refused to pay the landowner under the real estate contract, despite the landlord's repeated favors. By. Moreover, Pov Socheat continued to use various fraudulent tactics to evade payment and even used other means to prevent landowners from reselling their land to others.
In the same complaint, the landowner stated that Pov Socheat did not have the money to buy her land, but just bought the land without paying the full amount and paid for all the means in order to Landowners lose money, miss investment in land, and lose time.
In addition, the landowner said that she had suffered a lot of injustice in the past and that she was outraged that this wicked man named Pov Socheat was so bad that he bought the land and not only refused to pay the full amount according to the conditions. The real estate contract also uses back-and-forth tactics to prevent landowners from selling or investing in the land, and has even sued landowners in the past.
The landowner said that because the court found the evidence and she had enough legal documents, the court executed the order to detain Pov Socheat.
