Cambodia wants to speed up direct flights from India to boost tourism flow
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia has requested the Government of the Republic of India through the Indian Embassy in Phnom Penh to further encourage the flow of tourists from India to Cambodia and to expedite the arrangement of direct flights from India to Cambodia. Support the attraction of tourists to Cambodia.
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon also urged the Indian side to expedite the arrangement of direct flights between Cambodia and India to support the flow of tourists from each other, but in the future should start from Arrange for a weekly flight to Phnom Penh or Siem Reap first.
Minister Thong Khon pledged that the Cambodian Ministry of Tourism would be happy to fully cooperate in this regard, including cooperation in arranging flight changes and connecting direct flights.
It should be informed that as there are currently no direct flights between the two countries, tourists and passengers traveling by air from India to Cambodia have to change flights in Thailand or Singapore before continuing to arrive in Cambodia. . Cambodia-India Implements Phat Sanday Community Development Project in Kampong Thom Province and Project for Community-Based Ecotourism App Development
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism and the Embassy of the Republic of India in Cambodia have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on two projects: the project to promote ecotourism activities in Phat Sanday community, Kampong Thom province, and the mobile app development project to promote Promote potential and products in tourism and ecotourism communities across the country.
Mr. Chuk Chumnor explained that the first project, the project to promote ecotourism activities in the Phat Sanday ecotourism community, the Indian Embassy supports the development of infrastructure into the Phat Sanday community and helps to establish a "floating market" as a product. New tourism in this ecotourism community will soon benefit the community.
Phat Sanday Ecotourism Community is a community on the surface of Tonle Sap Lake, located in Phat Sanday Commune, Kampong Svay District, Kampong Thom Province, but if tourists travel from Phnom Penh or the western provinces of Tonle Sap Lake, it is possible. You can also enter Chhnuk Trou area of Boribo district, Kampong Chhnang province.
According to Chuk Chumnor, in addition to the two QIP projects, the Ministry of Tourism and the Embassy of India are also preparing to sign a Memorandum of Understanding on "Project to Promote Ecotourism Activities in Boeung Sneh Bird Ecotourism Community in Prey Veng Province" next year. .
