Neak Oknha Kith Meng emphasized that in 2022, Cambodia is the host of ASEAN, which is a good year to promote Australia-ASEAN relations. As the Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, the Duke President invited Australian companies to support the ASEAN Business and Investment Summit to be organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce during the 2022 ASEAN Summit.
The ASEAN Business and Investment Summit will bring important topics to discuss and submit a report to the ASEAN Economic Ministers as well as ASEAN leaders. The duke asked Australia to help promote agriculture in terms of cultivation techniques, harvesting, processing and marketing, because Australia is a country with technology and expertise in agriculture.
At the same time, the Ambassador expressed support for the remarks made by the President and stated that the Australian Embassy has always supported the agricultural sector and has been developing new programs that support the entire supply chain in particular. Establishment of agro-industrial parks, promotion of product standards, sanitation, agricultural diversification and irrigation systems.
He noted that the past year has been a difficult one due to the effects of Kovid 19 and reminded of Wing Bank's involvement in sending money to the real poor affected by the crisis. By Kovid 19. He highlighted the potential for Australian companies to invest in renewable energy and gold mining in Mondulkiri, an example of Australian investment.
He welcomed the visit to Australia and said that from April 18, 2022, Australia will open its host country with 19 vaccinated vaccines without the need for Kovid test as before.
In particular, the Trade Commissioner expressed her intention to cooperate with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and learn about companies that are members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to explore the possibility of cooperating with Australian companies in the region and in neighboring countries.
She supported the organization of joint events and continued discussions on arrangements for visits to Australia, as well as other programs, including the organization of Cambodian-Australian agricultural missions.
It should be informed that the talks ended fruitfully in a friendly and fraternal atmosphere.
