Samdech Techo Hun Sen's remarks were made on the occasion that he allowed the Special Envoy of the United Nations Secretary-General for Myanmar to pay a courtesy call and discuss work at the Peace Palace on April 1. 2022.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, confirmed to the media that during the meeting, Ms. Nolin expressed her congratulations to Samdech Techo who had received the Peace Medal in Korea in the past and also congratulated. Recently, the Cambodian Peacekeeping Force received a medal from the United Nations.
She briefed Samdech Techo on the work she has done over the past three months as a special envoy of the UN Secretary-General, including consideration of resolving the Myanmar issue through the establishment of a multilateral framework based on a three-tiered framework. Contains:
Layer 1: At the center of the circle is the Myanmar-led and proprietary solution process, which reflects the will of the people of Myanmar.
The second layer is the process led by the regional community, which includes ASEAN and all countries bordering Myanmar.
And the third layer: the outermost layer, the international community, mostly the West.
Ms. Nolin added that the framework is not different from the five ASEAN consensus: first, focus on humanitarian aid, second, protection of the people, and third, return to civilian rule. It is necessary to build trust.
In response, Samdech Techo thanked Ms. Nolin for her congratulations on receiving the Peace Medal and the Cambodian Peacekeepers for receiving the UN Medal.
