Numbering of ballots for Commune / Sangkat Council Election reached 1,622 communes / sangkats
(Phnom Penh): The draw to determine the order on the ballots for the Commune / Sangkat Council Election of the 5th Mandate 2022 of the participating political parties has reached 1,622 communes / sangkats out of the total number of communes / sangkats. 1,652 nationwide as of March 30, 2022. This is according to the announcement of the provisional results of the NEC.
Out of the 25 provincial capitals, 15 provinces have completed the lottery to determine the number of candidates on the ballot paper of each commune / sangkat. These include: Battambang, Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Speu, Kampot, Kandal, Koh Kong, Kratie, Mondulkiri, Preah Vihear, Prey Veng, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, Stung Treng, Takeo, Kep, Pailin, Oddar Meanchey and Tbong Khmum.
According to the rules and procedures for the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election in 2022, after the first list of candidates becomes the official list of candidates, the NEC must draw lots to determine the order of the list of candidates on the public ballot. Retired monks or dignitaries or elders who are neutral and acceptable to all political parties.
The draw to determine the order of the list of candidates on the ballot is to enable the NEC to print the ballots for each commune based on the official list of candidates in that commune and the results of the draw.
