(Phnom Penh): The Oreang Ov District Assistance Team, Tbong Khmum Province, headed by Mr. Eang Sophalleth, has compiled a story to educate its local people on the clear distinction between merit and punishment, especially Doing their good deeds one day turns into the murder of those who have done good to themselves all their lives.
The owner of the noodle shop offered two bowls of noodles to fill the stomach. Hungry for power, the son, who ran away from home, expressed his gratitude to the owner of the noodle shop and thanked and considered the owner of the noodle shop as his greatest benefactor.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth pointed out that in our lives, it is sometimes easy to be grateful for the little things that others do to themselves, but forget the gratitude of parents and relatives around them for the rest of their lives.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth hopes that through this educational story, people will be able to think and clearly distinguish between merits and demerits, avoid making the wrong decision, throw away rice, grab rice husks, throw national leaders and capture them. You have been democratized.
