BEIJING: China has decided to restrict the issuance of visas to some US officials in response to similar measures imposed by Washington in March on allegations of human rights abuses. This is according to the release by the Russian news agency RT on Friday, April 1, 2022.
The Chinese spokesman claimed that the United States used false excuses of human rights abuses to interfere in China's internal affairs, defame Beijing and put pressure on Chinese officials. Wang stressed that such actions are a serious violation of the fundamental principles of international law as well as international relations.
So far, the Chinese Foreign Ministry has not confirmed exactly how many US officials will be subject to the new restrictions, but a spokesman said those who created the "lies" on rights issues. People will harm China's national interests, already know who they are.
The announcement comes after the State Department imposed visa restrictions on Chinese officials whom Washington has accused of intimidating and harassing human rights activists and dissidents. China and around the world.
What are the key points we should explore and be interested in around this labor dispute case?
2: Acting in violation of the contract and stubbornly refusing to accept legal mediation
The Ministry of Labor and the competent authorities have tried their best and have mediated several times to resolve the labor dispute at NAGA WORLD, but the protesters are not willing to resolve the issue. They continued to demonstrate in violation of the law and in violation of the contract, which claimed to be released on bail, which all 11 of them asked the authorities.
According to the Ministry of Labor, under the Labor Law, the rights of employers can be terminated only if they are dealt with in accordance with the law, and if employees do not agree with the dismissal or dismissal, they have the right to sue. In the event that the employer resigns, there is no permission to return to work, only to agree to receive compensation, and after dismissal, they have no right to replace the new person.
In the past, protesters have tried to paint a fire to provoke public outrage, accusing authorities of bias against the company, and they have spread corrupt information that the company will lay off more than 600 employees, which could lead to unrest. In addition to continuing to demonstrate illegally, the protesters also used immoral, provocative and even violent words against the authorities.
3. Insecurity breaches public order
According to the authorities, gathering people to protest against the authorities' measures and spread false information is illegal and has been affecting security and public order, as well as violating health measures to prevent Epidemic of Kovid 19 disease.
Of course, any expression or claim to rights under the law cannot be arbitrary. At the same time, union leaders do not have immunity, but they are currently protesting with arrogant union rights and violating labor laws.
4: Relevant ministries and institutions maintain their position to continue to settle peacefully with the protesters
The Ministry of Labor confirmed that in the past, the Ministry has tried to resolve this dispute in accordance with legal procedures from the beginning until now, having already reconciled nine times. The Ministry resumed the mediation process by inviting employees and employers to the meeting, but was rejected by the employees. The ministry also called on union leaders and former employees to stop protesting and return to a joint dispute resolution by sending the matter to court.
In fact, the Ministry and the competent authorities have tried to resolve this dispute in accordance with the procedures based on the highest level of patience and understanding. Unfortunately, recent progress in the talks has not been accepted by the protesters due to incitement by their union leaders.
From a former RFA reporter, a senior official at the Ministry of Environment: Cambodia needs more funds to manage protected areas sustainably
(Phnom Penh): To date, the Royal Government of Cambodia has increased the area of protected areas under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Environment to about 41% of the area of Cambodia, equivalent to more than 7.2 million hectares with protected communities. In all, there are about 174 communities in protected areas.
With such a large area, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Sao Sopheap said that these protected areas needed to be protected. This protection management requires more funds to make all protected areas sustainable and improve the livelihoods of the people around the area.
Regarding the need for additional funding, the Secretary of State did not specify how much was needed, saying only that there was a high demand. Among the sources of revenue, the Secretary of State also mentioned the sale of carbon credits. Currently, Cambodia has expanded its carbon credit sales, starting from Stung Treng to Prey Lang, covering four provinces.
At the same time, Mr. Sao Sopheap stated that currently the Ministry of Environment has implemented the program budget, which means that every year, the budget for the implementation of the model environment throughout the country, including the management of natural resource protection areas, so for the budget to implement the project. These are still limited. At this point, the Ministry has to mobilize various sources of funding from various development partners.
According to this senior official, the budget that the Ministry is considering to increase is through the implementation of the "Red Plus" project, which can sell carbon credits, which the Ministry of Environment strives to manage the conservation of forest cover in natural resource protection areas throughout Cambodia. To use these funds for conservation and community development.
"Currently, we have more than $ 100 million for annual management, protection and conservation, so this budget is still limited, considering this sustainable financing option to ensure the protection, management and conservation of resources in the future. This. This is an additional emphasis of Mr. Sao Sopheap.
