Minister Pan Sosak made the remarks while attending the official inauguration ceremony of Cambodia Trade Market on March 31, 2022.
Cambodia Trade Market is an online marketplace for small and medium enterprises that can sell potential Cambodian products both domestically and abroad, as well as display products in a wide and borderless market.
Minister Pan Sosak said, "Indeed, the presence of the Cambodian Trade Market of the Ministry of Commerce is to push Cambodian products into the international market and help promote Cambodian products into the domestic market." "Through the Cambodia Trade Market, we encourage foreigners and Cambodians to use Cambodian products as much as possible to earn a living for Cambodians who produce Cambodian products."
He added that in recent years, the Ministry has been working hard to promote Cambodian products by organizing various campaigns as well as exhibitions on Cambodian products, and year after year sees that Cambodian products have changed a lot in production. , Both packaging and quality.
He said that at present, more than 100 enterprises have been approved by the Ministry of Commerce and more than 100,000 items have been put up for sale on the Cambodia Trade Market. Small and medium enterprises are ready to sell their products to overseas customers, as Cambodia Trade is fully integrated with legal payment and delivery services to facilitate transactions. Abroad.
"To make it easier to pay for purchases, the Ministry of Commerce has so far partnered with four banks and plans to work with more," he said. There is also Chip Mong Bank. ”
Ms. Soeng Sopha, General Manager of Seila Popper Co., Ltd., stated that the establishment of the Cambodia Trade Market of the Ministry of Commerce will further help the market for Cambodian products more widely.
