(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, on March 31, 2022, chaired a seminar to disseminate the policy of Digital Government of Cambodia 2022-2035 through video conferencing (Zoom).
The event was attended by representatives of the United Nations in Cambodia, ministries, institutions and national and international honorary speakers from the public sector, the private sector, educational institutions, experts, NGOs and development partners.
The main purpose of this workshop is to disseminate and raise awareness of the digital government policy of Cambodia 2022-2035, focusing on:
(1): Digital Government Infrastructure Development and Cyber Security (2): Digital Government Governance and Digital Public Services (3): Digital Talent and Innovation and (4): Cooperation with Private Sector Partners Developers and the public to participate in the implementation of this policy as well.
Addressing the seminar, the Minister emphasized that the policy of Digital Government of Cambodia 2022-2035 is a strategic document and a roadmap to achieve a complete digital government revolution based on the vision "Build a digital government to improve quality. Life and confidence of the people through better public service "in line with the attention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Minister Chea Van Det said the policy was designed in line with the global trends of the digital revolution, taking into account the experiences of developing regional and global digital governments.
Minister Chea Vandeth added that since the outbreak of Kovid-19 in Cambodia, there has been an increase in the use of digital technology in the public sector, the private sector and among the general population in line with the needs of economic activities, working methods and Daily living in a new normal trajectory.
It should be noted that the policy of digital government of Cambodia was decided by the Royal Government on January 28, 2022, which sets out 10 strategies, including:
Oddar Meanchey Ministry of Environment and Administration launches “Reduce the use of plastic bags and promote environmentally friendly basket” campaign to raise environmental awareness
(Oddar Meanchey): The General Department of Environmental Knowledge and Information, Ministry of Environment, this morning, April 1, 2022, in cooperation with the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration, organized a campaign "Reduce the use of plastic bags and promote the environment".
The campaign was attended by representatives of Samrong City Hall, Provincial Environment Department, surrounding provincial units, the three armed forces, youth and some people in Samrong City, Oddar Meanchey Province.
According to Mr. Di Rado, Deputy Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, he supported the campaign to reduce the use of plastic bags and promote environmental basket, which was held today as a way to raise awareness among the people in Oddar Meanchey to participate in environmental sanitation. Especially the pollution caused by plastic bags.
The Undersecretary of State expressed the hope that the current campaign will encourage all people to be aware and awake and turn it into practical and regular implementation for the environmental cause in Cambodia and the global environment to be sustainable.
Please note that the garbage in the town generates more than 10,000 tons per day. Each year, Cambodia produces about 5 million tons of waste, of which 20% is plastic waste.
Globally, the total amount of plastics reached more than 8 billion tons, but only about 9% of the plastic was recycled and 91% was dumped in landfills. The water of rivers, lakes and rivers flows into the sea. Each year, more than 400 million tons of plastic are produced.
The amount of plastic will increase from 8.3 billion tons in 2015 to 12 billion tons in 2050 if the current trends in consumption and management habits of plastic waste continue like this.
The biggest problem with plastics is that they can take thousands of years to decompose. The plastic does not dissolve, it just breaks down into smaller pieces of plastic. The plastic scraps pose a risk by releasing toxic chemicals during disintegration and pollute the environment, kill animals and endanger human health.
UNHCR issues statement that UN Human Rights Committee conducts a biased assessment of the state of freedom of expression and press freedom in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Union of Federation of Cambodian Journalists (UCJJ) issued a statement on April 1, 2022 stating that the UN Human Rights Committee has conducted a biased assessment of the status of the right to freedom of expression. Opinion and Freedom of the Press in Cambodia
The Union of Federation of Cambodian Journalists (UCJC) has claimed that it has thoroughly reviewed the summary report posted on social media and the full report of the UN Human Rights Committee in Cambodia. On March 30, 2022, this report was also re-broadcast by the UN Special Rapporteur on the situation of human rights in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The Australian Government plans to provide a new grant financing cooperation under the Cambodia-Australia Partnership for Sustainable Economic Development worth A $ 144 million, or more than US $ 107 million. For a period of 8 years from 2022 to 2030.
This was stated in the courtesy meeting between Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Pablo Kang, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia, to discuss bilateral relations between the two countries and New Development Cooperation of Cambodia-Australia Partnership Program for Sustainable Economic Development, March 31, 2022.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth expressed his deep gratitude to the Royal Government of Australia for its active contribution to the funding of the Kovid-19 vaccination program and the provision of vaccines and medical equipment to contribute to Prevent the spread of Kovid-19 in Cambodia.
He stressed that Australia has always supported Cambodia in socio-economic development through the provision of technical and financial assistance in many key areas, especially agriculture, infrastructure, education, energy, etc.
Australian Ambassador Pablo Kang highlighted the close and long-standing cooperation between the Royal Government of Australia and the Royal Government of Cambodia, and this year marks the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries. Australia will continue to strengthen and expand its cooperation and continue to provide its support to Cambodia.
1: Assist Cambodia in the development of high-value agriculture and start in the field of agricultural processing;
2. Cooperate with the Royal Government of Cambodia on trade and investment policy and enterprise development to assist Cambodia in expanding its market and supporting Cambodian businesses to raise its quality standards to be able to import into other markets.
3: Continue to invest to expand the quality of infrastructure in Cambodia, especially in the field of water, energy and logistics.
This new program was initiated and carefully considered in accordance with the Rectangular Strategy - Phase 4 and the National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023 and was implemented after the successful implementation of the first phase of the Cambodian Agricultural Value Chain Program and Second (CAVAC I & II) and investment programs in infrastructure.
On that occasion, Mr. Pablo Kang also expressed his appreciation for the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has achieved many fruitful achievements, especially the best measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid disease. 19.
He also stressed that he will continue to work to strengthen and expand cooperation in all priority areas of the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially will continue to promote the development of agriculture, agro-industry and irrigation management system to grow further.
