China to launch policy to stabilize economy as soon as possible
BEIJING: China will put in place policies to maintain economic stability as soon as possible as downward pressure on the economy escalates. According to Reuters.
The world's second-largest economy is facing the worst recurrence of the new Kovid-19 case since early 2020 with large-scale testing and curbing the spread. Outbreaks appear to be exacerbated in many cities.
Shanghai, home to 26 million people and China's financial hub, has been closed for three days as new Kovid-19 cases in the city have risen by a third. Strict measures are already in place to try to stop the spread of the virus.
China will not take unfavorable measures to stabilize market expectations, and it will increase the issuance of the remaining special government bonds.
The Chinese government has set quotas this year for local government special bond issuance of 3.65 trillion yuan ($ 574.3 billion) and 1.46 trillion yuan in bonds have already been issued.
According to the same Chinese cabinet meeting, the issuance of special government bonds will be given first to areas with high debt repayment capacity and large number of projects. According to Reuters, 37 new CPP members have been announced in Mlou Prey 1 commune, Cheb district, Preah Vihear province.
