National Bank of Cambodia: Riel transactions in the "Bakong" payment system of 2.5 trillion riels and 3 billion US dollars in 2021
The ease of access to payment services through the Bakong system has increased the number of people using payment services to about 8 million, equivalent to about 80% of the total adult population.
The Bakong payment system developed by the National Bank of Cambodia is becoming a proud new achievement for Cambodia as it is gaining traction and awarding a series of awards from world-class economic and financial institutions.
Bakong System is the world's first central bank payment system that uses blockchain technology, which allows users to make payments in general transactions and transfer money through banking and financial institutions through mobile banking applications. Immediately effective, safe and affordable.
Chea Serey, who initiated and led the development of the Bagong system, has also been included in CoinDesk's list of the 50 most creative individuals in the world by 2021.
These achievements come from the efforts of all the leaders and staff of the National Bank of Cambodia, and especially the benefits of peace and political stability in Cambodia under the long-term leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei. Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who made the economy grow rapidly.
It should be noted that in the past, the National Bank of Cambodia has considered the efficiency and resilience of Cambodia's payment system in line with regional trends by establishing bilateral relations with countries in the region using the national currency to reduce the use of the system. International payment.
The National Bank of Cambodia will continue to strengthen national monetary and bilateral payments with countries in the region to enhance the ownership, independence and resilience of the Cambodian payment system, as well as reduce over-reliance on international payment systems.
Meanwhile, the National Bank of Cambodia plans to cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions, especially the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, to use the Bakong system to facilitate the transfer of government subsidies to help vulnerable people. Well.
Please be informed that during the summit meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Prime Minister of Japan Kishida Famio on March 20, 2022, the two Prime Ministers acknowledged that the development of the payment system of the National Bank of Cambodia "Bakong" Supported by Japanese companies, it is a leading regional and global innovation effort and recognizes the importance of supporting this effort.
"We will start new cooperation in the fields of energy, security, digital economy and cyber," said Japanese Prime Minister Kishida Famio. Let me give you an example, the National Bank of Cambodia's Bakong digital payment system was developed in collaboration with a Japanese enterprise. "Japan will continue to support promising projects in the future, such as the Bakong project."
