(Phnom Penh): The meeting of the Council of Ministers chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Friday morning, April 1, 2022, fully approved the "Draft Law on the Amendment of Article 140 of the Law on Capital, Provincial and Municipal Administration. Khan district. Amendments to Article 140 pave the way for increasing the composition of the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Governments.
Separately, the new Article 140, which was amended and approved by the Council of Ministers this morning, determines the composition of the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan as follows:
The Law on the Administration of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts, Khans is a modern administrative system in the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts, Khans in accordance with the policy of decentralization and deconcentration in the sub-national administration, focusing on the promotion of governance and local development, with Citizen participation is fundamental to the process of local democracy and sustainable economic development, environment and social equity.
The Organizational Law also provides for a system of governance of sub-national administrations, with two main bodies, the first of which is the council, which is formed by elections to represent the voice and interests of the people in the territory. The competence of each sub-national administration and the second person is the board of governors appointed by the national level to work with the council of sub-national administration to manage the day-to-day work.
