MOSCOW (Reuters) - Putin on Thursday signed a decree on a new procedure for payment for Russian gas purchases with non-aligned countries in the Russian ruble from April 1. This is according to the release by RT on Thursday, March 31, 2022.
The new law stipulates that non-aligned countries must open accounts in Russian banks to purchase gas from Moscow, effective April 1, 2022.
The current gas supply contract will be terminated if the buyer from a non-friendly country does not meet the new payment terms.
