Mr. Prak Sokhon exchanged views and discussed with Dr. Noeleen Heyzer on the close cooperation between ASEAN and the United Nations as well as between the two Special Envoys at a working meeting held at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs on the 31st. March 2021. This is the second meeting after the first meeting on December 13, 2021.
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon informed Dr. Heyzer about the three steps of his next work as Special Envoy as follows:
* The second step: is about the project to organize a video meeting between Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen and Senior General Min Ong Lang.
Step 3: About his second visit to Myanmar.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and Dr. Heyzer had a lengthy discussion on the organization of humanitarian assistance consultations and the establishment of humanitarian corridors to ensure a smooth and safe delivery process. In this regard, the UN Special Envoy assured the Deputy Prime Minister of the full support and participation of the United Nations.
The two special envoys also discussed the role of some countries in the region and the international community as a whole in finding a solution to the Myanmar crisis. As for ASEAN-UN cooperation, the two envoys agreed to work together to help Myanmar get out of this crisis through the ASEAN Five-Point Agreement.
The Deputy Prime Minister and the UN envoy also discussed the complementary forms of cooperation to be implemented by ASEAN and the UN and by the two special envoys in a step-by-step process, starting with From the distribution of humanitarian aid to.]
Dr. Heyzer acknowledged the difficulties facing Cambodia as the current chair of ASEAN and commended the efforts of Prime Minister Hun Sen and Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon to pave the way for a solution to the Myanmar crisis. .
Minister Mam Bun Heng Closes the 25th National TB Control Conference
(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on the afternoon of March 31, 2022, closed the 25th National TB Control Conference at the Phnom Penh Hotel. The Closing Ceremony was attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State
And representatives of some relevant ministries and institutions.
On that occasion, Prof. Mam Bunheng said that the conference process in the past two days was successful, which reflects the joint efforts between health institutions and operators at all levels. As well as national and international organizations. Due to good communication and cooperation, therefore, the work of TB control in the past has been proudly successful.
According to the report, in 2021, the National Tuberculosis Control Program has achieved more important new achievements, especially maintaining a successful treatment rate of more than 90% and diagnosed a total of 21,627 TB cases. Maintaining TB coverage in all referral hospitals, health centers across the country, as well as community outreach services in 1,147 health centers in 89 districts.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Mam Bunheng gave some recommendations as follows:
1: In 2022, more efforts must be made to research at least 32,562 TB patients of all types and please continue to maintain a successful treatment rate of more than 90%.
2: Promote the provision of research services and treatment of high-risk TB
3: To prepare, strengthen and expand to better fight against drug-resistant TB in collaboration with stakeholders, especially to encourage patients to use TB drugs properly and completely.
4: To maintain the fight against tuberculosis activities in hospitals, health centers and to further expand the Dots community, which is the care and treatment activity closest to the patient's home.
5: Continue to promote the participation of other health institutions, such as the General Department of Prisons, the Department of Health of the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of National Defense, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, private health care services, including NGOs and the Cambodian Association in Combating Diseases. .
6. Further strengthen cooperation with partners at all levels and further mobilize resources to achieve program goals for 2022 and beyond, including existing donors and efforts to mobilize resources from donors. More recently.
In a report on Thursday, the Vietnamese Ministry of Health also announced 39 new cases of Kovid 19 disease.
The book "Samdech Chuon Nath" is expected to help scholars of literature and national history
(Phnom Penh): The Hat Book Research and Publishing House has published a work entitled "Samdech Chuon Nath" which is a series of biographical books and stories related to the field of national literature and Buddhism.
