Gabon is the fourth largest buyer of rice from Cambodia.
Gabon, a country in Central Africa, is the fourth largest exporter of rice in Cambodia, while in the first two months of 2022, Cambodia exported fragrant rice to Gabon has 2,592 tons, valued at more than 2.4 million US dollars. This is according to the release of the Cambodian Rice Federation on March 31, 2022.
According to the Cambodian Rice Federation, in the last five years, Cambodia has exported 188,198 tonnes of rice to Gabon, ranking fourth among the 90 international markets that Cambodia has exported. That is, after Malaysia came in third with 204,656 tonnes, France came in second with 396,486 tonnes and China came in first with 1,164,152 tonnes, excluding rice sales. To Hong Kong and Macau.
Please be informed that in the first two months of 2022, Cambodia exported 103,058 tons of rice and 641,101 tons of rice worth more than 214.56 million dollars. Zelensky: Other countries could emulate aggression if Russia is not punished
