(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, on March 31, 2022, reminded and advised all private security agencies that have received training from the Department of Private Security Management to take knowledge. That is to be used in a targeted and positive way for the benefit of society.
During the closing ceremony of the 34th Private Security Agency Training Course of the Department of Private Security Management, Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi emphasized that when the knowledge is to be shared to colleagues who have not received special training to use. In carrying out daily work to participate in maintaining security, order and social security.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi said, "Please take the knowledge we gained from this class to apply to contribute to the promotion of our colleagues who have not passed this course. "This is very important because it does not mean just study and do not use, what is important is the practice in the workplace."
The Deputy Chief of the National Police expressed his confidence that the private security agents who attended the refresher course would gain the knowledge that the trainers had been trying to share over the past two days. He said that this additional knowledge, combined with the experience that private security agencies are completing every day, will further strengthen the capacity.
According to the report of Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department, the 34th Private Security Agency Training Course lasted for 2 days with 153 Private Security Agency trainees (2 females) from the company. Provide private security services to 34 companies, 44 private security agencies (0 females) and from 16 enterprises, 109 private security agencies (1 female).
