Russia deploys 134,500 more troops but says they will not send them to Ukraine
LONDON: Russian President Vladimir Putin on Thursday signed a decree ordering the transfer of 134,500 new troops to the army as part of Russia's annual spring draft, but the Defense Ministry said. He said the call had nothing to do with the war in Ukraine. This is according to the release by Reuters on Thursday, March 31, 2022.
Sending soldiers to fight in war is a very sensitive issue. On March 9, Russia's Defense Ministry acknowledged the deployment of some troops to Ukraine after Putin denied the allegations on various occasions, saying only troops and professional officers had been sent. .
Putin's decree states that the annual spring troop deployment, which runs from April 1 to July 15, will affect Russian men aged 18 to 27.
