The following is the NEC statement: Analysis: "The 11 former NagaWorld staff members who were released on bail did not fulfill their promises with the intention of causing a bigger and more complicated incident."
(Phnom Penh): Labor disputes between former employees of NagaWorld and NagaWorld have not been resolved since May 2021 until now, despite attempts by the authorities at all levels. The long-running labor dispute has escalated day by day, leading to the arrest of 11 protest leaders from late December 2021 on charges of inciting social security unrest.
Demonstrators, who call themselves strikers, have already crossed the red line into violation of the law, which has led to arrests. Illegal activities include:
First, this protest is not a strike, because in the sense of the strike law, it is the protest of a group of employees who agreed to protest in the enterprise or company where they are working, but in fact, the protest of the former NagaWorld employees is in accordance with Public places without permission from the authorities.
Second, the wrong demonstrations evolved to the point of using insulting rhetoric against the authorities, inciting the demonstrators to become even angrier.
Third, the demonstration was planned in advance against the authorities, including pushing pregnant women and children to the front line against the authorities.
Fourth, planning to block access to private buildings, disrupt business, prevent other employees from working, especially the project to disturb people who are celebrating the Global New Year in December 2021.
Fifth: Violation of health rules by not cooperating with the sample of Kovid 19
As of March 12 and 15, 2021, a number of former NagaWorld employees in detention have written to the Minister of Labor, promising and calling for:
Employees and workers who are on strike have not yet returned to work, please return to work together to protect the interests in the workplace and create an environment for resolving legal disputes.
For employees who have been fired by NagaWorld, please stay calm to create an atmosphere for us to negotiate with NagaWorld and the Ministry of Labor to find a solution and legal compensation for you.
Following the written promise and thumbprint above, on March 16, 2022, some former NagaWorld employees who were detained were released on bail so that they could fulfill their promise to end the labor dispute. Chronic between NagaWorld and all the former employees who protested.
As a result, contrary to the authorities' intentions in resolving the labor dispute, the released union leaders did not appear at the invitation of the authorities. That even gathered to protest, despite the ban on demonstrations by the Phnom Penh administration.
In such a labor dispute, simply put, if the employer is not satisfied with any employee, the employer has the right to terminate without prior notice by simply paying the various benefits prescribed by law plus salary. Employees fired by their employer have no right to return the terms to their employer. Similarly, in the case of a NagaWorld labor dispute, unions or employees do not have the right or immunity to set conditions with the employer.
By: Yang Vises, NGO Officer
