Cambodia and the United Nations are committed to exploring all possible ways to safeguard Myanmar's interests.
This is according to the official Facebook post of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia and Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair in charge of Myanmar affairs after meeting with Dr. Nolin Heiser, Special Envoy of the UN Secretary-General in charge. Myanmar affairs on the morning of March 31, 2022.
Prak Sokhon briefly outlined the outcome of the meeting: "We both agree that the Myanmar issue continues to be complex, which requires the proactive spirit of the Myanmar side to accelerate the implementation of the five-point ASEAN consensus. "As special envoy, we are committed to exploring every possible way to achieve our mission and goals, which, of course, are for the benefit of Myanmar as a whole."
Please be informed that Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon paid his first working visit to Myanmar on March 21-23, 2022. The mission was accompanied by Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and Mr. Lim Jock Hoi, Secretary-General of ASEAN.
