18 Workers Injured in Car Crash in Kampong Ror District, Svay Rieng Province
(Svay Rieng): At least 18 factory workers were seriously and lightly injured in a car accident at 7:20 pm on March 30, 2022 in Trapeang Kampis village, Khseth commune, Kampong Rot district, province. Svay Rieng.
He said that when he arrived at the scene, a truck carrying factory workers overtook another car in an accident, causing the car to overturn on the south side of the road, causing a total of 18 minor injuries. One was seriously injured and two were female. The police called an ambulance to transport the injured to Svay Teap District Hospital for treatment.
The district inspector confirmed that the driver of the car, Moek Ratana, male, 24 years old, resided in Banteay Kraing village, Banteay Kraing commune, Kampong Rou district, Svay Rieng province. Missing from the scene.
Currently, the car exhibits are kept at the line administrative police station to wait for the car owner to come and deal with it. Two seriously injured people are still being treated at Svay Teap District Referral Hospital and all those with minor injuries have returned home. Skilled workforce will help attract investment and create a better business environment in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Meng Nimol, Deputy Director General of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, said that the training of Cambodian workers to have quality and clear skills is to contribute to attracting foreign investors to invest in Cambodia and create a favorable environment for work. Business and Investment in Cambodia.
Mr. Meng Nimol made this remark during a workshop on the funding of the Skills Development Fund project for skills training to factories organized by the Skills Development Fund (SDF) and the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce on March 31. 2022 at the Cambodiana Hotel to raise awareness of the budget to support skills training.
He added that human resource development is a priority of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to support and strengthen the capacity of local businesses. So far, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce has cooperated with foreign and local partners to provide training from 2020 to early 2022 on business management and technical skills to more than 2,000 participants, which is a contribution to the Royal Government in Develop human resources, especially the strengthening of local business resources.
"Our country has a rich young workforce that requires training to adapt to the circumstances of the national economy," he said. This work requires the participation of all stakeholders, both public and private, especially companies that meet directly and know the needs of human resources.
There are five priority sectors that can receive funding for this skill training: manufacturing, construction, electronics, tourism and telecommunications, and information technology. In addition, other sectors with high demand and high value-added can also apply.
General Professor Chea Dara: Samdech Techo left the work of national defense for the national cause to this day, so we must continue to preserve this heritage.
(Phnom Penh): General Professor Chea Dara, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia in Charge of Rector of the National Defense University, Representative of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, presided over the closing ceremony of the training course. 2020-2021 and open the course 2022, which is an important part of training human resources in the field of defense at the National Defense University.
He praised the efforts to promote training and effective training, participate in peacekeeping, strengthen defense, sovereignty, territorial integrity, security, social order and national development. In the context of the fight against Kovid 19, the National Defense University conducted the training according to the plan by going through and gaining the experience of education in Kovid 19.
Although the picture is a different event, the learning process is flexible to the situation of Kovid 19, that is, when it is easy to concentrate, learn to take turns when the epidemic is severe or when the distance learning system is closed. Online. According to the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, we must learn to live and fulfill our duties according to the transitional path of the 19th Kovid era.
In addition, General Professor Chea Dara advised the military, students and trainees, including:
* First, to strictly and effectively implement the 10 recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, stated at the celebration of the 20th anniversary of the establishment of the Army on the 24th. January 2019 ago.
* Third: To increase the will to respect, protect, support and be absolutely loyal to Commander Hun Manet, the future Prime Minister. For the army, the next generation must remember three points: first: to preserve the legacy left by the previous generation, second: to participate in building other achievements, and third: to build a nursery for the next generation.
"A strong nation is based on a strong defense sector and a strong defense sector is due to a strong army. "The previous generation of officers left a legacy of national defense for our national cause today, so we must continue to preserve this legacy on the basis of spirit, will, experience and combined with practical ability."
* Fourth: Military officers must continue to update teaching materials in accordance with the current evolving situation. Continue to lead the writing of dissertations or dissertations in a transparent and effective manner. Internal unity must be maintained and the various policies of the Royal Government, the Ministry of National Defense must be handed over to the mouth through regular open economic declarations.
* Fifth: Students and trainees must listen to the advice of military officers and respect the internal rules and regulations of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces must be willing to compete for knowledge.
* Sixth: For students and trainees who complete all courses must use this knowledge in their unit better.
