Three people were chased by a male stingray, causing serious and minor injuries in Oddar Meanchey province
(Oddar Meanchey): At least three men and women were seriously and lightly injured and their families were taken to the provincial hospital after being chased by a wild animal on March 30. 2022 is located in Seth Serey Chas village, Kork Mon commune, Banteay Ampil district, Oddar Meanchey province.
According to the villagers, before the incident, the three victims, farmers, went to his potato farm and sometimes they saw an animal thought to be an animal. The buffaloes knew that they were wild animals, so they chased them out of the field. While chasing the animals, they ran back to them, chasing them, causing them to be seriously injured and taken to the hospital by their families. Referral to Oddar Meanchey Province.
As for the stingray, Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, instructed the Banteay Ampil District Authority together with the conservation force of the Provincial Department of Environment, the Banteay Ampil Military Force and the District Police Inspectorate to watch and wait for the zoo conservation force to catch it. CP Cambodia Donates $ 50,000 to the 159th Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2022
