(Phnom Penh): Ms. Nhep Sopheap, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Council of Cambodia for Children, stated that online sexual exploitation of children is a global problem that occurs in various forms and has become a new concern. Another is that stakeholders, including the public, guardians of children, authorities and civil society, need to work together to prevent and protect children from abuse.
Ms. Nhep Sopheap said this morning, March 31, 2022, on the occasion of the opening of the training course on the protection of children from online sexual exploitation of children, which was held at the Phnom Penh Hotel with the participation of Ms. Sar Kimly, Under Secretary of State for the Ministry of Information and a member of the Cambodian National Council for Children, as well as representatives of Plan International and other stakeholders.
Ms. Nhep Sopheap added that the training aims to raise awareness of crimes that occur in social networks that pose a risk to children, as well as existing regulations and mechanisms for procedural action on criminal cases and identify Common rules for promoting effective and efficient procedures.
She added that the advancement of information technology also has some negative effects associated with misuse and intrusion by criminals to take advantage of the illegal and deviate from the moral and development trajectory by creating All forms of exploitation and abuse, including online child sexual exploitation, are a new form that is spreading and posing a high risk to children around the world, including Cambodia.
"As the Kovid 19 crisis continues to spread around the world, the use of information technology and the Internet has become increasingly important and important in communicating and addressing all issues, including the education of children and youth in the city," she said. Even in rural areas, criminals are more likely to engage in online child abuse.
The tricks and acts of sexual assault of the perpetrators are becoming more and more complex and worsening, requiring all parties involved to work together to address them. For child victims of sexual exploitation have left serious physical and psychological consequences, and most child victims find it difficult to trust others, despair, loneliness, confusion, frustration, self-blame and fear.
