UPDIS has prepared "Draft Results Report for the First Phase of Master Plan for the Development of Sihanoukville into a Multi-Purpose Special Economic Zone", focusing on two main areas: 1. Regional and Statistical Analysis; 2. Preliminary concept that shows the future picture of master planning. Overall, the draft report is a preliminary concept of the Sihanoukville Development Master Plan at the macro level, with a strategic character and policy direction.
The master plan is part of the Royal Government of Cambodia's medium- and long-term strategic considerations to turn Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose model economic zone and an important economic pole for national development. To grow sustainably and environmentally in accordance with the provisions of the Cambodia Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025.
The master plan is meticulously thought out, providing a highly innovative modern infrastructure that can be considered a smart city (SMART CITY), including the construction of buildings, residential areas, industrial zones, protected areas. Etc. Highly creative, aesthetically pleasing and comfortable to live in.
The meeting reviewed, discussed and decided on the main contents of the draft report, as well as made special recommendations focusing on development directions, potential economic-industrial sectors, master plans and institutional frameworks, etc. to help orient The UPDIS team revised the first phase of the draft report as a compass to serve as a basis for further study and preparation.
