New Pakistani Ambassador Asks Cambodian National Assembly President to Boost Parliamentary Cooperation
The National Assembly of Cambodia and Pakistan have a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) and the Vice President of the National Assembly of Pakistan visited Cambodia last year.
The National Assembly of Cambodia and Pakistan supported each other in the parliamentary forum on the international stage and pledged to work hard to further strengthen cooperation, especially the exchange of visits and experiences at all levels.
Samdech Heng Samrin stated that the National Assembly of Cambodia and Pakistan have maintained good relations and cooperation with each other, especially in the field of parliamentary diplomacy, by supporting each other in regional and global inter-parliamentary forums. The National Assembly of Cambodia has previously supported the Pakistani Parliament as the Vice President of the IPU and the IPA Intelligence Assembly.
The National Assembly President stated that by the end of 2022, the Cambodian Parliament will host the 43rd AIPA General Assembly and hoped that the Pakistani Parliament will be present at the AIPA General Assembly.
Mr. Zahiruddin Baba Thahim will deliver a speech by the President of the National Assembly to the leaders of the National Assembly of Pakistan and expressed confidence that the National Assembly of Pakistan will be present at the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) hosted by the Cambodian Parliament.
The Ambassador also briefed Samdech on the outcome of a working meeting with the leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia, leaders of various ministries and institutions, which he paid a courtesy call on at the beginning of his diplomatic mission in Cambodia to strengthen diplomatic relations. The two countries, which have been around for more than 70 years, are stronger in all areas.
