Chom Chao flyover and subway are projects of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Phnom Penh Capital Administration and contracted by the Overseas Cambodian Investment Company (OCIC). The flyover and subway project was opened under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on June 29, 2018. The project takes 30 months to build and costs about $ 22 million.
Based on the technical specifications of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, this construction site is divided into 3 parts, including:
* Bridge 1: It is the main flyover connecting traffic from Russian Boulevard to National Road No. 3, with a total length of 408 meters and a width of 15.8 meters, with two lanes to two lanes to a bridge slope of 4.5 meters and a maximum height. The traffic under the bridge is 5.5 meters.
* Second Bridge: Separate from the main flyover, turn left and connect the traffic from Russian Blvd. to Veng Sreng Road for one-way traffic with one lane for cars and one lane for motorcycles with a total length of 202 meters (40 meters of flyover, lower road The land is 118 meters long and the road is 44 meters long and 5.25 meters wide.
The project also built a 470-meter-long, 8.5-meter-wide subway, which connects traffic from National Road 4 to Russian Federation Boulevard, for one-way traffic with two lanes for cars and one lane for motorcycles.
For driving on the flyover and subway, Chom Chao has set a safe speed of 40 km per hour for 8.5 meters wide and 25 km per hour for 5.25 meters wide and 5 meters. .5 meters. Chom Chao flyover and subway are up to 100 years old and are equipped with street lighting poles, network around the flyover and underground reservoir, as well as automatic pump motors.
