Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: More than 300 tons of drug ingredients are being stored after the crackdown and are looking for ways to neutralize before destroying
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, on the afternoon of March 30, 2022, claimed that the Cambodian police have cracked down on more than 300 tons of drugs. All relevant experts are working together to find a way to neutralize all the ingredients before destroying them.
During the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the results of drug control work in 2021 and work direction in 2022 of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, Prince Sar Kheng said, "We have cracked down on more than 300 tons that we have seized to "Find a technician and find a substance that can neutralize all these chemicals before destroying them."
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that all the ingredients were imported into Cambodia both legally and illegally. Samdech explained that legal import means having a valid import license, but professional institutions do not follow up carefully when using it for the intended purpose. At this point, the prince has stated that most of those ingredients are licensed as raw materials for agricultural fertilizers.
Separately, illegal imports, Prince Kralahom Sar Kheng suspected that can be fraudulent with legal goods that the Czech authorities have not reached the level or can be imported through other corridors and so on. But the prince thinks that if the case of importing through the corridor is not more than tens of kilos, then only cheat with legal goods.
The drug problem has become a further concern of the Royal Government of Cambodia, at which point Sar Kheng once again reminded the competent authorities and all relevant ministries and institutions to pay attention and strengthen management. In particular, inspect imported goods for fear of fraudulent use of ingredients for drug production.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that currently more than 50% of the inmates in prisons are involved in drug offenses. All capitals-provinces. In this regard, Samdech Krala Hom claimed that the fight against drugs is not the exclusive responsibility of the competent authorities, that is, the people themselves must participate in this work together.
According to Samdech Sar Kheng, educating about the effects and disadvantages of drugs is also a priority. He said that if people are aware of the effects of drugs, then this is an important weapon in the fight against drug crimes, so it must be more active in promoting this education.
On that occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng reminded and issued strict orders to all civil servants, especially the police, not to be involved in this drug crime, by strictly implementing the "three do not" is not involved, do not Intervene and do not forgive. And citizens must participate in providing information to the authorities about trafficking, distribution, use, processing, production and storage of drugs.
