Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is currently building infrastructure in a country that is conducive to peace, while war-torn Ukraine is destroying infrastructure. Samdech reminded that 52 years ago, the infrastructure in Cambodia, including many bridges, were cut off.
"When there was a war, we saw the value of peace, and in Cambodia we saw the value of peace since March 1970, more than 50 years ago, but then we had no choice," Hun Sen said. He added that peace is the only way to develop, without peace, not to mention the development of democracy and human rights.
Samdech stated that peace in Cambodia is hard to find, and this peace enables Cambodia for two consecutive decades to grow at around 7% every year, even though the Cambodian population has tripled.
Samdech urges to look at Ukraine now, which has been fleeing and fleeing and suffering severe discrimination in Europe. "Now in the world, the first is shouting for peace and the second is defending peace," he said. "Everyone is worried about World War III and the war in Ukraine," he said, adding that "now someone is talking about democracy and human rights in Ukraine, now they are talking about peace in Ukraine."
Samdech has confirmed his political message in the past, which confirms the protection of peace at all costs. Peace must come first of all. "Whether this year or next year, Samdech is still talking about peace," he said.
It has been more than a month since Ukraine was attacked by Russian troops. Infrastructure in cities was devastated as more than 4 million people fled the war.
White House: Putin was lied to by his advisers about the real situation in the Ukraine war (Video inside) (Washington): Russian President Vladimir Putin received false information from his advisers regarding Russian military activities in Ukraine and The impact of Western sanctions on Russia's economy. This is according to the White House quoted by Reuters on Thursday, March 31, 2022.
According to US intelligence, Putin was unaware of Russia's military action and the effectiveness of his orders in Ukraine. But the Kremlin did not comment on the White House statement.
