(Phnom Penh): According to the report of the General Commission of the National Police, on March 30, 2022, there were five traffic accidents across the country, resulting in one death and six minor injuries.
OPEC + oil producers likely to keep oil output in line with existing agreement
LONDON (Reuters) - OPEC + countries, including Russia, are likely to stick to their existing agreement to gradually increase oil production, some sources said on Wednesday. According to Reuters.
The sources, speaking to Reuters on condition of anonymity, attended a joint technical committee meeting to advise OPEC + on market fundamentals. A full ministerial meeting will take place this Thursday.
Sources familiar with the talks told Reuters that OPEC + was likely to stick to a modest increase in oil production for May, despite rising prices due to the crisis in Ukraine and calls for a ceasefire. From the United States and other countries to increase oil supplies.
Private Security Management Department Conducts a Meeting to Strengthen Private Security Management in Preah Sihanouk Province
(Preah Sihanouk): Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department, on the afternoon of March 30, 2022, led a working group to open a meeting to strengthen private security management in enterprises and establishments in Sihanoukville.
The meeting was also attended by Lt. Gen. Seang Sen, Director of the Anti-Criminal Gambling Department and the working group of the Sihanoukville Provincial Police, as well as representatives of establishments in Sihanoukville.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey introduced the work of private security management and law, and set some goals as follows:
* Request for cooperation between institutions with the working group to update and have sufficient relevant documents * Request institutions to send private security to participate in the training course on 7-8 April 2022 (especially security chief) * Uniforms And use the right tools. Senior Minister Kun Kim inspects homes of veterans affected by strong winds
